window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0172", [{"word":"reciprocal","ipa_uk":"/rɪˈsɪprəkl/","ipa_us":"/rɪˈsɪprəkəl/","definition_zh":"相互的；对等的；有来有往的；倒数（数学）；相互代词（语法）","definition_en":"given or done by each of two sides to the other, so that what is received balances what is offered","core_image":"两个人隔着桌子互相递东西，你递过去一份，对方立刻回递同样一份，两只手在同一高度上往返","scene":"两家实验室签下协议，一方开放样本库，另一方回赠测序数据，双方义务一一对应。The two laboratories signed a reciprocal agreement to share samples and sequencing data.","sceneCN":"两家实验室签订对等协议：一方开放样本库，另一方回赠测序数据，双方义务彼此对应；句中的 reciprocal 指「双方对等互换的」（第 1 个义项：一方给出，另一方以同等之物回报）。图中可辨识物件：两份协议书、来回传递的样本盒、对开的签名页。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"相互的；对等的；互惠的；方向相反的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"倒数（数学）；相互代词（语法）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"reciprocal agreement","zh":"对等协议"},{"phrase":"reciprocal relationship","zh":"互惠关系"},{"phrase":"reciprocal exchange","zh":"对等交换"},{"phrase":"reciprocal obligation","zh":"相互义务"},{"phrase":"reciprocal trade","zh":"互惠贸易"},{"phrase":"reciprocal pronoun","zh":"相互代词"},{"phrase":"reciprocal altruism","zh":"互惠利他"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more reciprocal"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most reciprocal"},{"label":"副词","form":"reciprocally"},{"label":"复数（名词义）","form":"reciprocals"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"reciprocate","pos":"v.","zh":"回报；报答；往复运动（加表示动作的动词后缀，使「往复」成为可执行的动作）"},{"word":"reciprocation","pos":"n.","zh":"报答；互相给予；机械往复（加表示过程的名词后缀，把动作变为过程本身）"},{"word":"reciprocity","pos":"n.","zh":"互惠；互惠性（加表示性质的抽象名词后缀，把「对等」抽成一种性质）"},{"word":"reciprocally","pos":"adv.","zh":"相互地；对等地（加副词后缀，让对等关系修饰动作方式）"},{"word":"reciprocating","pos":"adj.","zh":"往复式的（现在分词作形容词，指机械沿直线来回）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Giving back what is given","titleCN":"有来有往的对等回报","definition":"given by each side to the other so that what one receives balances what one offers","definitionCN":"一方给出之后，另一方以分量相当之物回赠，使往来两端互相抵消","example":"The two universities run a reciprocal exchange of students every spring.","exampleCN":"两所大学每年春天互派学生，往来对等。","why":"Latin reciprocus described motion that turns back the way it came, so the oldest sense is a giving that returns to the giver rather than stopping at the receiver.","whyCN":"拉丁 reciprocus 描述的是掉头沿原路返回的运动，因此最早的意思是一种回到给出者手里的给予，而不是停在收受者那里。"},{"no":"02","title":"Matching in opposite direction","titleCN":"方向相反、彼此对应","definition":"placed or directed the opposite way so that the two sides correspond exactly","definitionCN":"朝相反方向放置或指向，使两侧恰好一一对应","example":"A reciprocal course steers the vessel back along the line it has just followed.","exampleCN":"反向航向把船引回它刚刚走过的那条航线。","why":"the idea of turning back is visible here as geometry: two lines run in opposite directions yet answer to each other exactly.","whyCN":"「掉头返回」在这里表现为几何关系：两条线方向相反，却彼此严丝合缝地对应。"},{"no":"03","title":"The number that gives one","titleCN":"数学中的倒数","definition":"the number by which a given number must be multiplied to produce one","definitionCN":"一个数与它相乘恰好得到一时，后者就是前者的倒数","example":"The reciprocal of four is one quarter.","exampleCN":"四的倒数是四分之一。","why":"a reciprocal value undoes a multiplication, so the term carries the old image of a step that exactly reverses another step.","whyCN":"倒数值能把一次乘法抵消回去，因此这个术语沿用了「一步恰好反转另一步」的旧意象。"},{"no":"04","title":"The pronoun of mutual action","titleCN":"语法中的相互代词","definition":"a pronoun such as each other or one another that shows an action passing both ways","definitionCN":"表示动作双向进行的代词，如「彼此」「互相」一类的词","example":"In the clause they blamed each other, the pronoun is reciprocal.","exampleCN":"在「他们互相责怪」这一小句中，该代词是相互代词。","why":"the grammar label borrows the core image directly: the action leaves one participant, reaches the other, and comes back.","whyCN":"这个语法标签直接借用了核心意象：动作从一方出发，到达另一方，又回到原处。"},{"no":"05","title":"A relation that holds both ways","titleCN":"逻辑与亲属关系中的对称关系","definition":"a relation that, whenever it holds between one item and another, also holds in the reverse order","definitionCN":"一种关系，只要甲对乙成立，颠倒过来乙对甲也成立","example":"Cousinship is a reciprocal relation, since the reverse of the link always holds too.","exampleCN":"表亲关系是一种对称关系，因为这条连线反过来也永远成立。","why":"logic took the everyday notion of a matched return and made it exact: no direction of the relation may be left without its counterpart.","whyCN":"逻辑学把日常「对等回报」的观念精确化：关系的任何一个方向都不允许缺少对应的一方。"},{"no":"06","title":"Mutual benefit among organisms","titleCN":"生物学与社会学中的互惠行为","definition":"describing behaviour in which help given now is returned later by the receiver","definitionCN":"描述这样一种行为：此刻给出的帮助，日后由受助者回还","example":"Grooming among unrelated animals is reciprocal: help given now is returned later.","exampleCN":"无亲缘关系的动物之间的理毛是对等的：此刻给出的帮助日后会被回还。","why":"field studies of animals reused the word because the pattern is literally give-and-take deferred in time, not shared possession.","whyCN":"动物行为研究借用了这个词，因为这种模式确实是延后兑现的给与取，而不是共同拥有。"},{"no":"07","title":"Back-and-forth motion","titleCN":"机械中的往复运动","definition":"describing motion that repeatedly travels one way and then the opposite way","definitionCN":"描述沿一个方向走完再反向走回、如此反复的运动","example":"The pump converts rotary drive into a reciprocal motion of the piston.","exampleCN":"这台泵把旋转驱动转成活塞的往复运动。","why":"this is the Latin image in its most physical form: the moving part never settles, because its path is a return.","whyCN":"这是拉丁意象最物理化的一面：运动部件从不停住，因为它的路径本身就是一次返回。"},{"no":"08","title":"Concessions exchanged in trade","titleCN":"外交与贸易中的互惠减让","definition":"describing tariff or market concessions that each country grants in return for those of the other","definitionCN":"指各国彼此给予、以换取对方同等让步的关税或市场减让","example":"Both governments offered reciprocal tariff reductions on agricultural machinery.","exampleCN":"两国政府就农业机械互相给予对等的关税减让。","why":"diplomacy fixed the word to signed bargains, where every clause granted by one party must be answered by a clause from the other.","whyCN":"外交文书把这个词固定用于签成的交易：一方让出的每一条，都必须由另一方以一条来回应。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Reciprocal comes from Latin reciprocus 'returning, alternating, mutual'. Its earlier pre-Latin shape is generally reconstructed as a compound of re- 'back' and pro- 'forward' with an adjectival ending, an image of movement that goes and comes. The deeper origin is uncertain, and the starred form is a reconstruction.","cn":"reciprocal 来自拉丁 reciprocus「返回的、交替的、相互的」。其更早的前拉丁形式一般重构为由表示「向后」的拉丁前缀与表示「向前」的拉丁前缀加形容词性后缀构成的复合词，意象是去了又回的往复运动；更深来源不确定，带星号的形式属于重构形式。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN RECIPROCUS","en":"Reciprocus meant 'returning, alternating, mutual'. It described things that move back the way they came, and from that 'alternating' sense it also came to mean 'shared by two sides'.","cn":"reciprocus 意为「返回的、交替的、相互的」，描述沿原路折返之物；由「交替」这一层，又引申出「双方共有」的意思。"},{"era":"RECONSTRUCTED STEM","en":"The pre-Latin form is generally reconstructed as a compound of re- 'backward' and pro- 'forward' plus an adjectival suffix; the pattern of a going and a coming is visible in the two prefixes. This starred form is a reconstruction, not a recorded word.","cn":"其前拉丁形式一般重构为由表示「向后」的成分与表示「向前」的成分加形容词性后缀构成的复合词，一去一回的格局就写在这两个前缀里；带星号的形式是重构形式，并非有记录的真实词形。"},{"era":"LATIN RECIPROCARE","en":"The verb reciprocare 'to move back and forth, to exchange' grew from the adjective, and English later took it as reciprocate.","cn":"动词 reciprocare「来回移动、交换」由该形容词长出，英语后来把它吸收为 reciprocate。"},{"era":"ENGLISH RECIPROCAL","en":"English adopted reciprocal in the sixteenth century, probably through French, first for things that correspond to each other in opposite directions.","cn":"英语在十六世纪吸收 reciprocal，可能经由法语，最初用于指方向相反却彼此对应的东西。"},{"era":"SPECIALIZED SENSES","en":"Mathematics fixed the noun sense 'inverse value' by the eighteenth century, grammar named the reciprocal pronoun in the nineteenth, and trade treaties made the adjective standard in the twentieth.","cn":"数学在十八世纪固定了「倒数值」的名词义，语法学在十九世纪命名了相互代词，贸易条约则在二十世纪使这个形容词成为标准用语。"},{"era":"SOURCE UNCERTAIN","en":"Source uncertain: the deeper origin of Latin reciprocus is not settled, and any Indo-European root proposed for it beyond the reconstructed compound is a hypothesis rather than a demonstrated derivation.","cn":"来源不确定：拉丁 reciprocus 的更早来源并无定论，在重构复合词之外为它提出的任何印欧词根都只是假说，并非已证实的派生。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms of the same Latin family that are easily mistaken for one another; group two holds words about two-way relations, where mutual and reciprocal differ in what they stress.","cn":"第一组是同一拉丁词族的各种形式，彼此极易认错；第二组都谈双向关系，其中 mutual 与 reciprocal 的侧重并不相同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"reciprocate","ipa":"/rɪˈsɪprəkeɪt/","tag":"the verb","definition":"The verb meaning to give or feel something in return, or of a machine part to move back and forth; reciprocal is the adjective built on the same stem.","definitionCN":"动词，指回赠、回应，或指机件往复运动；reciprocal 是由同一词干构成的形容词。"},{"word":"reciprocity","ipa":"/ˌresɪˈprɒsəti/","tag":"the abstract noun","definition":"Names the principle or practice of mutual giving; it is the quality, while reciprocal describes a particular arrangement.","definitionCN":"指互相给予的原则或做法，是抽象性质；reciprocal 则描述某一具体安排。"},{"word":"reciprocally","ipa":"/rɪˈsɪprəkli/","tag":"the adverb","definition":"Means 'in a mutual way' and modifies a verb; it cannot stand where the adjective is required.","definitionCN":"意为「以相互的方式」，修饰动词，不能放在需要形容词的位置。"},{"word":"reciprocation","ipa":"/ˌresɪprəˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"the process noun","definition":"The act or process of returning something, or the mechanical stroke that returns; it names an event, not a relation.","definitionCN":"指回赠的行为或过程，也指机械的回程；它命名事件，而非关系。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"mutual","ipa":"/ˈmjuːtʃuəl/","tag":"shared in common","definition":"Stresses something held or felt jointly by both sides, as mutual friends or mutual respect; it does not insist that each side return an equivalent, which reciprocal does.","definitionCN":"强调双方共同拥有或共同感到的东西，如共同的朋友、相互的尊重；它不要求各方回以等量之物，而 reciprocal 有此要求。"},{"word":"bilateral","ipa":"/baɪˈlætərəl/","tag":"two parties, formal","definition":"Said of agreements or talks involving exactly two parties; it counts the parties, while reciprocal describes the balance of what they exchange.","definitionCN":"指恰好涉及两方的协议或会谈；它数各方数目，而 reciprocal 描述交换是否对等。"},{"word":"corresponding","ipa":"/kəˈrɒspɒndɪŋ/","tag":"matching structurally","definition":"Describes two things that fit each other in form or position; it lacks the notion of return or repayment that reciprocal carries.","definitionCN":"指两物在形式或位置上彼此相配；它不含 reciprocal 那种回还与报偿的意味。"},{"word":"complementary","ipa":"/ˌkɒmplɪˈmentəri/","tag":"filling a gap","definition":"Describes parts that complete each other because they differ; reciprocal parts match by returning the same, not by supplying what is missing.","definitionCN":"指因彼此不同而互相补足的部分；reciprocal 的双方靠回以同样的东西相配，而不是靠补上缺口。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations here are the real Latin prefixes, the real word family and the real settings in which the word is used.","cn":"正常联想取自这个词真实的拉丁前缀、真实词族，以及它实际出现的场景。"},"normal":[{"en":"re- 'back' plus pro- 'forward': one step out, one step back, and the pair of steps is the meaning.","cn":"表示「向后」的成分加表示「向前」的成分：出去一步、退回一步，这一对步子就是词义。"},{"en":"The family runs reciprocal, reciprocate, reciprocation, reciprocity, reciprocally, reciprocating.","cn":"词族包括 reciprocal、reciprocate、reciprocation、reciprocity、reciprocally、reciprocating。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the settings: reciprocal agreement, reciprocal exchange, reciprocal trade, reciprocal altruism.","cn":"固定搭配标出使用场景：对等协议、对等交换、互惠贸易、互惠利他。"},{"en":"Contrast it with mutual: mutual friends are shared, reciprocal favours are returned.","cn":"与 mutual 对照：共同的朋友是共享的，对等的帮助是回还的。"},{"en":"Mathematics keeps the noun alive: the reciprocal of four is one quarter.","cn":"数学让名词义继续活着：四的倒数是四分之一。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a tennis rally in which neither player can end the point, because every shot is answered.","cn":"想象一场网球对拉，谁也结束不了这一分，因为每一拍都被回了过去。"},{"en":"Picture two mirrors facing each other, so each one contains the other without end.","cn":"想象两面相对而立的镜子，每一面里都装着另一面，无穷无尽。"},{"en":"Picture a handshake held a moment too long, each side waiting for the other to let go.","cn":"想象一次握得过久的握手，两边都在等对方先松手。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Field biologists describe reciprocal grooming as a form of deferred payment.","cn":"野外生物学家把互惠理毛描述为一种延后偿付。"},{"en":"The two cities agreed to reciprocal use of their emergency hospitals.","cn":"两座城市同意彼此对等使用对方的急救医院。"},{"en":"In any field, the reciprocal of a nonzero element is unique.","cn":"在任何域中，非零元素的倒数是唯一的。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"谐音「瑞西普若扣」：你扣我一下，我扣你一下，来回对等 → 相互的、对等的、倒数；前缀一去一回的意象可帮助记住「往复」这一核心。","word":"reciprocal"},"root":"拉丁 reciprocus「返回的、交替的、相互的」→ 前拉丁形式一般重构为 *reco-proco-（由表示「向后」的成分、表示「向前」的成分与形容词性后缀构成）→ 英语 reciprocal；更深来源不确定，带星号者为重构形式。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one line: a movement that turns back becomes a giving that is returned, then a structural opposite, an arithmetic inversion, a grammar of mutual action, a symmetric relation, deferred help among organisms, mechanical back-and-forth, and finally signed concessions between states.","cn":"八个义项沿一条线展开：折返的运动先变成回还的给予，再变成结构上的反向对应、算术上的取逆、语法上的互相动作、逻辑上的对称关系、生物间延后兑现的互助、机械的往复，最后落到国家间签成的对等减让。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a step that goes out and comes straight back, so that neither side ends up ahead of the other.","cn":"核心意象：迈出一步又原路退回，于是哪一方都不会比另一方多走一截。"},"chain":["RETURN","MATCHED GIVING","OPPOSITE CORRESPONDENCE","INVERSION","SYMMETRY","RECIPROCITY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"GIVE AND RETURN: the core movement becomes a balanced exchange, and in space it becomes two directions that answer each other.","cn":"给与回：核心的往复运动先成为均衡的交换，在空间上再成为彼此回应的两个方向。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"REVERSAL IN LANGUAGE AND NUMBER: multiplication is undone by an inverse value, and an action is undone by turning it back on both participants.","cn":"语言与数目中的反向：乘法被倒数值抵消，动作则被折回两个参与者身上。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"TWO-WAY STRUCTURE IN RELATIONS AND LIFE: a link that holds both ways, and help that returns after an interval.","cn":"关系与生命中的双向结构：一条正反皆成立的关系，一份隔一段时间又回来的帮助。"},{"senses":"07","en":"PHYSICAL STROKE: the same return, now as a piston that must come back before it can go out again.","cn":"物理冲程：同一个「回」，此时表现为活塞必须先退回才能再出去。"},{"senses":"08","en":"BARGAINED RETURN: states put the return into writing, so each concession is answered clause by clause.","cn":"写进条款的回：国家把回还固定成文字，于是每一项减让都由另一条条款来回应。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The word can be read as two opposed prefixes plus an adjectival ending: a going forward and a coming back, frozen into a quality.","cn":"这个词可以读成两个方向相反的前缀加一个形容词性结尾：一次向前与一次后退，被凝固成一种性质。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin reciprocus and the verb reciprocare supply the stem; the two prefixes are Latin re- and pro-, and the English endings -ate, -ity and -ally were added later.","cn":"拉丁 reciprocus 与动词 reciprocare 提供词干；两个前缀分别来自拉丁语的「向后」与「向前」，英语后缀表示动作、性质与方式，都是后来加上的。"},"items":[{"word":"re-","structure":"Latin prefix meaning backward","meaning":"back, in the reverse direction","meaningCN":"表示「向后、朝反方向」的前缀","example":"This prefix supplies the backward half of the image.","exampleCN":"这个前缀提供意象中「退回」的那一半。"},{"word":"pro-","structure":"Latin prefix meaning forward","meaning":"forward, in front","meaningCN":"表示「向前、在前」的前缀","example":"This prefix supplies the outward half of the image.","exampleCN":"这个前缀提供意象中「出去」的那一半。"},{"word":"-al","structure":"suffix forming adjectives from nouns","meaning":"relating to, of the kind of","meaningCN":"把名词变成形容词、表示「与……有关的」后缀","example":"The ending turns the Latin stem into an English adjective.","exampleCN":"这个结尾把拉丁词干变成英语形容词。"},{"word":"-ate","structure":"suffix forming verbs","meaning":"to make, to perform","meaningCN":"把词干变成动词、表示「做出该动作」的后缀","example":"The ending produced the verb for returning a favour.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出了表示回赠的动词。"},{"word":"-ity","structure":"suffix forming abstract nouns","meaning":"the state or quality of","meaningCN":"把形容词变成抽象名词、表示「性质或状态」的后缀","example":"The ending produced the noun for the principle of mutual giving.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出了表示互相给予这一原则的名词。"},{"word":"-ally","structure":"suffix forming adverbs from adjectives","meaning":"in the manner of","meaningCN":"把形容词变成副词、表示「以该方式」的后缀","example":"The ending produced the adverb meaning in a mutual manner.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出了表示「以相互方式」的副词。"},{"word":"reciprocus","structure":"Latin adjective, first and second declension","meaning":"returning, alternating, mutual","meaningCN":"返回的；交替的；相互的","example":"This adjective is the earliest recorded link in the chain.","exampleCN":"这个形容词是这条演变链上最早有记录的一环。"},{"word":"reciprocare","structure":"Latin verb, first conjugation","meaning":"to move back and forth, to exchange","meaningCN":"来回移动；交换","example":"The verb supplied the English verb for returning a favour.","exampleCN":"这个动词提供了英语中表示回赠的动词。"},{"word":"reciprocal","structure":"Latin stem + English adjectival ending","meaning":"given and returned in equal measure","meaningCN":"等量地给出并回还的","example":"The adjective entered English in the sixteenth century.","exampleCN":"这个形容词于十六世纪进入英语。"},{"word":"reciprocity","structure":"adjective stem + abstract noun ending","meaning":"the practice of mutual giving","meaningCN":"互相给予的做法","example":"The noun names the principle behind many treaties.","exampleCN":"这个名词指许多条约背后的原则。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"reciprocus","structure":"reciprocus, reciproca, reciprocum (adj., first and second declension)","meaning":"returning, alternating, mutual","meaningCN":"返回的；交替的；相互的"},{"word":"reciprocare","structure":"reciproco, reciprocare, reciprocavi, reciprocatus (v., first conjugation)","meaning":"to move back and forth, to exchange","meaningCN":"来回移动；交换"},{"word":"reciprocatio","structure":"reciprocatio, reciprocationis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a moving back and forth","meaningCN":"往复运动；来回"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"reciprocate","pos":"v.","zh":"回报；报答；往复运动"},{"word":"reciprocation","pos":"n.","zh":"报答；互相给予；机械往复"},{"word":"reciprocity","pos":"n.","zh":"互惠；互惠性"},{"word":"reciprocally","pos":"adv.","zh":"相互地；对等地"},{"word":"reciprocating","pos":"adj.","zh":"往复式的"}]}},{"word":"mutuality","ipa_uk":"/ˌmjuːtjuˈæləti/","ipa_us":"/ˌmjuːtʃuˈæləti/","definition_zh":"相互性；共同性；互惠性；（互助组织成员间的）互担与共有关系","definition_en":"the quality of being shared, felt or owed by two or more parties toward one another","core_image":"两只手同时握住同一根绳子的两端，绳子被两边一起拉紧，谁松手另一端都会立刻感觉到","scene":"合作社成员彼此承担风险，谁家遇到困难，其余人按章程分担。The mutuality of the cooperative rests on members trusting one another with shared risks.","sceneCN":"合作社成员彼此承担风险，谁家遇到困难便由其余人按章程分担；句中的 mutuality 指「双方彼此共有、互相承担的性质」（第 1 个义项：关系两端同时拥有并互负义务）。图中可辨识物件：绷紧的绳索、两只相对的手、章程册。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"相互性；共同性；互惠性；互担关系"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"sense of mutuality","zh":"相互感；彼此共有的感觉"},{"phrase":"mutuality of obligation","zh":"义务的相互性"},{"phrase":"mutuality of interests","zh":"利益的共同性"},{"phrase":"principle of mutuality","zh":"相互性原则"},{"phrase":"mutuality of trust","zh":"信任的相互性"},{"phrase":"mutuality of respect","zh":"尊重的相互性"}],"forms":[{"label":"不可数用法","form":"uncountable"},{"label":"复数（少见）","form":"mutualities"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"mutual","pos":"adj.","zh":"相互的；共同的（去掉抽象名词后缀，回到性质本身）"},{"word":"mutually","pos":"adv.","zh":"相互地；彼此地（加副词后缀，表示以相互方式行事）"},{"word":"mutualism","pos":"n.","zh":"互利共生；互助主义（加表示「学说、制度」的后缀，转为一种关系类型或主张）"},{"word":"mutualist","pos":"n.","zh":"互利共生者；互助主义者（加表示「从事者」的后缀，由学说转指信奉者或物种）"},{"word":"mutualistic","pos":"adj.","zh":"互利共生的；互助的（在名词后加形容词后缀，用来修饰这类关系）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The state of being shared both ways","titleCN":"关系两端彼此共有的状态","definition":"the condition in which two or more parties hold, feel or owe something to one another at the same time","definitionCN":"两方或多方在同一时刻对彼此拥有、感受或负担某事的状态","example":"The mutuality of the partnership was clear: each side contributed and each side received.","exampleCN":"这种伙伴关系的相互性十分清楚：各方都有付出，各方也都有所得。","why":"the noun suffix -ity turns mutual into a quality, and mutual itself comes from a Latin word for what can be exchanged, so the core is a relation that runs in both directions at once.","whyCN":"抽象名词后缀把「相互的」这一形容词变成一种性质，而这一形容词的拉丁源头表示「可交换之物」，因此核心是同时朝两个方向运行的关系。"},{"no":"02","title":"A condition held in common","titleCN":"多方共同拥有、共同处于的状态","definition":"the quality of belonging to several parties at once rather than to any one of them","definitionCN":"同时属于多个方面、而不专属于任何一方的性质","example":"A mutuality of purpose held the scattered team together through the long winter.","exampleCN":"一种目标的共同性让这支分散的团队熬过了漫长的冬季。","why":"English extended the word from two parties to any group: what is mutual belongs to all of them, and that shared ownership is exactly what the noun names.","whyCN":"英语把这个词从两方扩展到任意群体：凡是相互的，就属于其中所有成员，而这种共同归属正是这个名词所指。"},{"no":"03","title":"Benefit that each side receives","titleCN":"交换中双方都得益的互惠性","definition":"the quality of an exchange in which each party gains, so that neither gains only at the other's cost","definitionCN":"一种交换的性质：各方都有所得，没有哪一方是纯粹以对方的损失获利","example":"Trade has mutuality only when neither partner is meant to lose.","exampleCN":"只有当任何一方都不该亏损时，贸易才具有互惠性。","why":"because the Latin source meant 'exchangeable', the noun naturally covers bargains: a deal has mutuality when the benefit travels both ways.","whyCN":"由于拉丁语源头意为「可交换的」，这个名词自然涵盖交易：当好处双向流动时，一笔生意就具有互惠性。"},{"no":"04","title":"Feeling that answers feeling","titleCN":"情感上的相互回应","definition":"the quality of an affection or regard that is returned by the other person in kind","definitionCN":"一方的情意或关切被对方以同样方式回应的性质","example":"Their long friendship rested on a quiet mutuality of affection.","exampleCN":"他们长久的友谊建立在一份安静的、彼此回应的情意之上。","why":"the word moved from things exchanged to feelings exchanged, since affection can be given and returned just as goods can.","whyCN":"这个词从交换物品转向交换感情，因为情意与货物一样可以给出，也可以被回还。"},{"no":"05","title":"Obligations borne by both parties","titleCN":"组织与契约中双方互负的义务关系","definition":"the arrangement in which each party owes duties to the other, as between employer and worker or among members of a society","definitionCN":"各方对彼此负有义务的安排，如雇主与雇员之间，或互助团体成员之间","example":"Employment law asks whether there is mutuality of obligation between the worker and the firm.","exampleCN":"劳动法要问的是：劳动者与公司之间是否存在义务的相互性。","why":"in law the word marks the point where duties stop being one-way; a contract has mutuality only if each side is bound.","whyCN":"在法律中，这个词标出义务不再单向的那一点：只有各方都受约束，契约才具有相互性。"},{"no":"06","title":"A relation with no fixed direction","titleCN":"哲学与逻辑中无固定方向的互依关系","definition":"the property of a relation in which dependence runs both ways, so that no party is prior to the other","definitionCN":"一种关系的性质：依赖双向运行，任何一方都不先于另一方","example":"The mutuality of the relation rules out treating one term as the cause of the other.","exampleCN":"这种关系的相互性排除了把其中一项当作另一项之因的做法。","why":"philosophy sharpened the everyday sense into a structural claim: where the dependence is mutual, neither direction can be made basic.","whyCN":"哲学把日常语义磨成一条结构主张：当依赖是相互的，任何方向都不能被当作根本。"},{"no":"07","title":"Exchange between species","titleCN":"生物共生中的互利关系","definition":"the two-way benefit that partners of different species obtain from living together","definitionCN":"不同物种的伙伴因共同生活而各自获得的双向好处","example":"The mutuality between a flowering plant and its pollinator is often described as a bargain.","exampleCN":"开花植物与其传粉者之间的互利关系，常被形容为一笔交易。","why":"ecology borrowed the noun because the relation is literally an exchange of services, which is what the Latin source named.","whyCN":"生态学借用这个名词，因为这种关系确实是服务的交换，而这正是拉丁语源头所命名的东西。"},{"no":"08","title":"Care that runs both ways","titleCN":"照护伦理中的对等互依","definition":"the ideal in which giving and receiving care are shared rather than assigned permanently to one side","definitionCN":"一种理想：给予照护与接受照护由双方共同承担，而非永久分派给一方","example":"The ethic of care rests on mutuality rather than on one-way generosity.","exampleCN":"照护伦理建立在相互性之上，而不是单向的施与。","why":"care ethics uses the word to correct the image of a strong giver and a passive receiver, insisting that the tie itself is what is shared.","whyCN":"照护伦理用这个词纠正「强者施与、被动受助」的画面，坚持被共享的是那条纽带本身。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Mutuality is mutual plus the Latin noun suffix -itas, which appears in English as -ity. Mutual comes from Late Latin mutuus 'exchangeable, reciprocal, borrowed'. Mutuus is generally thought to be connected with Latin mutare 'to change, exchange', but that link is the mainstream hypothesis rather than a settled fact.","cn":"mutuality 由 mutual 加拉丁抽象名词后缀 -itas 构成，该后缀在英语中沿用为对应的抽象名词后缀。mutual 出自晚期拉丁 mutuus「可交换的、相互的、借来的」。一般认为 mutuus 与拉丁 mutare「改变、交换」有关，但这只是主流假说，并非定论。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MUTARE","en":"Mutare meant 'to change, alter, exchange'. It is the verb of swapping, and it supplies the idea of something passing from one hand to another.","cn":"mutare 意为「改变、更改、交换」，是表示调换的动词，提供「某物从一只手转到另一只手」的观念。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN MUTUUS","en":"Mutuus meant 'exchangeable, reciprocal, borrowed'. It described what passes between two parties, including a loan that must come back.","cn":"mutuus 意为「可交换的、相互的、借来的」，描述在两个方之间流转之物，包括必须归还的借款。"},{"era":"LATIN SUFFIX -ITAS","en":"The suffix -itas formed abstract nouns of quality, and its English descendant -ity does the same work, turning an adjective into a name for a property.","cn":"后缀 -itas 构成表示性质的抽象名词，这一后缀在英语中沿用下来做同样的工作，把形容词变成某种性质的名称。"},{"era":"ENGLISH MUTUAL","en":"Mutual entered English in the sixteenth century, first describing things shared or felt by two parties alike.","cn":"mutual 于十六世纪进入英语，最初描述两方共同拥有或共同感受到的东西。"},{"era":"ENGLISH MUTUALITY","en":"The abstract noun appeared soon after, and by the nineteenth century it named the principle behind friendly societies, cooperatives and mutual insurance, where members carried one another's risks.","cn":"抽象名词随后出现，到十九世纪已用来指互助会、合作社与相互保险背后的原则，即成员彼此承担对方的风险。"},{"era":"SOURCE UNCERTAIN","en":"Source uncertain in one respect: whether mutuus really derives from mutare is generally thought to be so but is not demonstrated, so the derivation is stated as the mainstream hypothesis, not as proof.","cn":"有一处来源不确定：mutuus 是否真的由 mutare 派生，一般认为是，但未获证明，因此这一派生只作为主流假说陈述，而非定论。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words from the same Latin stock that look close and are often swapped by mistake; group two holds near neighbours, with reciprocity differing from mutuality in what it stresses.","cn":"第一组同出拉丁词源，形貌相近，常被误换；第二组是近义词，其中 reciprocity 与 mutuality 的侧重点不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"mutual","ipa":"/ˈmjuːtʃuəl/","tag":"the adjective","definition":"The adjective that mutuality is built on; it describes the shared thing itself, while the noun names the property of being shared.","definitionCN":"mutuality 所由构成的形容词；它描述被共享的事物本身，而名词则命名「被共享」这一性质。"},{"word":"mutually","ipa":"/ˈmjuːtʃuəli/","tag":"the adverb","definition":"Means 'in a mutual way' and modifies a verb, as in mutually agreed; it cannot replace the noun in subject or object position.","definitionCN":"意为「以相互的方式」，修饰动词，如「相互商定」；它不能在主语或宾语位置替代名词。"},{"word":"mutualism","ipa":"/ˈmjuːtʃuəlɪzəm/","tag":"a system or a symbiosis","definition":"Names either a social doctrine of mutual aid or a biological partnership of mutual benefit; it is a type of arrangement, not the general property.","definitionCN":"或指互助的社会主张，或指互利共生的生物伙伴关系；它是一种关系类型，而非一般性质。"},{"word":"mutability","ipa":"/ˌmjuːtəˈbɪləti/","tag":"same root, other meaning","definition":"From the same Latin verb for change but means 'changeableness', the capacity to alter; it is a false friend of mutuality despite the shared root.","definitionCN":"同出表示「改变」的拉丁动词，却意为「可变性」，即发生变化的能力；虽同根，却是 mutuality 的形近异义词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"reciprocity","ipa":"/ˌresɪˈprɒsəti/","tag":"balanced return","definition":"Stresses that a benefit or concession is returned in equal measure; mutuality stresses that a condition is shared, whether or not anything is repaid.","definitionCN":"强调好处或让步被等量回还；mutuality 强调某种状态被共同拥有，无论是否有回报。"},{"word":"interdependence","ipa":"/ˌɪntədɪˈpendəns/","tag":"need on both sides","definition":"Names the fact that each party needs the other; it says nothing about equality of benefit, which mutuality implies.","definitionCN":"指各方都需要对方这一事实；它不涉及好处是否对等，而 mutuality 含有这层意思。"},{"word":"commonality","ipa":"/kəˈmɒnəlti/","tag":"what is held in common","definition":"Focuses on shared features or interests within a group; it lacks the two-way obligation that mutuality often carries.","definitionCN":"侧重群体内共同的特征或利益；它缺少 mutuality 常带的双向义务意味。"},{"word":"solidarity","ipa":"/ˌsɒlɪˈdærəti/","tag":"standing together","definition":"Names loyalty and support among members of a group; it is a stance they take, while mutuality is the shape of the tie itself.","definitionCN":"指群体成员间的忠诚与支援，是一种姿态；而 mutuality 是纽带本身的形状。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations here are the real Latin steps, the real word family and the real institutions that use the noun.","cn":"正常联想取自这个词真实的拉丁语演变、真实词族，以及真正使用这个名词的制度场景。"},"normal":[{"en":"A Latin verb for exchange produced a word for what can be exchanged, and the noun suffix made that into a quality.","cn":"一个表示交换的拉丁动词先造出「可交换之物」，名词后缀再把这一性质固定下来。"},{"en":"The family runs mutual, mutually, mutuality, mutualism, mutualist, mutualistic.","cn":"词族包括 mutual、mutually、mutuality、mutualism、mutualist、mutualistic。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases show the legal and social settings: mutuality of obligation, mutuality of interests, principle of mutuality.","cn":"固定搭配显示法律与社会场景：义务的相互性、利益的共同性、相互性原则。"},{"en":"Insurance and cooperatives carry the word in their names: members insure one another rather than a distant company.","cn":"相互保险与合作社的名称里就带这一层意思：成员彼此承保，而不是向远处的公司投保。"},{"en":"Keep the two ideas apart: what is held together is not the same as what is returned in kind.","cn":"把两种观念分开：共同持有的东西，与等量回还的东西并不是一回事。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a rope pulled tight from both ends, where slack on one side is felt at once on the other.","cn":"想象一根两端都被拉紧的绳子，一端松了，另一端立刻就能感到。"},{"en":"Picture two people carrying one heavy crate, each lifting half the weight without asking who started first.","cn":"想象两个人抬一只重箱，各自承担一半重量，谁也不问是谁先起的意。"},{"en":"Picture a door held open by one person for another, and then held again on the way back.","cn":"想象有人为另一个人扶住门，回程时门又被对方扶住。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The report stresses the mutuality of the relationship rather than the duties of either partner alone.","cn":"报告强调的是这段关系的相互性，而不是任何一方单方面的义务。"},{"en":"Small farming cooperatives survive on mutuality: members share machinery, seed and risk.","cn":"小型农业合作社靠相互性存续：成员共用机械、种子，并共同承担风险。"},{"en":"A friendship without mutuality soon becomes a service one person provides.","cn":"缺少相互性的友谊，很快就会变成一个人单方面提供的服务。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"拆作「相互的」加抽象名词后缀——两边同时握住同一根绳子，谁松手另一端都感到 → 相互性、共同性、互惠性。","word":"mutuality"},"root":"晚期拉丁 mutuus「可交换的、相互的」→ 一般认为与拉丁 mutare「改变、交换」有关（主流假说，非定论）→ 加拉丁抽象名词后缀 -itas → 英语 mutuality；相互性来自「彼此交换」的意象。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one line: an exchange between two parties becomes a condition they hold in common, then a gain that both receive, a feeling returned in kind, an obligation carried on both shoulders, a relation with no fixed direction, a bargain between species, and finally an ideal of care shared rather than assigned.","cn":"八个义项沿一条线展开：两方之间的交换先成为一种共同持有的状态，再成为双方都得到的好处、被回应的情意、两肩共担的义务、没有固定方向的关系、物种之间的交易，最后落到照护由双方共担而非分派的理想。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one rope gripped at both ends, so that whatever one side does is immediately present on the other.","cn":"核心意象：一根两端都被握住的绳子，任何一端有所动作，另一端立刻就能感到。"},"chain":["EXCHANGE","SHARED HOLDING","BOTH-WAY GAIN","RETURNED FEELING","BOUND DUTY","COMMON LIFE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THE TIE ITSELF: exchange first produces a condition that both parties hold at once, and that shared holding is the plainest meaning of the noun.","cn":"纽带本身：交换先造出一种双方同时持有的状态，而这种共同持有正是这个名词最朴素的意思。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"BENEFIT AND AFFECTION: the exchange can carry goods, so both gain, or it can carry feeling, so regard is answered by regard.","cn":"好处与情意：交换可以运送货物，于是双方都得益；也可以运送感情，于是关切得到关切的回应。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"OBLIGATION AND STRUCTURE: in law the tie becomes duties on both shoulders, and in philosophy it becomes a dependence with no first term.","cn":"义务与结构：在法律里纽带变成两肩共担的职责，在哲学里则变成没有首项的相互依赖。"},{"senses":"07","en":"LIFE: different species strike the same bargain, trading nectar for transport and shelter for defence.","cn":"生命：不同物种做成同样的交易，以花蜜换运送，以栖处换防卫。"},{"senses":"08","en":"CARE: the final sense asks that giving and receiving not be fixed to one side, so the rope stays gripped at both ends.","cn":"照护：最后一个义项要求给予与接受不固定在一方，好让绳子两端始终都被握紧。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The word is one Latin adjective plus one Latin abstract-noun ending, with no native English element at all.","cn":"这个词由一个拉丁形容词加一个拉丁抽象名词结尾构成，不含任何英语本族成分。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin mutuus supplies the meaning and Latin -itas supplies the grammar; the verb mutare stands behind the adjective as a generally accepted but unproved relative.","cn":"拉丁 mutuus 提供意义，拉丁 -itas 提供语法功能；动词 mutare 作为一般认可但未经证明的亲缘词，站在形容词背后。"},"items":[{"word":"mutuus","structure":"Latin adjective, first and second declension","meaning":"exchangeable, reciprocal, borrowed","meaningCN":"可交换的；相互的；借来的","example":"This adjective is the direct source of the English base word.","exampleCN":"这个形容词是英语基础词的直接来源。"},{"word":"mutare","structure":"Latin verb, first conjugation","meaning":"to change, to exchange","meaningCN":"改变；交换","example":"The verb is generally thought to stand behind the adjective, though the link is not proved.","exampleCN":"一般认为动词站在该形容词背后，但这一联系未获证明。"},{"word":"-itas","structure":"Latin suffix forming abstract nouns","meaning":"the state or quality of","meaningCN":"表示「性质或状态」的抽象名词后缀","example":"This ending is the Latin ancestor of the English noun ending.","exampleCN":"这个结尾是英语名词后缀的拉丁前身。"},{"word":"-ity","structure":"English suffix from Latin -itas","meaning":"the quality of being","meaningCN":"表示「具有某种性质」的后缀","example":"This ending turns the adjective into the abstract noun.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把形容词变成抽象名词。"},{"word":"mutual","structure":"Latin mutuus reshaped in English","meaning":"shared or felt by both sides","meaningCN":"双方共同拥有或共同感受到的","example":"The adjective entered English in the sixteenth century.","exampleCN":"这个形容词于十六世纪进入英语。"},{"word":"mutually","structure":"adjective + adverb ending","meaning":"in a way that runs both ways","meaningCN":"以双向运行的方式","example":"The adverb modifies verbs such as agree or support.","exampleCN":"这个副词修饰「同意」「支持」一类动词。"},{"word":"-ism","structure":"suffix naming a system or practice","meaning":"a doctrine or a type of relation","meaningCN":"表示「学说、制度或关系类型」的后缀","example":"The ending produced the name of the doctrine of mutual aid.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出了表示互助主张的名称。"},{"word":"mutualism","structure":"base noun + doctrine ending","meaning":"mutual aid as a principle, or symbiosis for mutual benefit","meaningCN":"作为原则的互助，或互利共生","example":"The noun is used both in politics and in ecology.","exampleCN":"这个名词在政治学与生态学中都有人使用。"},{"word":"mutualist","structure":"noun + person ending","meaning":"one who holds or lives by mutual aid","meaningCN":"信奉互助或靠互助生活的一方","example":"The ending marks the bearer of the doctrine or the species.","exampleCN":"这个后缀标出该主张的信奉者或相关物种。"},{"word":"mutuality","structure":"adjective + abstract noun ending","meaning":"the property of being shared both ways","meaningCN":"双向共享这一性质","example":"The noun appeared in English after the adjective.","exampleCN":"这个名词在形容词之后出现于英语。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"mutuus","structure":"mutuus, mutua, mutuum (adj., first and second declension)","meaning":"exchangeable, reciprocal, borrowed","meaningCN":"可交换的；相互的；借来的"},{"word":"mutare","structure":"muto, mutare, mutavi, mutatus (v., first conjugation)","meaning":"to change, to exchange","meaningCN":"改变；交换"},{"word":"mutatio","structure":"mutatio, mutationis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a change, an exchange","meaningCN":"改变；交换"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"mutual","pos":"adj.","zh":"相互的；共同的"},{"word":"mutually","pos":"adv.","zh":"相互地；彼此地"},{"word":"mutualism","pos":"n.","zh":"互利共生；互助主义"},{"word":"mutualist","pos":"n.","zh":"互利共生者；互助主义者"},{"word":"mutualistic","pos":"adj.","zh":"互利共生的"}]}},{"word":"social network","ipa_uk":"/ˌsəʊʃl ˈnetwɜːk/","ipa_us":"/ˌsoʊʃl ˈnetwɜːrk/","definition_zh":"社会网络；人际关系网；（在线）社交网络平台；某一群体内相互连接的关系总称","definition_en":"the web of ties linking people to one another, or an online service through which users connect and share content","core_image":"一张纸上画满小圆点，点与点之间连着细线，线最密的地方人最多，孤零零的点只有一条线","scene":"研究者把村里谁帮过谁逐一记下，再把名字用线连起来，纸上渐渐显出一片网。The team mapped the social network of the village by recording who helped whom.","sceneCN":"研究者把村里谁帮过谁逐一记录，再用线把名字连起来，纸上渐渐显出一片网；句中的 social network 指「由人际关系连成的整体网络」（第 1 个义项：人与人之间实际往来所构成的关系网）。图中可辨识物件：手绘的关系图、连线的名字卡、村落地图。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"社会网络；人际关系网；社交平台（可数短语名词）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"social network analysis","zh":"社会网络分析"},{"phrase":"social network site","zh":"社交网站"},{"phrase":"online social network","zh":"在线社交网络"},{"phrase":"social network ties","zh":"社会网络纽带"},{"phrase":"social network theory","zh":"社会网络理论"},{"phrase":"build a social network","zh":"建立人脉网络"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"social network"},{"label":"复数","form":"social networks"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"social networking","pos":"n.","zh":"社交网络活动；通过网络建立关系（短语后加表示「活动、过程」的后缀，由静态的网转为持续的交往行为）"},{"word":"networking","pos":"n.","zh":"建立人脉；联网（由「网」这一名词加表示过程的后缀，指把关系或设备连起来这件事）"},{"word":"socially","pos":"adv.","zh":"在社会方面；在社交上（加副词后缀，把「社会的」转为修饰行为方式）"},{"word":"socialize","pos":"v.","zh":"交往；使社会化（加表示「使成为」的动词后缀，由「社会的」转为进入社会关系的过程）"},{"word":"networked","pos":"adj.","zh":"联网的；连成网络的（加过去分词后缀，表示已被连入网中）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The web of personal ties","titleCN":"由实际往来连成的人际关系网","definition":"the set of relationships that link a person to relatives, friends, neighbours and colleagues","definitionCN":"把一个人与亲戚、朋友、邻居和同事连接起来的那些关系的总和","example":"Most jobs in the village were found through the social network rather than through advertisements.","exampleCN":"村里大多数工作是通过人际关系网找到的，而不是通过广告。","why":"the phrase joins a word for companionship to a word for a mesh of threads, so the literal picture is people held together by lines of contact.","whyCN":"这个短语把表示「同伴」的词与表示「线网」的词连在一起，字面画面就是人被一条条往来之线系在一起。"},{"no":"02","title":"A structure that can be measured","titleCN":"可作为结构测量的社会网络","definition":"the pattern of ties in a group, studied as nodes and links with measurable density and reach","definitionCN":"一个群体中连线的格局，以节点与连线来研究，其密度与覆盖范围都可测量","example":"Research using social network analysis showed that two brokers connected the two halves of the firm.","exampleCN":"运用社会网络分析的研究显示，两名中间人把公司的两半连接了起来。","why":"sociology turned the everyday web into an object of measurement: once ties are drawn as lines between points, questions of distance and clustering can be asked.","whyCN":"社会学把日常的关系网变成可测量的对象：一旦把往来画成点与点之间的线，距离与聚集程度就可以提问了。"},{"no":"03","title":"An online platform of connections","titleCN":"在线社交网络平台","definition":"a website or application on which users create profiles and link to one another","definitionCN":"用户在其中建立个人页面并互相连接的网站或应用","example":"The campaign reached younger voters mainly through a social network.","exampleCN":"这场竞选活动主要通过一个社交平台接触到年轻选民。","why":"the digital sense keeps the old image and changes only the medium: the lines are now drawn by clicks rather than by visits.","whyCN":"数字义保留旧的意象，只换了媒介：线不再由走动画出，而由点击画出。"},{"no":"04","title":"Relationships as usable capital","titleCN":"当作资源调用的人脉","definition":"the contacts a person can call on for advice, introductions or favours","definitionCN":"一个人可以求取建议、引荐或帮忙的那些联系人","example":"She spent her first year in the city building a social network she could rely on.","exampleCN":"她在这座城市的第一年都在经营一张可以依靠的人脉网。","why":"because a network can be drawn on, English uses it for advantage: the tie is not only a description of closeness but a resource that can be spent.","whyCN":"由于网可以被取用，英语便用它来表示优势：连线不只是亲疏的描述，也是可以花掉的资源。"},{"no":"05","title":"The path along which news travels","titleCN":"信息借以扩散的传播路径","definition":"the routes through which information, rumour or behaviour passes from person to person","definitionCN":"信息、传言或行为从一个人传到另一个人的那些路径","example":"A rumour moves faster through a dense social network than through scattered strangers.","exampleCN":"传言在稠密的社会网络中比在分散的陌生人之间传得更快。","why":"a mesh is also a channel: whatever is placed on one thread can travel along the threads that touch it.","whyCN":"网同时也是通道：放在某一根线上的东西，可以沿着与它相接的线传开。"},{"no":"06","title":"Kin and mutual aid","titleCN":"人类学中的亲属与互助网络","definition":"the ties of marriage, descent and reciprocal help that hold a community together","definitionCN":"由婚姻、血缘与互相帮助构成、把一个社群维系在一起的连线","example":"Anthropologists traced the social network that decided who would harvest whose field.","exampleCN":"人类学家追踪了那张决定谁帮谁收割的社会网络。","why":"in small communities the web is often the whole economy: obligations run along kin lines, and the diagram explains who owes what.","whyCN":"在小社群里，这张网常常就是全部经济：义务沿着亲属连线运行，图一画出来，谁欠谁一目了然。"},{"no":"07","title":"Customers linked by talk","titleCN":"由口碑相连的顾客网络","definition":"the web of customer relationships along which recommendations and complaints spread","definitionCN":"顾客之间的关系网，推荐与抱怨沿着它传播","example":"The brand grew because its social network of users recommended it without being paid.","exampleCN":"这个品牌之所以成长，是因为它的用户网络在无偿地为它推荐。","why":"marketing borrowed the term for the same reason sociology did: word of mouth follows existing ties, not random contact.","whyCN":"营销学借这个词的理由与社会学相同：口碑沿着既有的连线走，而不走随机的接触。"},{"no":"08","title":"Ties among animals","titleCN":"行为生态学中的动物社会网络","definition":"the pattern of repeated associations among animals of the same population","definitionCN":"同一动物群体中个体之间反复结伴所形成的格局","example":"Biologists mapped the social network of the troop by noting every grooming pair.","exampleCN":"生物学家记录下每一对互相理毛的个体，从而绘出这个族群的社会网络。","why":"the phrase was extended to any population whose members recognize and repeatedly meet one another, because the geometry of ties is the same.","whyCN":"这个短语被扩展到任何成员彼此识别并反复相遇的群体，因为连线的几何形状是一样的。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Social network is a two-part phrase with two very different histories. Social comes from Latin socius 'companion, ally' through the adjective socialis. Network is a native English compound of net and work, both Old English words, and has no Latin source. The phrase as a term of sociology took shape in the twentieth century.","cn":"social network 是由两部分组成的短语，两部分的来历很不相同。social 经拉丁形容词 socialis 出自拉丁 socius「同伴、盟友」；network 是英语本族复合词，由 net 与 work 两个古英语词构成，并无拉丁来源。这个短语作为社会学术语在二十世纪成形。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN SOCIUS","en":"Socius meant 'companion, ally, partner'. Its deeper origin is uncertain; a link to the Latin verb for following is sometimes suggested but remains a hypothesis.","cn":"socius 意为「同伴、盟友、伙伴」。其更深来源不确定；有人提出它与表示「跟随」的拉丁动词有关，但那仍是假说。"},{"era":"LATIN SOCIALIS","en":"The adjective socialis 'of a companion, allied, sociable' was formed with the adjective suffix -alis, and it supplied the English word social.","cn":"形容词 socialis「同伴的、结盟的、好交际的」由形容词性后缀 -alis 构成，英语的 social 即由此而来。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH NET","en":"Net is a native word for a mesh of cords with openings, recorded in Old English and going back to a reconstructed Germanic form; it is not related to Latin.","cn":"net 是英语本族词，指带孔洞的绳网，古英语已有记录，可追溯到日耳曼语的重构形式；它与拉丁语无关。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH WEORC","en":"Weorc meant 'work, deed, something made'. Net and weorc were joined in English to name a woven mesh of threads, and later any interconnected system.","cn":"weorc 意为「工作、作为、做成之物」。net 与 weorc 在英语中结合，先指编成的线网，后来指任何彼此连接的系统。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH PHRASE","en":"By the twentieth century the compound network was applied to railways, telephones and then to people, and social network became the standard phrase for a web of human ties.","cn":"到二十世纪，复合词 network 先后用于铁路、电话，再用于人，social network 于是成为表示人际关系网的标准说法。"},{"era":"SOURCE UNCERTAIN","en":"The phrase was fixed as a sociological term in the 1950s, and the online sense followed in the 2000s. Source note: the Latin noun for companion has an uncertain deeper origin, and every form proposed for the Germanic net is a reconstruction.","cn":"这个短语在二十世纪五十年代固定为社会学用语，在线义则在二十一世纪初出现。来源说明：拉丁语中表示同伴的名词其更深来源不确定，为日耳曼语 net 提出的形式均属重构形式。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds forms of the same phrase and its close compounds, which are constantly confused; group two holds neighbouring ideas, each naming a different part of the same picture.","cn":"第一组是同一短语的各种形式与近邻复合词，极易混淆；第二组是相邻概念，各自指同一幅画面中的不同部分。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"social networking","ipa":"/ˈsəʊʃl ˈnetwɜːkɪŋ/","tag":"the activity","definition":"Names the activity of building and using ties, especially online; the plain phrase names the web itself, not the doing.","definitionCN":"指建立并使用关系的活动，尤指在线进行；原短语指这张网本身，而不是这件事。"},{"word":"social media","ipa":"/ˈsəʊʃl ˈmiːdiə/","tag":"the content and channels","definition":"Names the platforms and published content; a social network is the pattern of connections those platforms make visible.","definitionCN":"指平台与发布的内容；social network 则是这些平台使之可见的连接格局。"},{"word":"network","ipa":"/ˈnetwɜːk/","tag":"the bare compound","definition":"The general word for any interconnected system, from railways to computers; it says nothing about people unless social is attached.","definitionCN":"泛指任何互联系统，从铁路到计算机；若不加上 social，便与人无关。"},{"word":"networking","ipa":"/ˈnetwɜːkɪŋ/","tag":"meeting people for use","definition":"The practical activity of making professional contacts, often at events; it is narrower and more purposeful than a whole social network.","definitionCN":"指在活动中建立职业联系的实际行为；它比整张社会网络更窄、更有目的性。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"community","ipa":"/kəˈmjuːnəti/","tag":"a bounded group","definition":"A group defined by place, interest or identity; a social network is defined by the ties themselves, which may cross community borders.","definitionCN":"由地点、兴趣或身份界定的群体；社会网络则由连线本身界定，可以跨越社群边界。"},{"word":"social capital","ipa":"/ˈsəʊʃl ˈkæpɪtl/","tag":"the value of ties","definition":"The advantage a person gains from having ties; it is the yield of the network, not the network's shape.","definitionCN":"一个人因拥有连线而获得的优势；它是网络的产出，而非网络的形状。"},{"word":"social circle","ipa":"/ˈsəʊʃl ˈsɜːkl/","tag":"immediate company","definition":"The people one regularly meets socially; it is a small, personal ring rather than a mapped structure.","definitionCN":"指一个人日常交往的那群人；它是小型的私人圈子，而非被绘出的结构。"},{"word":"kinship network","ipa":"/ˈkɪnʃɪp ˈnetwɜːk/","tag":"ties by blood and marriage","definition":"A web formed only by descent and marriage; the broader social network also includes friendship, work and exchange.","definitionCN":"仅由血缘与婚姻构成的网；更广义的社会网络还包括友谊、工作与交换关系。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations here are the real Latin half, the native English half and the real research settings in which the phrase is used.","cn":"正常联想取自这个短语真实的拉丁语一半、英语本族一半，以及它真正出现的研究场景。"},"normal":[{"en":"Half the phrase is Latin 'companion', half is Old English 'net' plus 'work': a mesh made of companions.","cn":"短语的一半是拉丁语的「同伴」，另一半是古英语的「网」加「做工」：由同伴编成的网。"},{"en":"The family runs social, socially, socialize, networking, networked.","cn":"词族包括 social、socially、socialize、networking、networked。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the research setting: social network analysis, social network ties, social network theory.","cn":"固定搭配标出研究场景：社会网络分析、社会网络纽带、社会网络理论。"},{"en":"The diagram is the mnemonic: dots are people, lines are contact, dense patches are where influence travels.","cn":"图本身就是记忆线索：点是人物，线是往来，线密处正是影响力流动的地方。"},{"en":"Digital use changes the medium, not the picture: profiles and follows are dots and lines again.","cn":"数字化只换媒介，不换画面：主页与关注仍然是点与线。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a rope bridge whose planks are names, each plank held by the two beside it.","cn":"想象一座绳桥，桥板是一个个名字，每块板都由左右两块托住。"},{"en":"Picture a rumour crossing a courtyard from window to window without ever entering the street.","cn":"想象一则传言从一个窗口传到另一个窗口，穿过整个院子，却始终没有走到街上。"},{"en":"Picture a single dot at the edge of the page with only one line leaving it, and everyone knows whom it relies on.","cn":"想象纸边一个孤点只伸出一条线，所有人都知道它靠的是谁。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"A longitudinal study found that a sparse social network predicted loneliness better than income did.","cn":"一项追踪研究发现，稀疏的社会网络比收入更能预测孤独感。"},{"en":"The firm's growth depended on a social network of suppliers who vouched for one another.","cn":"这家公司的成长依赖于一张供应商彼此担保的社会网络。"},{"en":"She left the platform but kept the social network it had given her.","cn":"她离开了那个平台，却留下了平台给她的那张人脉网。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"拆作「social（社会的）+ network（网）」——把认识的人用线连成一张网，网上既是关系也是平台 → 社会网络、人脉、社交网站。","word":"social network"},"root":"social：拉丁 socius「同伴、盟友」→ 形容词 socialis（加 -alis）→ 英语 social；network：古英语 net「网」+ weorc「工作、做成之物」构成英语本族复合词，非拉丁来源 → 二十世纪社会学中固定为 social network。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one line: a drawn web of personal ties becomes a measurable structure, then a platform that redraws it, a resource to spend, a channel for news, a kin-based support system, a market of talk, and finally the same geometry among animals.","cn":"八个义项沿一条线展开：一张被画出的人际网先成为可测量的结构，再成为重新绘制它的平台、可以花掉的资源、新闻的通道、以亲属为骨架的互助体系、由口碑构成的市场，最后落到动物之间同样的几何形状。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: names placed as dots on paper and joined by lines, so that closeness becomes a visible distance.","cn":"核心意象：把名字当作纸上的点，再用线连起来，亲疏于是变成可见的距离。"},"chain":["TIES","MEASURABLE STRUCTURE","ONLINE PLATFORM","USABLE RESOURCE","DIFFUSION","COMMUNITY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"FROM LIFE TO DIAGRAM: real visits first form the web, and method then turns that web into nodes, links and density.","cn":"从生活到图纸：真实走动先织成网，方法再把这张网变成节点、连线与密度。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"MEDIUM AND ADVANTAGE: the platform redraws the lines by clicks, and those lines become capital that can be called upon.","cn":"媒介与优势：平台用点击重新画线，而这些线又成为可以调用的资本。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"FLOW AND SUPPORT: the mesh carries news along its threads, and along kin threads it carries help and obligation.","cn":"流动与支撑：网沿着线运送消息，也沿着亲属线运送帮助与义务。"},{"senses":"07","en":"MARKET: talk about a product follows the same threads, so the network doubles as a sales channel.","cn":"市场：关于产品的谈论沿着同样的线走，于是这张网同时成为销售渠道。"},{"senses":"08","en":"OTHER SPECIES: the geometry is unchanged when the dots are animals that groom, hunt or travel together.","cn":"其他物种：当点是互相理毛、一同捕猎或迁徙的动物时，几何形状并未改变。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase splits cleanly into a Latin-derived half and a native English half, and neither half should be explained with the other's history.","cn":"这个短语可以干净地分成拉丁来源的一半与英语本族的一半，两半的历史不应互相套用。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin socius supplies the social half through socialis and the adjective suffix -alis; the network half comes from Old English net and weorc and has no Latin entry behind it.","cn":"拉丁 socius 经 socialis 与形容词后缀 -alis 提供「社会」这一半；「网」这一半来自古英语的 net 与 weorc，背后并没有拉丁词形。"},"items":[{"word":"socius","structure":"Latin noun, second declension","meaning":"companion, ally, partner","meaningCN":"同伴；盟友；伙伴","example":"This noun supplies the social half of the phrase.","exampleCN":"这个名词提供短语中「社会」的那一半。"},{"word":"-alis","structure":"Latin adjective suffix","meaning":"relating to, belonging to","meaningCN":"表示「与……有关的、属于……的」形容词后缀","example":"The ending turned the noun for companion into an adjective.","exampleCN":"这个结尾把表示同伴的名词变成形容词。"},{"word":"socialis","structure":"Latin adjective, third declension","meaning":"of companions, allied, sociable","meaningCN":"同伴的；结盟的；好交际的","example":"This adjective is the direct source of the English word for social.","exampleCN":"这个形容词是英语中表示「社会的」那个词的直接来源。"},{"word":"social","structure":"Latin adjective reshaped in English","meaning":"concerning people living together","meaningCN":"关于共同生活的人的","example":"The adjective entered English in the sixteenth century.","exampleCN":"这个形容词于十六世纪进入英语。"},{"word":"-ize","structure":"verb-forming suffix","meaning":"to make or become","meaningCN":"表示「使成为、变得」的动词后缀","example":"The ending produced the verb for entering social life.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出了表示进入社会生活的动词。"},{"word":"-ly","structure":"adverb-forming suffix","meaning":"in the stated manner","meaningCN":"表示「以所述方式」的副词后缀","example":"The ending produced the adverb from the adjective.","exampleCN":"这个后缀由该形容词造出副词。"},{"word":"net","structure":"Old English noun, native word","meaning":"a mesh of cords with openings","meaningCN":"带孔洞的绳网","example":"This native word is the first half of the compound.","exampleCN":"这个本族词是复合词的前一半。"},{"word":"weorc","structure":"Old English noun, native word","meaning":"work, deed, something made","meaningCN":"工作；作为；做成之物","example":"This native word is the second half of the compound.","exampleCN":"这个本族词是复合词的后一半。"},{"word":"network","structure":"native compound of net and work","meaning":"a woven mesh, later any interconnected system","meaningCN":"编成的网，后来指任何互联系统","example":"The compound was extended from threads to railways and telephones.","exampleCN":"这个复合词从线网扩展到铁路与电话。"},{"word":"-ing","structure":"suffix forming nouns of activity","meaning":"the doing of something","meaningCN":"表示「进行某事」的名词后缀","example":"The ending produced the name of the activity of making contacts.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出了表示建立联系这一活动的名词。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"socius","structure":"socius, soci (m., second declension)","meaning":"companion, ally, partner","meaningCN":"同伴；盟友；伙伴"},{"word":"socialis","structure":"socialis, sociale (adj., third declension)","meaning":"of companions, allied, sociable","meaningCN":"同伴的；结盟的；好交际的"},{"word":"societas","structure":"societas, societatis (f., third declension)","meaning":"association, partnership","meaningCN":"结社；合伙关系"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"social networking","pos":"n.","zh":"社交网络活动；建立人脉"},{"word":"networking","pos":"n.","zh":"建立人脉；联网"},{"word":"socially","pos":"adv.","zh":"在社会方面；在社交上"},{"word":"socialize","pos":"v.","zh":"交往；使社会化"},{"word":"networked","pos":"adj.","zh":"联网的；连成网络的"}]}},{"word":"social support","ipa_uk":"/ˈsəʊʃəl səˈpɔːt/","ipa_us":"/ˈsoʊʃəl səˈpɔːrt/","definition_zh":"社会支持；他人提供的实际援助与情感帮助；社会支持网络","definition_en":"the practical and emotional help that a person receives through family, friends, neighbours and institutions","core_image":"一个人病倒在床，门口陆续出现一篮菜、一张卡片和一双帮忙做饭的手","scene":"在老城区的一栋旧楼里，邻居轮流给独居的老人送饭、陪他说话，社区护士每周上门量血压。That steady social support helps him recover faster from illness.","sceneCN":"句中 social support 指由邻里与社区关系提供的实际照顾和陪伴（第 1 个义项：经由人际关系网络到达一个人的帮助）；句意为这种稳定的社会支持帮助老人更快康复。图中可辨识物件：饭盒、手写卡片、血压计、楼道扶手。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"社会支持（不可数名词短语）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"social support network","zh":"社会支持网络"},{"phrase":"emotional social support","zh":"情感性社会支持"},{"phrase":"perceived social support","zh":"感知到的社会支持"},{"phrase":"provide social support","zh":"提供社会支持"},{"phrase":"receive social support","zh":"获得社会支持"},{"phrase":"social support system","zh":"社会支持体系"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"social support"},{"label":"复数（少见，指多种支持）","form":"social supports"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"social","pos":"adj.","zh":"社会的；社交的"},{"word":"support","pos":"n./v.","zh":"支持；支撑；供养"},{"word":"supportive","pos":"adj.","zh":"给予支持的；体谅的"},{"word":"supporter","pos":"n.","zh":"支持者；拥护者"},{"word":"socially","pos":"adv.","zh":"在社会方面；在社交上"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Help given through personal ties","titleCN":"由人际关系网络提供的帮助","definition":"the practical and emotional help that comes to a person through family, friends and neighbours","definitionCN":"经由家人、朋友与邻里到达一个人身上的实际帮助与情感帮助","example":"That steady social support helps him recover faster from illness.","exampleCN":"那种稳定的社会支持帮助他更快地从疾病中恢复。","why":"social marks what belongs to a community of people, and support marks the act of holding something up from beneath, so together they name help that reaches a person through other people.","whyCN":"social 标出「属于人群共同体」的属性，support 标出「从下面托住」的动作，合起来就是通过他人到达某人的帮助。"},{"no":"02","title":"Emotional comfort from others","titleCN":"来自他人的情感安慰","definition":"the reassurance, sympathy and sense of being cared for that other people give","definitionCN":"他人给予的宽慰、同情与「有人关心我」的感受","example":"She drew emotional social support from a weekly call with her sister.","exampleCN":"她从每周与姐姐的一次通话中获得情感上的社会支持。","why":"the phrase covers not only goods and services but also the intangible weight of feeling, because being held up can be emotional as well as material.","whyCN":"这个短语不只覆盖物资与服务，也覆盖无形的情绪负担，因为「被托住」既可以是情感上的，也可以是物质上的。"},{"no":"03","title":"Instrumental aid and services","titleCN":"工具性援助与实际事务帮助","definition":"concrete assistance such as money, transport, childcare or help with chores","definitionCN":"金钱、交通、照看孩子或代做家务等具体援助","example":"Instrumental social support paid the bus fare and covered two weeks of meals.","exampleCN":"工具性社会支持付了公交费，还承担了两周的饭食。","why":"the oldest sense of support is bearing a weight from below, and the most literal way to bear a weight for someone is to run the errand or pay the bill.","whyCN":"support 最古老的意思是「从下方承重」，而为别人承重最字面的做法就是替他跑腿或付账。"},{"no":"04","title":"Perceived rather than received","titleCN":"主观感知到的支持而非实际所得","definition":"the help a person believes to be available, which may differ from what is actually given","definitionCN":"一个人相信可以获得的帮助，可能与实际得到的并不相同","example":"Perceived social support predicted wellbeing better than the number of visitors.","exampleCN":"感知到的社会支持比来访人数更能预测幸福感。","why":"psychology separates what is given from what is felt, because a person under strain may discount real help while believing that none is available.","whyCN":"心理学把「给予的」与「感受到的」分开，因为压力中的人可能贬低真实的帮助，却相信无人可依。"},{"no":"05","title":"The network itself","titleCN":"支持网络：能提供帮助的那张关系网","definition":"the set of relatives, friends, colleagues and agencies on whom a person can call","definitionCN":"一个人可以求助的亲属、朋友、同事与机构所构成的集合","example":"His social support thinned after the factory closed and the shift mates dispersed.","exampleCN":"工厂关闭、工友四散之后，他的社会支持网络变得稀薄。","why":"by metonymy the phrase shifts from the help to the people who supply it, so one may speak of support that grows thin or wide.","whyCN":"短语以转喻由「帮助」转到「提供帮助的人」，于是可以说支持网络变稀薄或变宽阔。"},{"no":"06","title":"Formal care in social policy","titleCN":"社会政策层面的正式照护与保障","definition":"the organised provision of care by public services, charities or employers","definitionCN":"由公共服务、慈善机构或雇主组织的照护供给","example":"The council treats social support for the elderly as part of public health.","exampleCN":"议会把面向老年人的社会支持视为公共卫生的一部分。","why":"once the concept entered policy, the phrase also named what institutions rather than kin provide, widening from private ties to public arrangement.","whyCN":"概念进入政策领域后，这个短语也指由机构而非亲属提供的照护，从私人关系扩展到公共安排。"},{"no":"07","title":"Buffer against stress","titleCN":"作为压力缓冲的社会支持","definition":"the protective effect that available help has on a person facing strain","definitionCN":"可获得的帮助对处于压力中的人产生的保护作用","example":"Researchers measured social support as a buffer between workload and burnout.","exampleCN":"研究者把社会支持作为工作量与职业倦怠之间的缓冲来测量。","why":"the buffering model pictures help as a cushion placed beneath a falling body, which keeps the original physical image of the word alive.","whyCN":"缓冲模型把帮助想象成垫在坠落身体下方的软垫，这个词的物理意象由此得以保留。"},{"no":"08","title":"Help that arrives through weak ties","titleCN":"经由弱连接到达的帮助","definition":"support that reaches a person through acquaintances and casual contacts rather than close family or intimate friends","definitionCN":"通过熟人、一般交往而非至亲密友到达一个人的帮助","example":"After he moved to the city, most social support came through weak ties at work.","exampleCN":"他搬到城里之后，大部分社会支持是经由工作上的弱连接得到的。","why":"weak ties bridge separate clusters of people, so aid can travel along links that are not intimate; sociologists use the phrase this way when they separate it from close-knit support.","whyCN":"弱连接把彼此分离的人群接起来，帮助因此能沿着并不亲密的联系传递；社会学家把它与至亲网络的支持区分开时，正是这个用法。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Social comes from Latin socialis, from socius 'companion, ally'. Support comes from Latin supportare, built on a prefix meaning 'under' and portare 'to carry', literally 'to bear up from beneath'. The two words joined as a fixed phrase in twentieth-century sociology and have been widely used since the 1970s. Dates are approximate.","cn":"social 出自拉丁 socialis，源于 socius「同伴、盟友」。support 出自拉丁 supportare，由表示「在下」的前缀与表示「搬运、承载」的 portare 构成，本义是「从下面托住」。两词在二十世纪社会学中合为固定短语，二十世纪七十年代起大量使用。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN SOCIUS","en":"Socius meant 'companion, ally' and gave the adjective socialis 'of companions, of a community', which English took as social.","cn":"socius 意为「同伴、盟友」，其形容词 socialis 意为「同伴的、共同体的」，英语吸收为 social。"},{"era":"LATIN SUPPORTARE","en":"The prefix meaning 'under' plus portare 'to carry' produced supportare 'to bear up, sustain', a picture of something held from below.","cn":"表示「在下」的前缀加 portare「搬运」构成 supportare「托住、支撑」，画面是一个东西被从下面承住。"},{"era":"FRENCH AND ENGLISH","en":"Support reached English through Old French supporter, at first naming a physical prop and later any assistance, including money and encouragement.","cn":"support 经古法语 supporter 进入英语，先指实际的支撑物，后指任何援助，包括金钱与鼓励。"},{"era":"SOCIAL SCIENCE TERMS","en":"From the nineteenth century social was attached to many new compound terms in the study of society, and social support appeared among them in the twentieth century.","cn":"十九世纪起 social 在社会研究中与大量新复合词结合，social support 于二十世纪加入其中。"},{"era":"RESEARCH SINCE THE 1970S","en":"In the 1970s studies of health and stress fixed the phrase as a technical term for help drawn from relationships, and it spread into medicine and policy.","cn":"二十世纪七十年代的健康与压力研究把这个短语固定为指「由关系中获得帮助」的术语，随后进入医学与政策领域。"},{"era":"SOURCE UNCERTAIN","en":"The deeper origin of Latin portare is uncertain; the link sometimes proposed to a root meaning 'to lead across' is a reconstruction rather than a settled derivation.","cn":"拉丁 portare 的更早来源不确定；有人提出的、与表示「引过、渡送」的词根的联系属重构形式，并非已定论的派生。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds expressions built on the same support stock that are easily confused; group two holds social-science terms about help, each covering a different slice.","cn":"第一组是同出「支撑」词族、容易混淆的说法；第二组是关于帮助的社会学术语，各自覆盖不同的一块。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"support system","ipa":"/ˈsʌpɔːt ˈsɪstəm/","tag":"parts that hold a structure","definition":"The collection of beams, struts or devices that carry a load; it is a technical phrase, not the sociological one.","definitionCN":"承担荷载的梁柱或装置集合；属技术说法，不是社会学概念。"},{"word":"social network","ipa":"/ˈsəʊʃəl ˈnetwɜːk/","tag":"the web of ties","definition":"Names the connections themselves; social support names what flows through those connections.","definitionCN":"指关系连线本身；社会支持指通过这些连线流动的东西。"},{"word":"social capital","ipa":"/ˈsəʊʃəl ˈkæpɪtl/","tag":"resources of trust","definition":"The trust and reciprocity stored in a community, viewed as a resource; it is broader than one person's support.","definitionCN":"一个社群中储存的信任与互惠，被当作资源看待；比单个人获得的支持更宽。"},{"word":"social security","ipa":"/ˈsəʊʃəl sɪˈkjʊərəti/","tag":"state payments","definition":"Government payments to those in need; it is an institution, while social support also includes informal help.","definitionCN":"政府向有需要者的给付；属制度安排，而社会支持还包括非正式帮助。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"assistance","ipa":"/əˈsɪstəns/","tag":"generic help","definition":"Any help given, without implying a lasting relationship; social support stresses ties that persist.","definitionCN":"泛指给予的帮助，不含持久关系的意味；社会支持强调持续存在的关系。"},{"word":"care","ipa":"/keə/","tag":"looking after someone","definition":"The work of tending to someone's needs; social support is the wider frame in which such care counts as help.","definitionCN":"照料某人需要的劳动；社会支持是把这类照料算作帮助的更大框架。"},{"word":"solidarity","ipa":"/ˌsɒlɪˈdærəti/","tag":"mutual commitment","definition":"A shared readiness to stand by others; it is a collective attitude, whereas social support is the help actually received.","definitionCN":"共同承担、彼此站在一边的态度；它是集体态度，而社会支持是实际得到的帮助。"},{"word":"backing","ipa":"/ˈbækɪŋ/","tag":"endorsement or funding","definition":"Support in the form of approval, money or influence, often from an organisation; it lacks the personal warmth of social support.","definitionCN":"以认可、资金或影响力形式给出的支持，多来自机构；缺少社会支持那种人情温度。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations here are the real Latin parts of both words, the real terms built on them, and the real research setting in which the phrase was fixed.","cn":"正常联想取自两个词真实的拉丁成分、由它们构成的真实术语，以及这个短语被固定下来的真实研究背景。"},"normal":[{"en":"socius 'companion' gives social: help that arrives through companions.","cn":"socius「同伴」给出 social：通过同伴到达的帮助。"},{"en":"The prefix for 'under' plus portare 'to carry': support is literally bearing a weight from below.","cn":"表示「在下」的前缀加 portare「搬运」：support 字面上就是从下面承重。"},{"en":"The family runs support, supportive, supporter, social and socially.","cn":"词族包括 support、supportive、supporter、social 与 socially。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the research sense: perceived social support, social support network, emotional social support.","cn":"固定搭配标出研究义：感知到的社会支持、社会支持网络、情感性社会支持。"},{"en":"Keep it apart from support system, which names beams and struts rather than people.","cn":"与「支持系统」区分开，后者指梁柱构件，不指人。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture an outstretched palm under a falling object: that is support before it ever becomes a word.","cn":"想象一只摊开的手掌垫在坠落物下方：那是 support 成为词之前的样子。"},{"en":"Picture a doorway where three different neighbours leave three different things on the same day.","cn":"想象同一天里，三个邻居在同一扇门口放下三样不同的东西。"},{"en":"Picture a net woven of names, and the net still holds when one strand is cut.","cn":"想象一张由人名织成的网，断掉一根线时网仍然托得住。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"That steady social support helps him recover faster from illness.","cn":"那种稳定的社会支持帮助他更快地从疾病中恢复。"},{"en":"After moving to a new city, he built social support slowly, one neighbour at a time.","cn":"搬到一个新城市后，他慢慢地建立起社会支持，一个邻居一个邻居地来。"},{"en":"The survey asked whether perceived social support matched the help actually received.","cn":"这项调查询问感知到的社会支持是否与实际得到的帮助相符。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「social（同伴）+ support（从下面托住）」——同伴把你从下面托住 → 社会支持","word":"social support"},"root":"拉丁 socius「同伴、盟友」→ socialis → social；拉丁表示「在下」的前缀 + portare「搬运、承载」→ supportare「托住」→ 古法语 supporter → support。两词在二十世纪社会学中合为短语，二十世纪七十年代起广泛使用。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one gesture: a weight is held from below by people around the bearer, and that gesture is then split into emotional and material help, into what is felt rather than given, into the network itself, into public provision, into a cushioning effect, and finally into aid that travels along weak ties.","cn":"八个义项沿同一个动作展开：周围的人从下方承住承受者的重量；这一动作再分出情感与物质两类帮助，分出「感受到的」而非「给予的」，分出关系网本身，分出公共供给，分出缓冲效应，最后落到经由弱连接到达的帮助。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: hands placed under a burden so that the bearer does not fall.","cn":"核心意象：一双手垫在重负之下，使承重者不至于倒下。"},"chain":["COMPANIONS","BEAR FROM BELOW","HELP RECEIVED","EMOTIONAL AID","NETWORK OF TIES","BUFFER EFFECT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"HELP THROUGH TIES: the basic sense and its emotional side, both arriving through people one knows.","cn":"经关系而来的帮助：基本义及其情感面，都经由认识的人到达。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"GIVEN AND FELT: concrete aid on one side, the subjective estimate of available help on the other.","cn":"给予与感受：一边是具体援助，另一边是对可获得帮助的主观估计。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"FROM PEOPLE TO INSTITUTIONS: the phrase shifts from the network of kin to organised public care.","cn":"从人到机构：短语由亲属网络扩展到有组织的公共照护。"},{"senses":"07","en":"CUSHION: the help works as a pad that absorbs the shock of strain.","cn":"缓冲垫：帮助像垫子一样吸收压力带来的冲击。"},{"senses":"08","en":"BRIDGE: support also names the aid that arrives along weak ties, which link clusters that intimate ties cannot reach.","cn":"桥接：社会支持也指沿弱连接到达的援助，这种联系能抵达亲密关系所到不了的群体。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase can be read in two halves: social, built on the Latin noun for a companion, and support, built on a prefix for 'under' plus a verb for carrying.","cn":"这个短语可以分两半读：social 建立在拉丁语表示「同伴」的名词上，support 建立在表示「在下」的前缀与表示「搬运」的动词上。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin socius and socialis supply social; Latin portare and supportare supply support and its English family.","cn":"拉丁 socius 与 socialis 提供 social 的来源；拉丁 portare 与 supportare 提供 support 及其英语词族。"},"items":[{"word":"soci-","structure":"Latin stem of socius, 'companion, ally'","meaning":"companion; ally; associated person","meaningCN":"同伴；盟友；结伴者","example":"The stem carries the idea of people bound together.","exampleCN":"这个词干带着「人们结伴相连」的意思。"},{"word":"-alis","structure":"Latin adjective suffix, from -alis","meaning":"belonging to, relating to","meaningCN":"属于……的；与……相关的","example":"The suffix turns the noun for a companion into an adjective.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把表示同伴的名词变成形容词。"},{"word":"social","structure":"soci- + -alis","meaning":"of companionship or community","meaningCN":"同伴的；共同体的","example":"Social ties are the channel through which help arrives.","exampleCN":"社会关系是帮助得以到达的通道。"},{"word":"sub-","structure":"Latin prefix meaning 'under'","meaning":"under; from below","meaningCN":"在下；从下方","example":"The prefix fixes the direction of the action.","exampleCN":"这个前缀确定了动作的方向。"},{"word":"portare","structure":"Latin verb, first conjugation","meaning":"to carry, bear","meaningCN":"搬运；承载","example":"The verb supplies the carrying in support.","exampleCN":"这个动词为 support 提供「承载」之义。"},{"word":"support","structure":"sub- + portare","meaning":"to bear up from beneath","meaningCN":"从下面托住；支撑","example":"The verb became a noun as well as a verb.","exampleCN":"这个词同时成为名词与动词。"},{"word":"-ive","structure":"suffix forming adjectives from verbs","meaning":"tending to, having the nature of","meaningCN":"倾向于……的；具有……性质的","example":"The suffix yields supportive, describing a person who gives help.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出表示「给予支持」的形容词。"},{"word":"-er","structure":"suffix forming agent nouns","meaning":"one who does","meaningCN":"做某事的人","example":"The suffix yields supporter, one who backs another.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出表示「支持者」的名词。"},{"word":"-ly","structure":"suffix forming adverbs from adjectives","meaning":"in the manner of","meaningCN":"以……的方式","example":"The suffix yields socially, as in socially isolated.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出副词，用于「在社会上被孤立」一类说法。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"socius","structure":"socius, socii (m., second declension)","meaning":"companion, ally, associate","meaningCN":"同伴；盟友；合伙人"},{"word":"socialis","structure":"socialis, sociale (adj., third declension)","meaning":"of companions, of a community","meaningCN":"同伴的；共同体的"},{"word":"portare","structure":"portare, portavi, portatum (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to carry, bear, transport","meaningCN":"搬运；承载；运送"},{"word":"supportare","structure":"supportare, supportavi, supportatum (verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to bear up, sustain, support","meaningCN":"托住；支撑；维持"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"social","pos":"adj.","zh":"社会的；社交的"},{"word":"support","pos":"n./v.","zh":"支持；支撑；供养"},{"word":"supportive","pos":"adj.","zh":"给予支持的；体谅的"},{"word":"supporter","pos":"n.","zh":"支持者；拥护者"},{"word":"socially","pos":"adv.","zh":"在社会方面；在社交上"}]}},{"word":"social interaction","ipa_uk":"/ˈsəʊʃəl ˌɪntərˈækʃən/","ipa_us":"/ˈsoʊʃəl ˌɪntərˈækʃən/","definition_zh":"社会互动；社会交往；人与人之间的相互往来","definition_en":"the reciprocal action and communication that takes place between people","core_image":"两个人隔着桌子一来一往地递东西，一个递出，一个接住，动作始终不断","scene":"在菜市场里，摊主与熟客一边挑菜一边聊天，一个问价，一个还价，话头来回接住。Everyday social interaction in the market keeps neighbours informed and ties them together.","sceneCN":"句中 social interaction 指摊主与顾客之间你一言我一语、彼此回应的往来（第 1 个义项：人与人之间相互动作与交流的基本形态）；句意为市场里的日常社会互动让邻里互通消息、彼此联结。图中可辨识物件：菜筐、秤、零钱、写价目的纸牌。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"社会互动；社会交往（可数或不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"face-to-face social interaction","zh":"面对面的社会互动"},{"phrase":"patterns of social interaction","zh":"社会互动的模式"},{"phrase":"social interaction skills","zh":"社会交往技能"},{"phrase":"meaningful social interaction","zh":"有意义的社会交往"},{"phrase":"online social interaction","zh":"线上社会互动"},{"phrase":"social interaction between groups","zh":"群体之间的社会互动"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"social interaction"},{"label":"复数","form":"social interactions"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interact","pos":"v.","zh":"互动；相互作用"},{"word":"interaction","pos":"n.","zh":"互动；相互作用"},{"word":"interactive","pos":"adj.","zh":"互动的；交互式的"},{"word":"interactivity","pos":"n.","zh":"互动性"},{"word":"social","pos":"adj.","zh":"社会的；社交的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Reciprocal action between people","titleCN":"人与人之间相互动作与交流的基本形态","definition":"the general process in which people act toward one another and each response invites a further response","definitionCN":"人们彼此做出行动、每次回应又引出下一次回应的总体过程","example":"Everyday social interaction in the market keeps neighbours informed and ties them together.","exampleCN":"市场里的日常社会互动让邻里互通消息、彼此联结。","why":"interaction joins a prefix meaning 'between' to a verb meaning 'do, drive', so its core is action that passes back and forth rather than action in one direction.","whyCN":"interaction 把表示「在……之间」的前缀加到表示「做、驱动」的动词上，因此核心是来回传递的动作，而非单向动作。"},{"no":"02","title":"A single encounter","titleCN":"一次具体的社交接触","definition":"one bounded occasion of people dealing with each other, with a beginning and an end","definitionCN":"人们彼此打交道的一个有始有终的具体场合","example":"A brief social interaction at the bus stop turned into a job offer.","exampleCN":"公交站一次短暂的社会互动后来变成了一份工作机会。","why":"because the process sense can be counted off into episodes, the phrase also names one occasion, much as a conversation can be counted.","whyCN":"因为过程义可以切分为一个个片段，这个短语也指单次场合，正如谈话可以计数一样。"},{"no":"03","title":"A sustained pattern of dealings","titleCN":"长期维持的往来格局","definition":"regular, repeated contact between the same people or communities over a long period","definitionCN":"同一些人或社群在长时期内规律而反复的接触","example":"The two villages have kept up social interaction through market days for generations.","exampleCN":"这两个村子靠赶集日维持社会交往，已经延续了好几代人。","why":"when single encounters repeat, they harden into a pattern, and the phrase shifts from the event to the standing relation between the parties.","whyCN":"单次接触反复发生便固化为格局，短语于是从「事件」转向各方之间长期存在的关系。"},{"no":"04","title":"Turn-taking in face-to-face talk","titleCN":"面对面交谈中的轮流发言","definition":"the moment-by-moment coordination of speech, gaze and gesture when people talk in person","definitionCN":"人们当面交谈时对说话、目光与手势的即时协调","example":"Group size shapes how much talk each person contributes to a social interaction.","exampleCN":"群体规模会影响每个人在一次社会互动中贡献多少话语。","why":"the micro-sociological sense narrows the general process to the second-by-second mechanics by which turns are offered and taken.","whyCN":"微观社会学义把一般过程收窄到「话轮如何让出与接住」的逐秒机制。"},{"no":"05","title":"Mediated and online contact","titleCN":"经由媒介的线上交往","definition":"interaction carried on through text, platforms or calls rather than physical presence","definitionCN":"通过文字、平台或通话而非身在现场进行的互动","example":"Online social interaction can be as supportive as meeting in person.","exampleCN":"线上社会互动能像当面相见一样给人支持。","why":"the phrase kept its shape while the channel changed: the action still passes between people, even when the space between them is digital.","whyCN":"渠道变了而短语不变形：动作仍在人与人之间传递，即便两人之间的空间是数字的。"},{"no":"06","title":"Shared meanings built in encounter","titleCN":"在往来中共同建构意义","definition":"the sociological view that meaning, identity and social order are produced and repaired in everyday dealings","definitionCN":"社会学观点：意义、身份与秩序在日常往来中被生产与修补","example":"Sociologists study how social interaction builds shared meanings that no single person owns.","exampleCN":"社会学家研究社会互动如何建构出并非任何个人独有的共同意义。","why":"this sense extends the reciprocal-action core into a theory: if every response adjusts to the last, then meanings are jointly made rather than privately held.","whyCN":"这一义项把「相互动作」的核心扩展为理论：若每次回应都调整向前一次，那么意义就是共同造出的，而非私人持有的。"},{"no":"07","title":"Contact across group boundaries","titleCN":"跨越群体界限的接触","definition":"dealings between people of different languages, classes or communities","definitionCN":"不同语言、阶层或社群的人之间的往来","example":"Festivals create social interaction across language boundaries.","exampleCN":"节庆活动造出跨越语言界限的社会互动。","why":"the phrase can be scaled up from two persons to whole groups, because the same back-and-forth pattern appears between collectives.","whyCN":"短语可从两个人放大到整个群体，因为同样的来回模式也出现在集体之间。"},{"no":"08","title":"Coordination and unwritten rules","titleCN":"互动中的协调与不成文规矩","definition":"the subtle cues, timing and politeness that keep an exchange smooth or make it fail","definitionCN":"使交流顺畅或失败的那些细微线索、时机与礼貌","example":"Daily social interaction depends on subtle cues such as timing and gaze.","exampleCN":"社会互动依赖时机与目光这类细微线索。","why":"the prefix 'between' implies two sides that must stay in step, and that requirement for mutual adjustment is what the rules of interaction formalise.","whyCN":"表示「在……之间」的前缀意味着两侧必须同步，而相互调适的要求正是互动规则所形式化的东西。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Social comes from Latin socialis, from socius 'companion, ally'. Interaction comes from inter- 'between' plus agere 'to do, to drive', whose past participle stem act- gives action; the noun therefore means action that runs between two parties. The fixed phrase took shape in twentieth-century sociology. Dates are approximate.","cn":"social 出自拉丁 socialis，源于 socius「同伴、盟友」。interaction 出自表示「在……之间」的拉丁前缀加 agere「做、驱动」，其过去分词提供的词干又构成表示「行动」的名词，因此本义是「在两者之间来回动作」。这个固定短语在二十世纪社会学中定型。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN SOCIUS","en":"Socius 'companion, ally' gave socialis 'of companions, of a community', which English shortened to social.","cn":"socius「同伴、盟友」给出 socialis「同伴的、共同体的」，英语截取为 social。"},{"era":"LATIN AGERE","en":"Agere meant 'to do, to drive, to set in motion'; its past participle actus supplied the stem act- used in nouns of action.","cn":"agere 意为「做、驱动、使动」，其过去分词提供名词中所用的动作词干。"},{"era":"ENGLISH WORD FORMATION","en":"The prefix inter- 'between' combined with the action stem produced a noun for action passing between parties, recorded in English from the early eighteenth century.","cn":"表示「在……之间」的前缀与动作词干结合，造出「在双方之间传递的动作」这一名词，英语自十八世纪初有记录。"},{"era":"ENGLISH INTERACTION","en":"English formed interaction from the prefix and the noun action, and the verb interact was later back-formed from it.","cn":"英语用该前缀与表示「行动」的名词造出表示「互动」的名词，动词形式则是后来由它逆构而成。"},{"era":"SOCIOLOGY PHRASE","en":"Sociology adopted the phrase in the twentieth century to name the basic unit of everyday life, the exchange between two or more people.","cn":"社会学在二十世纪采用这一短语，用来指日常生活的基本单位，即两个或更多人之间的往来。"},{"era":"DIGITAL BROADENING","en":"From the late twentieth century the phrase extended to mediated and online contact without changing its core of reciprocal action.","cn":"二十世纪后期起，这个短语扩展到经由媒介与线上的接触，而其「相互动作」的核心未变。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words from the same action stock that are routinely mixed up; group two holds terms for people dealing with one another, each narrower or wider than the phrase.","cn":"第一组是同出「动作」词族、常被混用的词；第二组是关于人们彼此打交道的术语，各自比这个短语更窄或更宽。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"interaction","ipa":"/ˌɪntərˈækʃən/","tag":"the bare noun","definition":"The noun without the social label; it also covers drugs, particles and systems, so it is broader than the phrase.","definitionCN":"不带「社会」限定的名词，也覆盖药物、粒子与系统，因此比该短语更宽。"},{"word":"interact","ipa":"/ˌɪntərˈækt/","tag":"the verb","definition":"The verb back-formed from the noun; it names the doing, while the phrase names the process as a topic of study.","definitionCN":"由名词逆构而成的动词，指「去做」这个动作；短语则把该过程当作研究对象。"},{"word":"interactive","ipa":"/ˌɪntərˈæktɪv/","tag":"the adjective","definition":"Describes something that responds to a user, such as software; it is a property, not an event between people.","definitionCN":"描述能对使用者作出反应的事物，如软件；它是一种属性，不是人与人之间的事件。"},{"word":"sociability","ipa":"/ˌsəʊsiəˈbɪləti/","tag":"the disposition","definition":"The trait of enjoying company; the phrase names actual dealings, not the taste for them.","definitionCN":"喜欢与人相处的性情；短语指实际的往来，而非对这种往来的喜好。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"communication","ipa":"/ˌkɒmjʊnɪˈkeɪʃən/","tag":"message transfer","definition":"The passing of information or feeling; it can be one-way, while interaction requires response.","definitionCN":"信息或情感的传递；它可以单向，而互动要求有回应。"},{"word":"contact","ipa":"/ˈkɒntækt/","tag":"touch or reach","definition":"The state of being in touch with someone; it may be minimal, whereas interaction implies repeated exchange.","definitionCN":"与某人保持接触的状态；可以极为有限，而互动意味着反复交换。"},{"word":"engagement","ipa":"/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒmənt/","tag":"involvement","definition":"Active involvement with people or a task; it stresses commitment of attention rather than reciprocity.","definitionCN":"对人主动投入；强调注意力的投入，而非相互回应。"},{"word":"intercourse","ipa":"/ˈɪntəkɔːs/","tag":"old formal word","definition":"An older word for dealings between people or nations; it survives mainly in formal and historical writing.","definitionCN":"指人或国家间往来的旧词，如今主要用于正式与历史文本。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the real Latin steps behind both halves, the real derived family, and the real settings in which the phrase is used.","cn":"正常联想取自两半背后真实的拉丁演变、真实的派生词族，以及这个短语被使用的真实场景。"},"normal":[{"en":"socius 'companion' gives social: the parties who face each other.","cn":"socius「同伴」给出 social：彼此面对的那两方。"},{"en":"inter- 'between' plus agere 'do': action running back and forth between two sides.","cn":"表示「在……之间」的前缀加 agere「做」：动作在两侧之间来回跑。"},{"en":"The family runs interact, interaction, interactive, interactivity and social.","cn":"词族包括 interact、interaction、interactive、interactivity 与 social。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the research sense: face-to-face social interaction, patterns of social interaction, online social interaction.","cn":"固定搭配标出研究义：面对面社会互动、社会互动模式、线上社会互动。"},{"en":"The countability is real and useful: one interaction can be counted, but interaction as a process cannot.","cn":"可数性确有其用：一次互动可以计数，而作为过程的互动则不可数。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture two hands passing a cup back and forth across a table.","cn":"想象两只手在桌面上来回传递一只杯子。"},{"en":"Picture two people stepping in time because neither will move before the other.","cn":"想象两个人同步迈步，因为谁也不肯先于对方动。"},{"en":"Picture a conversation where every answer is already shaped by the question before it.","cn":"想象一场谈话，每个回答都已被前一个问题塑过形。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Everyday social interaction in the market keeps neighbours informed and ties them together.","cn":"市场里的日常社会互动让邻里互通消息、彼此联结。"},{"en":"Online social interaction can be as supportive as meeting in person.","cn":"线上社会互动能像当面相见一样给人支持。"},{"en":"The study coded every social interaction in the classroom by speaker turn.","cn":"这项研究按发言轮次对教室里的每一次社会互动进行编码。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「social（同伴）+ interaction（你来我往）」——同伴之间一来一往 → 社会互动","word":"social interaction"},"root":"拉丁 socius「同伴」→ socialis → social；拉丁表示「在……之间」的前缀 + agere「做、驱动」，其过去分词提供的词干构成表示「行动」的名词，合成表示「互动」的名词；二十世纪社会学中与 social 合为固定短语。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses unroll from one motion: action passes between two sides, is cut into single encounters, repeats into a pattern, settles into turn-taking, moves onto screens, becomes the place where meaning is made, scales up to groups, and finally reveals the rules that keep the whole motion smooth.","cn":"八个义项由同一个动作展开：动作在两侧之间传递，被切成单次接触，反复成格局，落成话轮，移上屏幕，成为意义生成之处，再放大到群体，最后显出维持整个过程顺畅的规则。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a cup passing back and forth across a table, neither hand letting go for long.","cn":"核心意象：一只杯子在桌面上来回传递，两只手都不久握不放。"},"chain":["BETWEEN","ACT BACK AND FORTH","ENCOUNTER","ROUTINE EXCHANGE","SHARED MEANING","RULES OF TURN"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THE BASIC MOTION: reciprocal action as a process, and one bounded episode of it.","cn":"基本动作：作为过程的相互动作，以及其中一次有始有终的片段。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"REPETITION AND RHYTHM: repeated episodes harden into a pattern, and the pattern is lived out in turn-taking.","cn":"重复与节奏：反复的片段硬化为格局，而格局就在轮流发言中被实际活出来。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"SCREEN AND MEANING: the same motion moves online, and in sociology it becomes the workshop where shared meaning is built.","cn":"屏幕与意义：同一动作移往线上，并在社会学中成为共同意义被制造的工坊。"},{"senses":"07","en":"SCALE: the pattern repeats between groups, not only between two persons.","cn":"尺度：这一模式不只在两人之间，也在群体之间重现。"},{"senses":"08","en":"RULES: timing, gaze and politeness are the grease that keeps the back-and-forth from jamming.","cn":"规则：时机、目光与礼貌是润滑剂，使来回传递不致卡死。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase splits cleanly: social from a Latin noun for a companion, and interaction from a prefix meaning 'between' plus a verb of doing.","cn":"这个短语可以干净地拆开：social 来自拉丁语表示「同伴」的名词，interaction 来自表示「在……之间」的前缀加一个表示「做」的动词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin socius and socialis stand behind social; Latin inter- and agere, with its participle stem act-, stand behind interaction.","cn":"拉丁 socius 与 socialis 是 social 的来源；拉丁表示「在……之间」的前缀与 agere 及其分词词干是 interaction 的来源。"},"items":[{"word":"soci-","structure":"Latin stem of socius, 'companion, ally'","meaning":"companion; ally; associated person","meaningCN":"同伴；盟友；结伴者","example":"The stem supplies the social half of the phrase.","exampleCN":"这个词干提供短语中「社会」的一半。"},{"word":"-alis","structure":"Latin adjective suffix","meaning":"belonging to, relating to","meaningCN":"属于……的；与……相关的","example":"The suffix turns the noun for a companion into an adjective.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把表示同伴的名词变成形容词。"},{"word":"social","structure":"soci- + -alis","meaning":"of companionship or community","meaningCN":"同伴的；共同体的","example":"Social ties set the stage for the exchange.","exampleCN":"社会关系为这种往来搭好台子。"},{"word":"inter-","structure":"Latin prefix meaning 'between, among'","meaning":"between; mutual","meaningCN":"在……之间；相互","example":"The prefix makes the action run between two sides.","exampleCN":"这个前缀使动作在两侧之间运行。"},{"word":"agere","structure":"Latin verb, third conjugation","meaning":"to do, drive, set in motion","meaningCN":"做；驱动；使动","example":"The verb supplies the acting inside interaction.","exampleCN":"这个动词为 interaction 提供「动作」。"},{"word":"act-","structure":"past participle stem of agere","meaning":"done; performed","meaningCN":"已做的；已施行的","example":"The stem appears in action and in the noun of interaction.","exampleCN":"这个词干出现在表示「行动」的名词中。"},{"word":"-ion","structure":"suffix forming nouns of action or result","meaning":"the act or process of","meaningCN":"……的动作或过程","example":"The suffix yields interaction from the action stem.","exampleCN":"这个后缀由动作词干造出表示「互动」的名词。"},{"word":"interaction","structure":"inter- + act- + -ion","meaning":"action passing between parties","meaningCN":"在双方之间传递的动作","example":"The noun entered English in the early eighteenth century.","exampleCN":"这个名词于十八世纪初进入英语。"},{"word":"-ive","structure":"suffix forming adjectives from verbs","meaning":"tending to, having the nature of","meaningCN":"倾向于……的；具有……性质的","example":"The suffix yields interactive, said of software that answers back.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出表示「能回应使用者」的形容词。"},{"word":"-ity","structure":"suffix forming nouns of quality","meaning":"the quality of being","meaningCN":"……的性质","example":"The suffix yields interactivity, the quality of responding.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出表示「互动性」的名词。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"socius","structure":"socius, socii (m., second declension)","meaning":"companion, ally, associate","meaningCN":"同伴；盟友；合伙人"},{"word":"socialis","structure":"socialis, sociale (adj., third declension)","meaning":"of companions, of a community","meaningCN":"同伴的；共同体的"},{"word":"agere","structure":"agere, egi, actum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to do, drive, set in motion","meaningCN":"做；驱动；使动"},{"word":"actio","structure":"actio, actionis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a doing, action, performance","meaningCN":"行为；行动；施行"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interact","pos":"v.","zh":"互动；相互作用"},{"word":"interaction","pos":"n.","zh":"互动；相互作用"},{"word":"interactive","pos":"adj.","zh":"互动的；交互式的"},{"word":"interactivity","pos":"n.","zh":"互动性"},{"word":"social","pos":"adj.","zh":"社会的；社交的"}]}},{"word":"economics","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈkɒnəmɪks/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈkɑːnəmɪks/","definition_zh":"经济学；（某项活动或部门的）经济核算与成本收益；（历史上的）家政管理","definition_en":"the academic study of how societies produce, distribute and consume goods and services","core_image":"一间账房里，管家把全家的粮食、柴火与钱币分门别类记在册子上，盘算怎样才够一年之用","scene":"旧时一户人家在秋收后清点粮仓、柴垛与钱串，管家把各项开支记进册子，盘算来年如何分配。Modern economics grew out of that household habit of counting what comes in and what goes out.","sceneCN":"前半段画的是秋收后清点家产、记账分粮的旧式家政；句中 economics 指研究生产、分配与消费的现代学科（第 1 个义项：作为一门社会科学的经济学），句意为现代经济学正是从这种盘点收支的家务习惯中长出来的。图中可辨识物件：账册、算盘、粮袋、钱串。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"经济学（不可数，作单数）；经济核算；家政管理（旧义）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"development economics","zh":"发展经济学"},{"phrase":"labour economics","zh":"劳动经济学"},{"phrase":"the economics of publishing","zh":"出版业的经济核算"},{"phrase":"applied economics","zh":"应用经济学"},{"phrase":"mainstream economics","zh":"主流经济学"},{"phrase":"home economics","zh":"家政学"}],"forms":[{"label":"学科名称（不可数）","form":"economics"},{"label":"作主语时的谓语","form":"takes a singular verb"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"economist","pos":"n.","zh":"经济学家"},{"word":"economic","pos":"adj.","zh":"经济的；经济学的"},{"word":"economical","pos":"adj.","zh":"节省的；划算的"},{"word":"economize","pos":"v.","zh":"节约；节省开支"},{"word":"economy","pos":"n.","zh":"经济；经济体；节约"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The academic discipline","titleCN":"作为一门社会科学的经济学","definition":"the systematic study of how goods and services are produced, distributed and consumed","definitionCN":"系统研究商品与服务如何被生产、分配与消费的学问","example":"Modern economics grew out of that household habit of counting what comes in and what goes out.","exampleCN":"现代经济学正是从那种盘点收支的家务习惯中长出来的。","why":"the Greek compound meant household management, and when that management was scaled up to whole societies and given a method, it became a discipline whose name kept the old shape.","whyCN":"这个希腊复合词本指治家之术；当这种管理被放大到整个社会并配上一套方法，它就成了学科，而名称仍保留旧形。"},{"no":"02","title":"A theory or school of thought","titleCN":"某一经济学理论或学派","definition":"a particular body of theory or a school that explains how an economy works","definitionCN":"解释经济如何运转的一套特定理论或学派","example":"Keynesian economics shaped policy after the war.","exampleCN":"凯恩斯主义经济学在战后塑造了政策。","why":"because the discipline contains rival frameworks, the same name is used for a framework, with the school named in front as a modifier.","whyCN":"由于这门学科内部有相互竞争的理论框架，同一个名称也被用来指某一框架，前面加学派名作限定。"},{"no":"03","title":"The financial side of an activity","titleCN":"某项活动背后的财务面与收支逻辑","definition":"the financial considerations that decide whether an activity can pay for itself","definitionCN":"决定一项活动能否自我维持的财务考量","example":"She studied the economics of publishing before launching the imprint.","exampleCN":"她在创办出版品牌之前先研究了出版业的经济核算。","why":"this sense narrows the discipline to one sector: not the whole society, but the money-in and money-out of a single trade.","whyCN":"这一义项把学科窄化到一个部门：不是整个社会，而是单一行业的进账与出账。"},{"no":"04","title":"Cost arithmetic that may not add up","titleCN":"成本收益账，也可能算不过来","definition":"the calculation of costs against returns, often used to say that a plan is not viable","definitionCN":"成本与回报的计算，常用于说明某方案难以为继","example":"The economics of the plan simply do not add up.","exampleCN":"这个方案的经济账根本算不过来。","why":"from the study of allocation came a blunt everyday use: the numbers themselves, which can be added and found short.","whyCN":"从「资源配置的学问」引申出一种直白的日常用法：数字本身可以相加，并发现不够。"},{"no":"05","title":"Economics of a single sector","titleCN":"某一专门领域的经济学分支","definition":"a specialised branch that applies the method to one field, such as health, education or the environment","definitionCN":"把方法应用于卫生、教育或环境等某一领域的专门分支","example":"Health economics asks what a treatment buys for its cost.","exampleCN":"卫生经济学追问一项治疗用其成本换来了什么。","why":"as the discipline matured it split into named branches, each keeping the plural name and taking the field as a prefix.","whyCN":"学科成熟后分裂为有名称的分支，各分支保留这个复数名称，并以领域名作前置限定。"},{"no":"06","title":"The course, degree or profession","titleCN":"作为课程、学位或职业的经济学","definition":"the subject as it is taught, examined and practised rather than the science as such","definitionCN":"被教授、考核与从业的科目，而非作为科学本身的经济学","example":"He read economics at university and later joined a bank.","exampleCN":"他在大学读经济学，后来进了银行。","why":"a discipline is also an institution: departments, degrees and jobs make the name stand for a course of study and a career.","whyCN":"学科也是一种建制：系所、学位与职位使这个名称也代表一门课程与一种职业。"},{"no":"07","title":"Household management, the old sense","titleCN":"旧义：治家之术与家政管理","definition":"the original sense of managing a household's stores, labour and money","definitionCN":"最初指管理一家的储粮、劳力与钱财","example":"In its oldest sense economics meant the good order of a household.","exampleCN":"在其最古老的意义上，economics 指的是一个家的良好秩序。","why":"the Greek word was built from a noun for a house and a verb for distributing, and that domestic craft is still the literal layer beneath the modern science.","whyCN":"这个希腊词由一个表示「家宅」的名词与一个表示「分配」的动词构成，那门家务手艺至今仍是现代科学底下的字面层。"},{"no":"08","title":"The older label political economy","titleCN":"旧称「政治经济学」","definition":"the earlier name for the study of wealth and policy, still used for historical or critical approaches","definitionCN":"研究财富与政策的较早名称，至今仍用于历史性或批判性取径","example":"The study of national wealth kept the older name political economy long before economics took over.","exampleCN":"研究国家财富的学问长期沿用「政治经济学」这个旧名，后来才由经济学取代。","why":"before the shorter name settled in the nineteenth century, the subject was called political economy because it studied the wealth of nations and the laws that shaped it.","whyCN":"在较短的名称于十九世纪定下来之前，这门学问被称为政治经济学，因为它研究国家的财富与塑造财富的法律。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Economics comes from Greek oikonomia, built on oikos 'household' and nemein 'to distribute, to manage', literally 'household management'. The word passed into Latin as a transliteration, oeconomia, then through French into English, where economy came first and economics was formed with the suffix used for disciplines. It became the modern name of the subject in the nineteenth century, when political economy was the older label. Dates are approximate.","cn":"economics 来自希腊 oikonomia，由 oikos「家宅」与 nemein「分配、管理」构成，本义是「治家之术」。该词以转写形式进入拉丁语作 oeconomia，再经法语进入英语；英语先有 economy，后加表示学科的后缀构成 economics。它在十九世纪成为这门学问的现代名称，而此前的通行名称是「政治经济学」。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK OIKOS","en":"Oikos meant 'house, household' and supplied the first element of the compound, pointing to the domestic setting of the whole idea.","cn":"oikos 意为「家宅、家户」，提供复合词的第一部分，指明整个观念的家务场景。"},{"era":"GREEK NEMEIN","en":"Nemein meant 'to distribute, to allot, to manage', so the compound named the management of a household's stores.","cn":"nemein 意为「分配、分派、管理」，因此复合词指对家中储粮与财物的管理。"},{"era":"GREEK OIKONOMIA","en":"Oikonomia meant 'household management' and later extended to the management of any resources, including public ones.","cn":"oikonomia 意为「治家之术」，后扩展到对任何资源的管理，包括公共资源。"},{"era":"LATIN OECONOMIA","en":"Latin took the Greek word as a transliteration, oeconomia, keeping both the spelling shape and the sense of management.","cn":"拉丁语以转写形式接收这个希腊词作 oeconomia，保留了拼写形态与「管理」之义。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ECONOMY","en":"English gained economy through French in the fifteenth century; it meant management of resources and later also thrift, a sense that economy kept for itself.","cn":"英语经法语在十五世纪得到 economy，意为资源管理，后来又指节约；「节约」这一义项留给了 economy。"},{"era":"POLITICAL ECONOMY TO ECONOMICS","en":"From the seventeenth century the study of national wealth was called political economy; in the nineteenth century the shorter name economics was formed with the discipline suffix and gradually replaced the older label.","cn":"十七世纪起，研究国家财富的学问被称为政治经济学；十九世纪用表示学科的后缀造出较短的名称 economics，并逐渐取代旧称。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the family words that are confused daily, especially the two adjectives; group two holds neighbouring names for money and its study, each with a different scope.","cn":"第一组是日常最易混的词族，尤其是两个形容词；第二组是邻近的、关于金钱及其研究的名称，各自范围不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"economy","ipa":"/ɪˈkɒnəmi/","tag":"the system or thrift","definition":"The noun for a country's system of production and trade, or for careful saving; economics is the study of that system.","definitionCN":"指一国的生产与贸易体系，或指节约；economics 是对该体系的研究。"},{"word":"economic","ipa":"/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪk/","tag":"about the economy","definition":"An adjective meaning 'of the economy'; it never means thrifty, which is the job of economical.","definitionCN":"意为「经济的、与经济体有关的」形容词；它从不表示「节省」，后者由 economical 承担。"},{"word":"economical","ipa":"/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪkəl/","tag":"saving money","definition":"An adjective meaning 'using money or resources carefully'; a small economical car, not an economical policy.","definitionCN":"意为「节省钱财或资源的」形容词；可说省油的小车，却不说「节省的政策」。"},{"word":"economist","ipa":"/ɪˈkɒnəmɪst/","tag":"the person","definition":"The noun for a person who studies or practises the subject; it is the human counterpart of the discipline name.","definitionCN":"指研究或从事这门学问的人；是学科名称在人身上的对应词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"political economy","ipa":"/pəˈlɪtɪkəl ɪˈkɒnəmi/","tag":"the older name","definition":"The earlier label for the study of wealth, trade and policy; it survives for historical and critical approaches.","definitionCN":"研究财富、贸易与政策的较早名称；如今见于历史性与批判性取径。"},{"word":"finance","ipa":"/ˈfaɪnæns/","tag":"money and credit","definition":"The management of money, credit and investment; it is one subject matter that economics studies, not the study itself.","definitionCN":"对金钱、信用与投资的管理；它是经济学研究的一块对象，而非研究本身。"},{"word":"accounting","ipa":"/əˈkaʊntɪŋ/","tag":"recording flows","definition":"The practice of recording and reporting money flows; it supplies economics with data rather than theory.","definitionCN":"记录与报告资金流动的实务；它为经济学提供数据，而非理论。"},{"word":"commerce","ipa":"/ˈkɒmɜːs/","tag":"trade itself","definition":"The activity of buying and selling on a large scale; economics is the analytical study of such activity.","definitionCN":"大规模买卖活动本身；经济学是对这类活动的分析性研究。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the real Greek compound, the real Latin step, the real nineteenth-century rename, and the real family of derived words.","cn":"正常联想取自真实的希腊复合词、真实的拉丁环节、真实的十九世纪更名，以及真实的派生词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"oikos 'household' plus nemein 'distribute': the art of running a house.","cn":"oikos「家宅」加 nemein「分配」：经营一个家的技艺。"},{"en":"The Greek word entered Latin as a transliteration, not as a native compound.","cn":"这个希腊词以转写形式进入拉丁语，并非拉丁语本土构词。"},{"en":"The family runs economy, economic, economical, economist and economize.","cn":"词族包括 economy、economic、economical、economist 与 economize。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the branches: development economics, labour economics, health economics, home economics.","cn":"固定搭配标出各分支：发展经济学、劳动经济学、卫生经济学、家政学。"},{"en":"Remember the split: economic is about the economy, economical is about saving money.","cn":"记住分工：economic 关乎经济体，economical 关乎省钱。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a ledger where every sack of grain is entered twice, once as stock and once as promise.","cn":"想象一本账册，每一袋粮都记两遍，一遍作存货，一遍作承诺。"},{"en":"Picture a family deciding in autumn how much to eat and how much to sow.","cn":"想象一家人在秋天决定吃多少、留多少作种子。"},{"en":"Picture a whole nation doing at scale what one household did at its kitchen table.","cn":"想象整个国家在更大尺度上做着一户人家在灶桌边做过的事。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"She gave up a career in law to teach economics at a provincial college.","cn":"她放弃法律职业，到一所地方学院教经济学。"},{"en":"The economics of running a small bookshop leave almost no margin for error.","cn":"经营一家小书店的经济账几乎不留容错余地。"},{"en":"In its oldest sense economics described the orderly management of a household.","cn":"在其最古老的意义上，economics 描述的是对一个家的有序管理。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「eco（家宅）+ nomics（管理之学）」——把家管好的学问 → 经济学","word":"economics"},"root":"希腊 oikos「家宅」+ nemein「分配、管理」→ oikonomia「治家之术」→ 拉丁转写 oeconomia → 法语 → 英语 economy；十九世纪加表示学科的后缀构成 economics，此前通行名称是「政治经济学」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one line: a household is managed, that management grows into the study of how a whole society allocates its resources, then splits into schools, sectors, taught courses and blunt cost sums, while the old domestic sense and the old name political economy remain visible beneath.","cn":"八个义项沿一条线展开：先管理一个家，这种管理长成对整个社会如何配置资源的研究，再分出学派、部门、授课科目与直白的成本账，而旧的家政义与旧称「政治经济学」始终在底下可见。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a steward at a ledger deciding how much grain to use now and how much to keep for the next season.","cn":"核心意象：管家对着账册，决定多少粮食现在用、多少留到下一季。"},"chain":["HOUSEHOLD","MANAGE THE STORE","ALLOCATE RESOURCES","WEALTH OF NATIONS","ACADEMIC SCIENCE","COST ARITHMETIC"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THE DISCIPLINE AND ITS SCHOOLS: one science, and the rival frameworks inside it that also carry the name.","cn":"学科及其学派：一门科学，以及内部同样使用这一名称的竞争性框架。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"MONEY IN AND OUT: the finances of one activity, and the blunt sum that may fail to add up.","cn":"进出之账：单项活动的财务面，以及可能算不过来的直白总和。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"SPECIAL FIELDS AND THE CLASSROOM: named branches, and the course, degree and job that the name also stands for.","cn":"专门领域与课堂：有名称的分支，以及这个名称同时代表的课程、学位与职业。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE ORIGINAL HOUSEHOLD: the domestic craft that lies beneath the whole modern structure.","cn":"最初的家户：支撑整个现代结构的那门家务手艺。"},{"senses":"08","en":"THE OLD NAME: political economy marks the period before the shorter label took over.","cn":"旧名：政治经济学标示较短名称接管之前的那个时期。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The word is a Greek compound transliterated into Latin and then fitted with an English suffix that names disciplines; it is not a native Latin construction.","cn":"这个词是希腊复合词，先被转写进拉丁语，再配上英语中用来命名学科的后缀；它不是拉丁语本土的构词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Greek oikos and nemein build oikonomia; Latin receives it as the transliteration oeconomia, and English draws economy, economic, economical, economist and economics from that stock.","cn":"希腊 oikos 与 nemein 构成 oikonomia；拉丁语以转写形式 oeconomia 接收它，英语再由这一词干引出 economy、economic、economical、economist 与 economics。"},"items":[{"word":"oikos","structure":"Greek noun, second declension","meaning":"house, household, family estate","meaningCN":"家宅；家户；家产","example":"The noun supplies the first half of the Greek compound.","exampleCN":"这个名词提供希腊复合词的前一半。"},{"word":"nemein","structure":"Greek verb","meaning":"to distribute, allot, manage","meaningCN":"分配；分派；管理","example":"The verb supplies the managing half of the compound.","exampleCN":"这个动词提供复合词中「管理」的一半。"},{"word":"oikonomia","structure":"oikos + nemein, Greek compound noun","meaning":"household management","meaningCN":"治家之术；家政管理","example":"The compound later widened to the management of public resources.","exampleCN":"这个复合词后来扩展到公共资源的管理。"},{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"Latin transliteration of the Greek noun","meaning":"management of a household or estate","meaningCN":"家户或产业的管理","example":"Latin kept the Greek shape rather than coining a native compound.","exampleCN":"拉丁语保留希腊词形，而非另造本土复合词。"},{"word":"economy","structure":"English noun from the Latin stock through French","meaning":"management of resources; the system of production; thrift","meaningCN":"资源管理；生产体系；节约","example":"Economy took the thrift sense, leaving economics for the science.","exampleCN":"economy 承担了「节约」义，把「科学」义留给 economics。"},{"word":"-ic","structure":"suffix forming adjectives","meaning":"relating to","meaningCN":"与……相关的","example":"The suffix yields economic, relating to the economy.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出表示「与经济体相关」的形容词。"},{"word":"-ical","structure":"compound adjective suffix","meaning":"having the nature of, practising","meaningCN":"具有……性质的；从事……的","example":"The suffix yields economical, meaning careful with money.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出表示「用钱节省」的形容词。"},{"word":"-ics","structure":"suffix forming names of disciplines","meaning":"the study or science of","meaningCN":"……学；……研究","example":"The suffix turned the subject into a named discipline in the nineteenth century.","exampleCN":"这个后缀在十九世纪把这门学问变成一个有名称的学科。"},{"word":"-ist","structure":"suffix forming agent nouns","meaning":"one who studies or practises","meaningCN":"研究或从事……的人","example":"The suffix yields economist, a person who practises the subject.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出表示「经济学家」的名词。"},{"word":"-ize","structure":"suffix forming verbs","meaning":"to make, to act in a given way","meaningCN":"使……化；按某种方式行事","example":"The suffix yields economize, to cut down on spending.","exampleCN":"这个后缀造出表示「节省开支」的动词。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"oeconomia, oeconomiae (f., first declension)","meaning":"household management, administration","meaningCN":"家政管理；经营管理"},{"word":"oeconomus","structure":"oeconomus, oeconomi (m., second declension)","meaning":"steward, manager of an estate","meaningCN":"管家；产业管理者"},{"word":"oeconomicus","structure":"oeconomicus, oeconomica, oeconomicum (adj.)","meaning":"of household management","meaningCN":"家政管理的；经营上的"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"economist","pos":"n.","zh":"经济学家"},{"word":"economic","pos":"adj.","zh":"经济的；经济学的"},{"word":"economical","pos":"adj.","zh":"节省的；划算的"},{"word":"economize","pos":"v.","zh":"节约；节省开支"},{"word":"economy","pos":"n.","zh":"经济；经济体；节约"}]}},{"word":"economist","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈkɒnəmɪst/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈkɑːnəmɪst/","definition_zh":"经济学家；经济学者；旧义：治家者、善于理财的人","definition_en":"a person who studies how economies work, or who is professionally trained to analyse production, trade and the use of resources","core_image":"一个人站在堆满统计年鉴的桌前，用粉笔把一整排数字连成一条向右上走的趋势线","scene":"一份关于物价与就业的长篇报告在议会传阅，顾问们轮流在页边写下自己的判断。The economist told the committee that wage growth had outpaced prices for three straight quarters.","sceneCN":"议会传阅一份关于物价与就业的长篇报告，顾问轮流在页边写下判断；句中的 economist 指「以经济分析为专业的人」（第 1 个义项：研究经济体系如何运行的人）。图中可辨识物件：统计年鉴、粉笔、趋势线、议会长桌。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"经济学家；经济分析者"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"chief economist","zh":"首席经济学家"},{"phrase":"leading economist","zh":"知名经济学家"},{"phrase":"labour economist","zh":"劳动经济学家"},{"phrase":"agricultural economist","zh":"农业经济学家"},{"phrase":"economists' forecast","zh":"经济学家的预测"},{"phrase":"classical economist","zh":"古典经济学家"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"economists"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"economics","pos":"n.","zh":"经济学；经济状况"},{"word":"economic","pos":"adj.","zh":"经济的；经济学的"},{"word":"economical","pos":"adj.","zh":"节约的；省钱的"},{"word":"economize","pos":"v.","zh":"节约；节省开支"},{"word":"econometrics","pos":"n.","zh":"计量经济学"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The academic researcher","titleCN":"以经济为研究对象的学者","definition":"a researcher who studies how economies work and publishes work on the subject","definitionCN":"研究经济体系如何运行、并就此发表成果的研究者","example":"As an economist she studies why young firms fail so often.","exampleCN":"作为经济学家，她研究年轻企业为何如此频繁地倒闭。","why":"The person suffix marks someone occupied with the field named by the base, and that base first named household management and later the whole economy.","whyCN":"表示人的后缀标记「从事基础词所指领域的人」，而这个词根先指治家，后指整个经济。"},{"no":"02","title":"The professional forecaster","titleCN":"职业预测者","definition":"a person paid to forecast output, inflation or employment for a bank, a government or a firm","definitionCN":"受雇于银行、政府或企业，负责预测产出、通胀或就业的人","example":"The bank's economist expects inflation to fall below three percent.","exampleCN":"该银行的经济学家预计通胀将降到百分之三以下。","why":"Once the discipline acquired predictive tools, the same label covered the people paid to turn those tools into forecasts.","whyCN":"当这门学科有了预测工具，同一个称呼便也覆盖那些受雇把工具变成预测的人。"},{"no":"03","title":"The specialist in a branch","titleCN":"某一分支的专家","definition":"someone working inside a particular branch such as labour, agriculture or development","definitionCN":"在劳动、农业或发展等某一具体分支内工作的人","example":"A labour economist studies how wages respond to migration.","exampleCN":"劳动经济学家研究工资如何随人口迁移而变化。","why":"The suffix names an occupant of a field, and a field can be narrowed to one branch without changing the label.","whyCN":"这个后缀指某一领域的从业者，而领域可以收窄到某个分支，称呼本身不必改变。"},{"no":"04","title":"The policy adviser","titleCN":"政策顾问","definition":"a person who translates economic analysis into advice for ministers, central banks or regulators","definitionCN":"把经济分析转化为给部长、央行或监管机构建议的人","example":"The economist advised the ministry to phase in the tax over two years.","exampleCN":"这位经济学家建议该部在两年内分阶段引入这项税。","why":"Advice is the applied edge of the discipline, so the person who supplies it is still called by the discipline's name.","whyCN":"建议是这门学科最靠近应用的一端，提供建议的人便仍以学科之名相称。"},{"no":"05","title":"The public commentator","titleCN":"面向公众的解说者","definition":"a writer or broadcaster who explains economic events to a general audience","definitionCN":"向普通读者或听众解释经济事件的写作者或广播者","example":"The newspaper's economist explained the rate rise in plain language.","exampleCN":"该报的经济学家用平实的语言解释了这次加息。","why":"The label can name anyone who speaks from the discipline in public, not only those who research it.","whyCN":"这个称呼可以指任何在公共场合以这门学科发言的人，而不只限于做研究的人。"},{"no":"06","title":"Historical household manager","titleCN":"旧义：治家者","definition":"in earlier use, a person who managed a household and its property","definitionCN":"较早用法中指管理家宅及其财产的人","example":"In seventeenth-century usage an economist was the steward of a great house.","exampleCN":"在十七世纪的用法里，经济学家是一座大宅的管家。","why":"The Greek base named household management, so the earliest English users applied the person suffix to the one who ran a household.","whyCN":"希腊词根本指治家，因此早期英语使用者把这个表示人的后缀加在主持家宅事务的人身上。"},{"no":"07","title":"Historical thrifty person","titleCN":"旧义：善于理财节俭的人","definition":"in earlier use, a person skilled in saving and careful with money","definitionCN":"较早用法中指善于储蓄、用钱谨慎的人","example":"Her grandfather was called an economist for wasting nothing.","exampleCN":"她的祖父因从不浪费而被称作善于理财的人。","why":"Household management included frugality, and the label could describe anyone who practised it in daily life.","whyCN":"治家包含节俭，于是这个称呼也能描述在日常生活中实践节俭的任何人。"},{"no":"08","title":"Member of a school of thought","titleCN":"某一学派的经济学家","definition":"a thinker identified with a particular tradition such as the classical or Keynesian school","definitionCN":"归属于古典、凯恩斯等某一思想传统的思想者","example":"The classical economist argued that prices would adjust on their own.","exampleCN":"这位古典经济学家主张价格会自行调整。","why":"A discipline organised into rival traditions lets the person label attach to the followers of each tradition.","whyCN":"一门学科若分成相互竞争的传统，表示人的称呼便能附着于各传统的追随者。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Economist joins the economy family with the person suffix -ist. Economy came from Greek oikonomia, itself oikos 'household' plus nemein 'to distribute or manage', and passed through Latin oeconomia into English. The suffix came from Greek -istes through Latin -ista and French -iste. The word is not a Latin root with a suffix glued on: its base is Greek in origin and reached English through Latin transcription, and the person suffix arrived by way of Latin and French. The word is generally thought to have appeared in the seventeenth century.","cn":"这个词由表示经济的词干加上一个表示人的后缀构成，并不是在拉丁词根上直接加后缀：词干源自希腊 oikonomia（由 oikos「家宅」与 nemein「分配、管理」合成），经拉丁 oeconomia 转写进入英语；表示人的后缀则出自希腊 -istes，经拉丁 -ista 与法语 -iste 传来。一般认为这个词在十七世纪出现。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK OIKOS","en":"Oikos meant a house, a household and the property attached to it, the basic unit of ancient domestic life.","cn":"oikos 指房屋、家宅及附属于它的财产，是古代家庭生活的基本单位。"},{"era":"GREEK OIKONOMIA","en":"Oikonomia joined oikos with nemein 'to distribute, manage', naming the art of running a household, including its slaves, stores and accounts.","cn":"oikonomia 把 oikos 与表示「分配、管理」的 nemein 结合，指经营家宅的技艺，包括人丁、仓储与账目。"},{"era":"LATIN OECONOMIA","en":"Latin took the Greek word as oeconomia and widened it from household management to the management of a state or an estate.","cn":"拉丁语借入该词作 oeconomia，并把范围从治家扩大到治理国家或庄园。"},{"era":"FRENCH ECONOMISTE","en":"French économiste named a writer on economic matters in the seventeenth century, and English took the pattern of the word from French.","cn":"十七世纪法语 économiste 指撰写经济事务的作者，英语沿用了这个词的构词方式。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ECONOMIST","en":"English economist is generally thought to have arisen in the seventeenth century, when it first meant a household manager or a thrifty person rather than a university researcher.","cn":"一般认为英语 economist 在十七世纪出现，最初指治家者或节俭的人，而不是大学研究者。"},{"era":"MODERN DISCIPLINE","en":"After political economy was shortened to economics in the nineteenth century, economist settled into its modern sense of a professional analyst of the economy.","cn":"十九世纪政治经济学缩称为经济学之后，economist 固定为对经济作专业分析的人这一现代含义。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group gathers words from the same economy family whose word class or meaning is often confused with the person noun; the near-meaning group gathers analysts who work with numbers but from different angles.","cn":"形近组收的是同一经济词族中词性或含义易与「指人名词」混淆的词；近义组收的是同样与数字打交道的分析者，但角度不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"economy","ipa":"/ɪˈkɒnəmi/","tag":"the system itself","definition":"The system of production and trade in a country or region; it is the base noun, not the person, and it is not a description of a job.","definitionCN":"指一国或一地区的生产与贸易体系；它是基础名词，不指人，也不描述职业。"},{"word":"economics","ipa":"/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪks/","tag":"the discipline","definition":"The name of the academic subject; it looks like a plural but names one field and never one person.","definitionCN":"学科名称；形式像复数，却指一个领域，绝不指某个人。"},{"word":"economic","ipa":"/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪk/","tag":"adjective of the system","definition":"An adjective describing the economy, as in economic growth; unlike the person noun it cannot be the subject of a sentence about a job.","definitionCN":"描述经济的形容词，如经济增长；与指人的名词不同，它不能作「从事某职业」的主语。"},{"word":"economical","ipa":"/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪkəl/","tag":"thrifty or good value","definition":"Means saving money or cheap to run; it is close in shape but has nothing to do with the profession.","definitionCN":"意为省钱、运行成本低；外形相近，却与这门职业无关。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"econometrician","ipa":"/ɪˌkɒnəˈmetrɪʃən/","tag":"statistical testing","definition":"An economist who specialises in statistical methods; the broader label also covers those who never run a regression.","definitionCN":"专精统计方法的经济学家；范围更广的称呼也涵盖从不做回归分析的人。"},{"word":"financial analyst","ipa":"/faɪˈnænʃəl ˈænəlɪst/","tag":"markets and firms","definition":"Someone who values shares, bonds or companies; the work is market-facing rather than a study of the whole economy.","definitionCN":"评估股票、债券或公司价值的人；其工作面向市场，而非研究整个经济。"},{"word":"statistician","ipa":"/stəˈtɪstɪʃən/","tag":"data, not theory","definition":"A person trained in collecting and interpreting data; the economist adds a body of theory about incentives and markets.","definitionCN":"受训于收集与解读数据的人；经济学家则另有关于激励与市场的理论体系。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations here follow the real Greek household root, the Latin transfer, the person suffix and the fixed phrases the word actually keeps.","cn":"正常联想取自这个词真实的希腊家宅词根、拉丁转写、表示人的后缀，以及它实际保留的固定搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"Oikos 'household' plus nemein 'distribute' gives oikonomia, the art of managing a house and its stores.","cn":"oikos「家宅」加 nemein「分配」构成 oikonomia，即管理家宅与仓储的技艺。"},{"en":"Latin oeconomia widened the household art into the management of a state or estate.","cn":"拉丁 oeconomia 把治家之术扩大到治理国家或庄园。"},{"en":"The person suffix -ist, from Greek -istes, marks someone occupied with a field, as in physicist or biologist.","cn":"表示人的后缀出自希腊 -istes，标记从事某领域的人，如物理学家或生物学家。"},{"en":"The subject was long called political economy before it was shortened to economics.","cn":"这门学科长期称作政治经济学，后来才缩称为经济学。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the professional sense: chief economist, labour economist, economists' forecast.","cn":"固定搭配标出职业义：首席经济学家、劳动经济学家、经济学家的预测。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a single line on a large graph that stands for the mood of millions of households.","cn":"想象一张大图上的单独一条线，它代表着千百万家庭的处境。"},{"en":"Picture a committee table where one person is asked to say what all those numbers will do next year.","cn":"想象一张委员会长桌，其中一人被要求说出这些数字明年会怎样。"},{"en":"Picture a candlelit ledger in an old house, kept by the one person trusted to balance it.","cn":"想象旧宅里一本烛光下的账簿，由唯一被信任能把它做平的人掌管。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The economist's model predicts a slowdown in household spending next year.","cn":"这位经济学家的模型预测明年家庭支出将放缓。"},{"en":"Government economists were divided over the size of the stimulus package.","cn":"政府的经济学家对刺激方案的规模意见分歧。"},{"en":"In the older sense, an economist was simply someone who kept a household in order.","cn":"在较早的含义里，经济学家不过是把家宅打理得井井有条的人。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"谐音「一抠呢米斯特」：一位姓米斯特的先生凡事都要一抠到底，于是被称作经济学家。","word":"economist"},"root":"希腊 oikos「家宅」+ nemein「分配、管理」→ 希腊 oikonomia「治家之术」→ 拉丁 oeconomia（由家宅扩大到国家）→ 法语 économiste → 英语 economist，再加希腊来源、经拉丁与法语传来的表示人的后缀；一般认为十七世纪出现，最初指治家者或节俭者。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one line: a household is managed, that art is widened to the state, the manager becomes a researcher, and the researcher splits into forecaster, branch specialist, adviser, commentator, school member and finally the older steward and thrifty figure.","cn":"八个义项沿一条线展开：先有家宅的经营，这门技艺再扩大到国家，治家者变为研究者，研究者又分化为预测者、分支专家、顾问、解说者、学派成员，最后回到较早的管家与节俭者形象。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one person at a desk turning a household ledger into a national account.","cn":"核心意象：一个人坐在桌前，把一本家宅账簿换成一本国民账户。"},"chain":["HOUSEHOLD","MANAGEMENT","WEALTH","ECONOMY","DISCIPLINE","EXPERT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"RESEARCH AND FORECAST: the academic who explains the economy and the professional who is paid to say what comes next.","cn":"研究与预测：解释经济的学者，以及受雇判断下一步走势的职业人士。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"NARROWING AND APPLYING: work inside one branch, then carry that work into advice for ministers and regulators.","cn":"收窄与应用：先在某一分支内做研究，再把研究带进给部长与监管者的建议。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"PUBLIC VOICE AND OLD STEWARD: the commentator who speaks to readers, and the earlier steward who ran a great house.","cn":"公共言说与旧日管家：面向读者的解说者，以及更早掌管大宅的管家。"},{"senses":"07","en":"FRUGALITY: the older figure who saved carefully, the domestic virtue inside the household art.","cn":"节俭：较早那位精打细算的人，是治家之术里的家庭美德。"},{"senses":"08","en":"SCHOOLS: the thinker placed inside a tradition, where the discipline becomes an identity.","cn":"学派：被归入某一传统的思想者，此时学科变成一种身份。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The word reads in three parts: a Greek household root, a Latin transfer of that root, and a Greek-origin person suffix that reached English through Latin and French.","cn":"这个词可分三段读：希腊的家宅词根、该词根的拉丁转写，以及一个经拉丁与法语进入英语、源自希腊的表示人的后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin oeconomia and oeconomus are the forms that carried the household idea into medieval and modern European languages.","cn":"拉丁 oeconomia 与 oeconomus 是把治家观念带入中世纪及现代欧洲语言的形式。"},"items":[{"word":"-ist","structure":"suffix forming person nouns from fields or activities","meaning":"one who practises or studies a field","meaningCN":"表示从事或研究某一领域的人","example":"The suffix turns economics into economist.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把经济学变成经济学家。"},{"word":"oikos","structure":"Greek noun, second declension","meaning":"house, household, family property","meaningCN":"房屋；家宅；家庭财产","example":"Oikos is the first element of the compound.","exampleCN":"oikos 是这个复合词的第一部分。"},{"word":"nemein","structure":"Greek verb","meaning":"to distribute, to manage, to allot","meaningCN":"分配；管理；分派","example":"Nemein supplies the managing half of the compound.","exampleCN":"nemein 提供这个复合词中「管理」的一半。"},{"word":"oikonomia","structure":"oikos + nemein, Greek compound noun","meaning":"household management, later public administration","meaningCN":"治家之术，后指公共管理","example":"Oikonomia named the art before it named a science.","exampleCN":"oikonomia 先指一门技艺，后来才指一门科学。"},{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"Latin noun, first declension, from Greek","meaning":"management of a household or a state","meaningCN":"对家宅或国家的管理","example":"Oeconomia entered medieval Latin learning.","exampleCN":"oeconomia 进入中世纪拉丁学术。"},{"word":"oeconomus","structure":"Latin noun, second declension, from Greek oikonomos","meaning":"steward, household manager","meaningCN":"管家；治家者","example":"An oeconomus kept the accounts of a great estate.","exampleCN":"管家负责一座大庄园的账目。"},{"word":"economic","structure":"economy + -ic, adjective suffix","meaning":"relating to the economy","meaningCN":"与经济相关的","example":"Economic growth is measured in total output.","exampleCN":"经济增长以总产出来衡量。"},{"word":"economics","structure":"economy + -ics, suffix naming a discipline","meaning":"the academic study of production, trade and resources","meaningCN":"研究生产、贸易与资源的学科","example":"Economics became a university subject in the nineteenth century.","exampleCN":"经济学在十九世纪成为大学科目。"},{"word":"economist","structure":"the oikonomia line + -ist, person suffix","meaning":"one who studies or advises on the economy","meaningCN":"研究经济或就经济提供建议的人","example":"Economist first meant a household manager.","exampleCN":"economist 最初指治家者。"},{"word":"econometrics","structure":"economics + -metrics, suffix of measurement","meaning":"statistical measurement applied to economic data","meaningCN":"把统计测量用于经济数据","example":"Econometrics tests theory against observed data.","exampleCN":"计量经济学用观测数据检验理论。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"oeconomia, oeconomiae (f., first declension)","meaning":"household or state management","meaningCN":"家宅或国家的管理"},{"word":"oeconomicus","structure":"oeconomicus, oeconomica, oeconomicum (adj., first and second declension)","meaning":"of household management","meaningCN":"治家的；家政的"},{"word":"oeconomus","structure":"oeconomus, oeconomi (m., second declension)","meaning":"steward, manager of an estate","meaningCN":"管家；庄园管理者"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"economics","pos":"n.","zh":"经济学"},{"word":"economic","pos":"adj.","zh":"经济的"},{"word":"economical","pos":"adj.","zh":"节约的"},{"word":"economize","pos":"v.","zh":"节约；节省"},{"word":"econometrics","pos":"n.","zh":"计量经济学"}]}},{"word":"macroeconomics","ipa_uk":"/ˌmækrəʊˌiːkəˈnɒmɪks/","ipa_us":"/ˌmækroʊˌiːkəˈnɑːmɪks/","definition_zh":"宏观经济学；研究整体经济的产出、就业、物价与增长的经济学分支","definition_en":"the branch of economics that studies the economy as a whole, especially total output, employment, price levels and growth","core_image":"一张从高空拍下的城市照片，港口、工厂与公路被压缩成几条并排的总量曲线","scene":"央行与财政部门的官员围坐一桌，争论的是全国产出、失业与物价的整体走向。Macroeconomics asks why total output and employment rise and fall together over the business cycle.","sceneCN":"央行与财政官员围坐一桌，争论全国产出、失业与物价的整体走向；句中的 macroeconomics 指「把整个经济当作一个总量单位来研究的分支」（第 1 个义项：研究整体经济运行的学科）。图中可辨识物件：总量曲线、城市航拍图、会议桌、报表。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"宏观经济学；总量经济学"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"macroeconomics textbook","zh":"宏观经济学教材"},{"phrase":"macroeconomics course","zh":"宏观经济学课程"},{"phrase":"intermediate macroeconomics","zh":"中级宏观经济学"},{"phrase":"applied macroeconomics","zh":"应用宏观经济学"},{"phrase":"modern macroeconomics","zh":"现代宏观经济学"},{"phrase":"principles of macroeconomics","zh":"宏观经济学原理"}],"forms":[{"label":"不可数","form":"uncountable"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"macroeconomic","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观经济的；总量经济的"},{"word":"macroeconomist","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观经济学家"},{"word":"macroeconometrics","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观计量经济学"},{"word":"macroeconometric","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观计量经济学的"},{"word":"macroeconomy","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观经济体；整体经济"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The branch studying the whole economy","titleCN":"研究整体经济的学科分支","definition":"the division of economics that treats the economy as a single system rather than as separate markets","definitionCN":"把经济当作一个单一体系、而非若干独立市场来研究的经济学分支","example":"Macroeconomics examines how investment and consumption move together.","exampleCN":"宏观经济学考察投资与消费如何同步变动。","why":"The prefix marks scale, and the base names the discipline, so the compound literally means the study of the economy at its largest scale.","whyCN":"前缀标记尺度，基础词指学科，因此这个复合词字面上就是「在最大尺度上研究经济」。"},{"no":"02","title":"The university subject","titleCN":"大学课程与教材科目","definition":"the name of a standard course and textbook in a degree programme","definitionCN":"学位课程中一门标准课程与教材的名称","example":"She took macroeconomics before moving on to monetary policy.","exampleCN":"她先修宏观经济学，之后才转向货币政策。","why":"A discipline that is taught in set courses turns its branch names into subject titles, and this one is among the earliest in any programme.","whyCN":"学科若按固定课程讲授，分支之名便成为科目名称，而这个分支是任何培养方案里最早的科目之一。"},{"no":"03","title":"The aggregate viewpoint","titleCN":"总量视角（与微观相对）","definition":"the habit of looking at totals and averages instead of at individual buyers and sellers","definitionCN":"看总量与平均值、而非单个买卖双方的习惯视角","example":"Macroeconomics smooths away individual choices to show the total picture.","exampleCN":"宏观经济学把个体选择抹平，以呈现总体图景。","why":"The word's scale prefix sets it against the small-scale branch, so using it signals that the unit of analysis is a total, not a person.","whyCN":"这个词表示尺度的前缀使它与小尺度分支相对，因此使用它就表明分析单位是总量而非个人。"},{"no":"04","title":"Analysis for fiscal and monetary policy","titleCN":"为财政与货币政策服务的分析","definition":"the applied use of totals to decide on spending, taxation and interest rates","definitionCN":"把总量分析用于决定支出、税收与利率的应用做法","example":"The treasury relied on macroeconomics to size the stimulus.","exampleCN":"财政部依靠宏观经济学来确定刺激方案的规模。","why":"Governments act on totals, so the branch that supplies totals became the natural language of budget and rate decisions.","whyCN":"政府依据总量行动，因此提供总量的分支自然成为预算与利率决策的语言。"},{"no":"05","title":"Short-run fluctuation","titleCN":"短期波动与商业周期","definition":"the study of booms and recessions over months and a few years","definitionCN":"研究数月到数年之间的繁荣与衰退","example":"Macroeconomics explains why recessions spread from one sector to all.","exampleCN":"宏观经济学解释衰退为何从一个部门扩散到所有部门。","why":"When totals are measured quarterly, their short swings become visible, and the branch took that rhythm as one of its central problems.","whyCN":"总量一旦按季度计量，短期摆动便显现出来，这个分支便把这种节奏当作核心问题之一。"},{"no":"06","title":"Long-run growth","titleCN":"长期增长与生产率","definition":"the study of why output per person rises over decades","definitionCN":"研究数十年间人均产出为何提高","example":"Macroeconomics now devotes much of its attention to productivity growth.","exampleCN":"宏观经济学如今把大量注意力放在生产率增长上。","why":"The same totals, viewed across decades rather than quarters, raise the separate question of growth, which the branch treats as its long horizon.","whyCN":"同样一些总量若按数十年而非季度来看，便提出增长这一独立问题，这个分支把它当作长期视野。"},{"no":"07","title":"The open economy","titleCN":"开放经济中的宏观分析","definition":"the study of totals when trade, exchange rates and capital cross borders","definitionCN":"在贸易、汇率与资本跨越国界时研究总量","example":"Macroeconomics of the open economy tracks the trade balance alongside growth.","exampleCN":"开放经济的宏观经济学把贸易差额与增长一并追踪。","why":"Once national totals are measured against other countries, the branch must add exchange rates and cross-border flows to its core accounts.","whyCN":"一旦国民总量要与他国比较，这个分支就必须在核心核算中加入汇率与跨境流动。"},{"no":"08","title":"Loose talk about the big picture","titleCN":"口语引申：从整体层面看问题","definition":"in informal use, the habit of judging a local event by its effect on the whole system","definitionCN":"非正式用法中指以整体体系所受影响来判断局部事件的习惯","example":"Treating the plant closure as macroeconomics, the mayor asked what it did to the whole town.","exampleCN":"市长把工厂关闭当作宏观层面的问题，追问它给整个城镇带来了什么。","why":"Because the term's core is the whole rather than the part, it can be borrowed for any decision that must be judged at the level of the system.","whyCN":"因为这个术语的核心是整体而非局部，它可以被借用来描述任何必须在体系层面判断的决定。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Macroeconomics joins a Greek prefix meaning 'long, large' to economics, which descends from Greek oikonomia through Latin oeconomia. The compound and its adjective are generally thought to have risen in the 1930s with national income accounting and Keynesian aggregate analysis; the exact year of first use is uncertain.","cn":"这个词把一个表示「长的、大的」的希腊前缀加在经济学科之名上，而后者经拉丁 oeconomia 源自希腊 oikonomia。一般认为这个复合词及其形容词形式在二十世纪三十年代随国民收入核算与凯恩斯式总量分析兴起；具体首见年份来源不确定。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK MAKROS","en":"Makros meant 'long, large, far-reaching' and was widely used in compounds for things on a great scale.","cn":"makros 意为「长的、大的、范围广的」，广泛用于表示大尺度的复合词。"},{"era":"GREEK OIKONOMIA","en":"Oikonomia, from oikos 'household' and nemein 'to manage', named the running of a household and later of public affairs.","cn":"oikonomia 由 oikos「家宅」与 nemein「管理」构成，指经营家宅，后也指管理公共事务。"},{"era":"LATIN OECONOMIA","en":"Latin oeconomia carried the word into European learned usage, where it covered the management of an estate or a state.","cn":"拉丁 oeconomia 把这个词带入欧洲学术用语，其范围包括庄园或国家的管理。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ECONOMICS","en":"In the nineteenth century political economy was shortened to economics, giving the base that the large-scale prefix would later attach to.","cn":"十九世纪政治经济学缩称为经济学，为后来加接大尺度前缀提供了基础词。"},{"era":"MACROECONOMIC","en":"The adjective is generally thought to have appeared in the 1930s, when economists needed a word for analysis of totals rather than of single markets.","cn":"一般认为这个形容词在二十世纪三十年代出现，当时经济学家需要为「分析总量而非单个市场」造一个词。"},{"era":"MACROECONOMICS","en":"The noun settled as the name of a branch in the same decade, alongside national income accounts and aggregate demand analysis; the first recorded year is uncertain.","cn":"同一时期，这个名词固定为一个分支的名称，与国民收入核算和总需求分析相伴；最早见于记载的年份不确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group holds forms from the same compound that differ in word class or scale; the near-meaning group holds neighbouring fields that also work with totals but answer different questions.","cn":"形近组收的是同一复合词中词性或尺度不同的形式；近义组收的是同样处理总量、但回答不同问题的邻近领域。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"macroeconomic","ipa":"/ˌmækrəʊiːkəˈnɒmɪk/","tag":"the adjective","definition":"Describes totals or the branch itself, as in macroeconomic policy; it cannot stand alone as the name of a course.","definitionCN":"描述总量或该分支本身，如宏观经济政策；它不能单独用作课程名称。"},{"word":"microeconomics","ipa":"/ˌmaɪkrəʊiːˈkɒnəmɪks/","tag":"the opposite branch","definition":"Studies single buyers, sellers and markets; the two words share their ending and are constantly paired and confused.","definitionCN":"研究单个买方、卖方与市场；两词词尾相同，常被成对使用也常被混淆。"},{"word":"economics","ipa":"/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪks/","tag":"the parent discipline","definition":"The whole subject, of which the large-scale branch is one part; it is broader, not a synonym.","definitionCN":"整个学科，大尺度分支只是其中一部分；它范围更广，并非同义词。"},{"word":"macroeconomy","ipa":"/ˌmækrəʊɪˈkɒnəmi/","tag":"the object studied","definition":"Names the whole economy as an object; it is what the branch studies, not the study itself.","definitionCN":"指作为研究对象的整体经济；它是该分支研究的对象，而不是研究本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"national income analysis","ipa":"/ˈnæʃənəl ˈɪnkʌm əˈnæləsɪs/","tag":"the accounts","definition":"The measurement of total output, income and spending; it supplies the data that the branch interprets.","definitionCN":"对总产出、总收入与总支出的计量；它提供该分支所解读的数据。"},{"word":"business cycle theory","ipa":"/ˈbɪznəs ˈsaɪkəl ˈθɪəri/","tag":"the short swings","definition":"A narrower study of expansions and contractions; it is one part of the larger branch, not the whole of it.","definitionCN":"对扩张与收缩的更窄研究；它是该分支的一部分，而非全部。"},{"word":"monetary economics","ipa":"/ˈmʌnɪtəri ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪks/","tag":"money and rates","definition":"Studies money, banking and interest rates; it overlaps with the branch but centres on one mechanism.","definitionCN":"研究货币、银行与利率；它与该分支重叠，却以一个机制为中心。"},{"word":"growth theory","ipa":"/ɡrəʊθ ˈθɪəri/","tag":"the long horizon","definition":"Explains why output per person rises over decades; it is the long-run wing of the branch.","definitionCN":"解释数十年间人均产出为何提高；它是该分支的长期一翼。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations here use the real Greek scale prefix, the real household root behind economics, and the real institutional setting in which the term grew up.","cn":"正常联想取自表示尺度的真实希腊前缀、经济学背后真实的治家词根，以及这个术语成长的真实制度背景。"},"normal":[{"en":"Makros means long or large, so the prefix marks the scale of the whole economy.","cn":"makros 意为长或大，因此这个前缀标记的是整个经济的尺度。"},{"en":"Oikonomia, household management, is the same root that gave economics.","cn":"oikonomia 即治家之术，正是给经济学提供词根的那个词。"},{"en":"The field grew with national income accounting, which first made totals measurable.","cn":"这门分支随国民收入核算成长，后者第一次让总量可以被计量。"},{"en":"The pair with microeconomics is built into the word: large scale against small scale.","cn":"它与微观经济学的配对就写在这个词里：大尺度对小尺度。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the teaching sense: intermediate macroeconomics, applied macroeconomics.","cn":"固定搭配标出教学义：中级宏观经济学、应用宏观经济学。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture an aerial photograph in which a whole city becomes a few clean lines.","cn":"想象一张航拍照片，整座城市被压缩成几条干净的线。"},{"en":"Picture three curves, output, jobs and prices, drawn on one board and read together.","cn":"想象一块板子上画着产出、就业与物价三条曲线，被一起解读。"},{"en":"Picture one lever in a control room that is said to move every household at once.","cn":"想象控制室里的一根拉杆，据说能同时牵动每一个家庭。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Macroeconomics is usually taught after students have learned how single markets work.","cn":"宏观经济学通常在学生了解单个市场如何运行之后才讲授。"},{"en":"The central bank's forecasts are grounded in macroeconomics rather than in firm-level data.","cn":"央行的预测依据的是宏观经济学，而不是企业层面的数据。"},{"en":"A recession is the kind of event that macroeconomics was invented to explain.","cn":"衰退正是宏观经济学被创立出来要解释的那类事件。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"谐音「麦克罗伊科诺米克斯」：麦克罗先生只翻全国的厚账本，看的是整体的大数，不是一家小店的流水。","word":"macroeconomics"},"root":"希腊 makros「长的、大的」+ 希腊 oikonomia（oikos「家宅」+ nemein「管理」）→ 拉丁 oeconomia → 英语中的经济学；再加表示「大」的前缀构成宏观经济学，一般认为二十世纪三十年代随国民收入核算与总量分析定型，首见年份来源不确定。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one line: the branch is named, taught, defined by its aggregate viewpoint, applied to policy, divided into short swings and long growth, widened to open economies, and finally borrowed in speech for any whole-system view.","cn":"八个义项沿一条线展开：先给分支命名，再进入课堂，以总量视角界定自身，用于政策，分为短期波动与长期增长，扩展到开放经济，最后被口语借去指任何整体层面的看法。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one dashboard where the whole country's output, jobs and prices are read as a single instrument.","cn":"核心意象：一块仪表盘，全国的产出、就业与物价被当作同一台仪器来读。"},"chain":["AGGREGATE","OUTPUT","EMPLOYMENT","PRICES","CYCLE","POLICY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"NAMING AND TEACHING: the branch is defined by its whole-economy object, then fixed as a standard course and textbook.","cn":"命名与教学：该分支以整体经济为对象而被界定，随后固定为标准课程与教材。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"VIEWPOINT AND USE: looking at totals rather than individuals, and turning those totals into budget and rate decisions.","cn":"视角与用途：看总量而非个体，再把总量变成预算与利率决策。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"TIME SCALES: quarterly swings of boom and slump, and the decades-long rise of output per person.","cn":"时间尺度：季度性的繁荣与衰退摆动，以及数十年的人均产出增长。"},{"senses":"07","en":"BORDERS: exchange rates, trade balances and capital flows enter the same accounts.","cn":"国界：汇率、贸易差额与资本流动进入同一套核算。"},{"senses":"08","en":"BORROWED SCALE: the term escapes the classroom and names any judgment made at the level of the whole.","cn":"被借用的尺度：这个术语走出课堂，用来指任何在整体层面作出的判断。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The word is a prefix plus a discipline noun: a Greek element of size in front, and the household-derived name of economics behind.","cn":"这个词是「前缀加学科名词」：前面是表示尺度的希腊成分，后面是由治家一词演变来的经济学之名。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin oeconomia and oeconomicus provide the older European forms of the economics half, while the size element was latinised as a combining form.","cn":"拉丁 oeconomia 与 oeconomicus 提供「经济学」那一半较早的欧洲形式，而表示尺度的成分则被拉丁化为组合形式。"},"items":[{"word":"macro-","structure":"prefix of Greek origin meaning large or long","meaning":"at a large scale, taken as a whole","meaningCN":"表示「大、整体」的前缀","example":"The prefix marks the whole economy as the unit of study.","exampleCN":"这个前缀把整个经济标记为研究单位。"},{"word":"makros","structure":"Greek adjective","meaning":"long, large, far-reaching","meaningCN":"长的；大的；范围广的","example":"Makros supplied the size element of the compound.","exampleCN":"makros 提供了这个复合词中表示尺度的成分。"},{"word":"oikonomia","structure":"Greek compound noun, oikos plus nemein","meaning":"household management","meaningCN":"治家之术","example":"Oikonomia is the oldest layer of the base word.","exampleCN":"oikonomia 是基础词最古老的一层。"},{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"Latin noun, first declension","meaning":"management of an estate or state","meaningCN":"庄园或国家的管理","example":"Oeconomia carried the idea into learned Latin.","exampleCN":"oeconomia 把这个观念带入学术拉丁语。"},{"word":"economics","structure":"economy + -ics, discipline suffix","meaning":"the study of production, trade and resources","meaningCN":"研究生产、贸易与资源的学科","example":"Economics is the base to which the size prefix is added.","exampleCN":"经济学是加接尺度前缀的基础词。"},{"word":"-ics","structure":"suffix naming a field of study","meaning":"the academic field of","meaningCN":"表示某一学科领域","example":"The suffix makes a subject name out of a noun.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把名词变成学科名称。"},{"word":"macroeconomic","structure":"macro- + economic, adjective","meaning":"relating to the economy as a whole","meaningCN":"与整体经济相关的","example":"Macroeconomic data cover national totals.","exampleCN":"宏观数据涵盖国民总量。"},{"word":"macroeconomist","structure":"macro- + economist, person noun","meaning":"a specialist in the whole-economy branch","meaningCN":"整体经济分支的专家","example":"A macroeconomist reads national accounts first.","exampleCN":"宏观经济学家最先读的是国民账户。"},{"word":"micro-","structure":"prefix of Greek origin meaning small","meaning":"at a small scale, one unit at a time","meaningCN":"表示「小、单个」的前缀","example":"The opposite prefix names the smaller unit of study.","exampleCN":"相对的前缀命名更小的研究单位。"},{"word":"macroeconomics","structure":"macro- + economics, discipline noun","meaning":"the discipline of whole-economy totals","meaningCN":"研究整体经济总量的学科","example":"Macroeconomics grew beside national income accounts.","exampleCN":"宏观经济学与国民收入核算一同成长。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"oeconomia, oeconomiae (f., first declension)","meaning":"management of a household or state","meaningCN":"家宅或国家的管理"},{"word":"oeconomicus","structure":"oeconomicus, oeconomica, oeconomicum (adj., first and second declension)","meaning":"of household or state management","meaningCN":"治家的；治国的"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"macroeconomic","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观经济的"},{"word":"macroeconomist","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观经济学家"},{"word":"macroeconometrics","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观计量经济学"},{"word":"macroeconometric","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观计量经济学的"},{"word":"macroeconomy","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观经济体；整体经济"}]}},{"word":"microeconomics","ipa_uk":"/ˌmaɪkrəʊˌiːkəˈnɒmɪks/","ipa_us":"/ˌmaɪkroʊˌiːkəˈnɑːmɪks/","definition_zh":"微观经济学；研究单个消费者、厂商与单个市场如何作出选择的经济学分支","definition_en":"the branch of economics that studies how individual consumers, firms and single markets make choices and set prices","core_image":"一枚放大镜移到一个菜市场摊位上，画面里只剩一个买主和一个卖主在讨价还价","scene":"菜市场里其余摊位都被略去，只留下一张桌子、一个买主和一个卖主，研究者记录他们如何议价。Microeconomics explains how a single firm decides what price to charge when its rivals are watching.","sceneCN":"菜市场其余摊位被略去，只留一张桌子、一个买主与一个卖主，研究者记录议价过程；句中的 microeconomics 指「研究单个消费者、厂商与市场的分支」（第 1 个义项：以个体经济单位为研究对象的经济学分支）。图中可辨识物件：放大镜、菜摊、价签、记账本。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"微观经济学；个体经济学"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"microeconomics textbook","zh":"微观经济学教材"},{"phrase":"microeconomics course","zh":"微观经济学课程"},{"phrase":"principles of microeconomics","zh":"微观经济学原理"},{"phrase":"intermediate microeconomics","zh":"中级微观经济学"},{"phrase":"applied microeconomics","zh":"应用微观经济学"},{"phrase":"microeconomics exam","zh":"微观经济学考试"}],"forms":[{"label":"不可数","form":"uncountable"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"microeconomic","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观经济的；个体经济的"},{"word":"microeconomist","pos":"n.","zh":"微观经济学家"},{"word":"microeconometrics","pos":"n.","zh":"微观计量经济学"},{"word":"microeconometric","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观计量经济学的"},{"word":"micro","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观的；小范围的（口语缩略）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The branch studying single units","titleCN":"研究个体经济单位的学科分支","definition":"the division of economics that studies individual consumers, firms and markets rather than national totals","definitionCN":"研究单个消费者、厂商与市场而非国民总量的经济学分支","example":"Microeconomics begins with one household buying bread.","exampleCN":"微观经济学从一个购买面包的家庭开始。","why":"The prefix marks small scale and the base names the discipline, so the compound means the study of the economy at the level of single units.","whyCN":"前缀标记小尺度，基础词指学科，因此这个复合词意为「在单个单位层面研究经济」。"},{"no":"02","title":"The university subject","titleCN":"大学课程与教材科目","definition":"the name of a standard first course and textbook in economics degrees","definitionCN":"经济学学位中一门标准入门课程与教材的名称","example":"Microeconomics is usually the first economics course students meet.","exampleCN":"微观经济学通常是学生接触的第一门经济学课程。","why":"When a branch is taught in a fixed sequence, its name becomes a subject title, and this branch is conventionally the introductory one.","whyCN":"当分支按固定顺序讲授，其名称便成为科目名，而这个分支传统上正是入门的那一门。"},{"no":"03","title":"Price formation and equilibrium","titleCN":"价格形成与市场均衡","definition":"the analysis of how supply and demand set a price in a single market","definitionCN":"分析单个市场中供给与需求如何决定价格","example":"Microeconomics shows how a shortage pushes the price of a single good up.","exampleCN":"微观经济学说明短缺如何推高单一商品的价格。","why":"Because the small-scale unit is a single market, the branch's oldest task is to explain the price formed there.","whyCN":"由于小尺度的单位是单个市场，这个分支最古老的任务就是解释在那里形成的价格。"},{"no":"04","title":"Consumer choice and utility","titleCN":"消费者选择与效用","definition":"the study of how one person weighs wants, income and prices before buying","definitionCN":"研究个人在购买前如何权衡欲望、收入与价格","example":"Microeconomics models the consumer as choosing between two goods on a fixed budget.","exampleCN":"微观经济学把消费者建模为在固定预算下于两种商品之间作选择。","why":"If the unit of analysis is one person, the natural question is what that person chooses and why, which the branch formalises as utility.","whyCN":"若分析单位是一个人，自然的问题就是这个人选择什么、为何选择，该分支把它形式化为效用。"},{"no":"05","title":"Firm production and cost","titleCN":"厂商的生产与成本决策","definition":"the study of how one business combines inputs and decides output and price","definitionCN":"研究单个企业如何组合投入并决定产量与价格","example":"Microeconomics asks how a bakery decides whether to hire a second baker.","exampleCN":"微观经济学追问一家面包店如何决定是否再雇一名面包师。","why":"The same individual-level lens applied to a producer turns into questions of input, cost and output.","whyCN":"同一套个体层面的视角用在生产者身上，就转为投入、成本与产量的问题。"},{"no":"06","title":"Market structure and competition","titleCN":"市场结构与竞争","definition":"the comparison of monopoly, oligopoly and competitive markets by the number and power of sellers","definitionCN":"按卖者数量与势力比较垄断、寡头与竞争性市场","example":"Microeconomics predicts that a monopoly will charge more than a competitive market.","exampleCN":"微观经济学预测垄断者会比竞争性市场要价更高。","why":"Once single markets are the unit, they can be classified by how many sellers meet how many buyers, and the branch compares those structures.","whyCN":"一旦以单个市场为单位，就可以按卖者与买者的数量给市场分类，该分支便比较这些结构。"},{"no":"07","title":"Applied microeconomic policy","titleCN":"应用微观政策分析","definition":"the use of individual-level analysis to judge taxes, regulation, labour and public programmes","definitionCN":"用个体层面分析评判税收、监管、劳动与公共项目","example":"Applied microeconomics evaluated whether the childcare subsidy raised employment.","exampleCN":"应用微观经济学评估育儿补贴是否提高了就业。","why":"Policy questions about specific groups and prices fall inside the small-scale lens, so the branch supplies the evaluation tools.","whyCN":"关于特定群体与价格的政策问题落在小尺度视角之内，该分支便提供评估工具。"},{"no":"08","title":"Microfoundations for the whole","titleCN":"为总体解释提供微观基础","definition":"the methodological role of explaining aggregate outcomes through the choices of individual agents","definitionCN":"以个体行为者的选择来解释总体结果的方法论角色","example":"Microeconomics supplies the microfoundations that aggregate models are built on.","exampleCN":"微观经济学提供总体模型赖以建立的微观基础。","why":"Even when the question is national, the small-scale branch can claim authority by showing that totals are the sum of individual decisions.","whyCN":"即使问题是全国的，小尺度分支也能通过说明总量是个体决策之和来主张自己的解释力。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Microeconomics joins a Greek prefix meaning 'small' to economics, which descends from Greek oikonomia through Latin oeconomia. The compound and its adjective are generally thought to have settled around the 1940s as the discipline divided into small-scale and large-scale branches; the exact first year is uncertain.","cn":"这个词把一个表示「小的」的希腊前缀加在经济学科之名上，而后者经拉丁 oeconomia 源自希腊 oikonomia。一般认为这个复合词及其形容词形式在二十世纪四十年代前后随学科分工固定下来；具体首见年份来源不确定。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK MIKROS","en":"Mikros meant 'small, little, slight' and formed the opposite in scale to the large prefix used for the whole economy.","cn":"mikros 意为「小的、微小的、轻微的」，在尺度上与表示整体经济的大前缀相对。"},{"era":"GREEK OIKONOMIA","en":"Oikonomia, from oikos 'household' and nemein 'to manage', named the running of a household and later of public affairs.","cn":"oikonomia 由 oikos「家宅」与 nemein「管理」构成，先指经营家宅，后也指管理公共事务。"},{"era":"LATIN OECONOMIA","en":"Latin oeconomia carried the word into European learned usage, covering the management of an estate or a state.","cn":"拉丁 oeconomia 把这个词带入欧洲学术用语，其范围包括庄园或国家的管理。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ECONOMICS","en":"In the nineteenth century political economy was shortened to economics, giving the base to which the small-scale prefix was later attached.","cn":"十九世纪政治经济学缩称为经济学，为后来加接小尺度前缀提供了基础词。"},{"era":"MICROECONOMIC","en":"The adjective is generally thought to have appeared in the early twentieth century, when analysis of single units needed a name of its own.","cn":"一般认为这个形容词在二十世纪初出现，当时针对单个单位的分析需要一个自己的名称。"},{"era":"MICROECONOMICS","en":"The noun is generally thought to have settled around the 1940s as teaching and research split into individual-level and whole-economy branches; the exact year is uncertain.","cn":"一般认为这个名词在二十世纪四十年代前后固定，当时教学与研究分成个体层面与整体经济两个分支；具体年份不确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group holds forms from the same compound that differ in word class or scale; the near-meaning group holds smaller theories that each take one part of the individual-level picture.","cn":"形近组收的是同一复合词中词性或尺度不同的形式；近义组收的是各自的更小理论，只取个体层面图景的一部分。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"microeconomic","ipa":"/ˌmaɪkrəʊiːkəˈnɒmɪk/","tag":"the adjective","definition":"Describes individual-level analysis, as in microeconomic evidence; it cannot serve as the name of a course.","definitionCN":"描述个体层面的分析，如微观经济证据；它不能用作课程名称。"},{"word":"macroeconomics","ipa":"/ˌmækrəʊiːˈkɒnəmɪks/","tag":"the opposite branch","definition":"Studies national totals; the two words share their ending and are routinely paired, so the prefixes are the only thing that keeps them apart.","definitionCN":"研究国民总量；两词词尾相同且常被成对使用，真正区分它们的只有前缀。"},{"word":"economics","ipa":"/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪks/","tag":"the parent discipline","definition":"The whole subject, of which the individual-level branch is one part; it is broader, not a synonym.","definitionCN":"整个学科，个体层面分支只是其中一部分；它范围更广，并非同义词。"},{"word":"micro","ipa":"/ˈmaɪkrəʊ/","tag":"informal shortening","definition":"A casual abbreviation for the branch or a word for anything small; it never appears in a formal course title.","definitionCN":"对该分支的随口简称，也可泛指细小之物；它从不出现于正式课程名称。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"price theory","ipa":"/praɪs ˈθɪəri/","tag":"the older core","definition":"An older name for the study of how prices form in single markets; it covers the price sense but not consumer choice in general.","definitionCN":"研究单个市场价格如何形成的旧名；它覆盖价格方面，却不涵盖一般的消费者选择。"},{"word":"consumer theory","ipa":"/kənˈsjuːmə ˈθɪəri/","tag":"the buyer side","definition":"The part of the branch that models one buyer's preferences and budget; it is a component, not the whole field.","definitionCN":"该分支中为单个买主的偏好与预算建模的部分；它是组成部分，而非整个领域。"},{"word":"industrial organization","ipa":"/ɪnˈdʌstriəl ˌɔːɡənaɪˈzeɪʃən/","tag":"firms and markets","definition":"Studies how firms compete and how markets are structured; it is the branch's firm-centred wing.","definitionCN":"研究企业如何竞争、市场如何构成；它是该分支以企业为中心的一翼。"},{"word":"welfare economics","ipa":"/ˈwelfeə ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪks/","tag":"judging outcomes","definition":"Asks whether a market outcome is good for people overall; it evaluates results rather than explaining the choices behind them.","definitionCN":"追问某一市场结果对人们整体是否有利；它评判结果，而不解释其背后的选择。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations here use the real Greek small prefix, the real household root behind economics, and the real division of labour inside the modern discipline.","cn":"正常联想取自表示「小」的真实希腊前缀、经济学背后真实的治家词根，以及现代学科内部真实的分工。"},"normal":[{"en":"Mikros means small, so the prefix marks the scale of one buyer, one firm, one market.","cn":"mikros 意为小，因此这个前缀标记的是一个买主、一家企业、一个市场的尺度。"},{"en":"Oikonomia, household management, is the same root that gave economics.","cn":"oikonomia 即治家之术，正是给经济学提供词根的那个词。"},{"en":"Price theory was the older label for this work before the compound became standard.","cn":"在这个复合词通行之前，这项工作旧称价格理论。"},{"en":"The pair with macroeconomics is built into the word: small scale against large scale.","cn":"它与宏观经济学的配对就写在这个词里：小尺度对大尺度。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the teaching sense: principles of microeconomics, applied microeconomics.","cn":"固定搭配标出教学义：微观经济学原理、应用微观经济学。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a magnifying glass held over one stall while every other stall is blurred out.","cn":"想象一枚放大镜停在某一个摊位上，其余摊位都被虚化。"},{"en":"Picture one buyer and one seller at a table, with a researcher writing down every word they trade.","cn":"想象桌边只有一个买主和一个卖主，研究者在旁记下他们交换的每一句话。"},{"en":"Picture a single price tag that can be moved by one decision rather than by a national trend.","cn":"想象一张价签，推动它的不是全国趋势，而是某一个决定。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Microeconomics teaches students to treat a household and a firm as the basic units of analysis.","cn":"微观经济学教学生把家庭与企业当作分析的基本单位。"},{"en":"The regulator used microeconomics to argue that two merging shops would raise local prices.","cn":"监管者用微观经济学论证两家商店合并会推高本地价格。"},{"en":"Without microeconomics, the aggregate model would have no account of individual choices at all.","cn":"若没有微观经济学，总体模型便完全无法交代个体选择。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"谐音「麦克柔伊科诺米克斯」：麦克柔先生只盯着一个摊位的一买一卖，算的是小处的账。","word":"microeconomics"},"root":"希腊 mikros「小的」+ 希腊 oikonomia（oikos「家宅」+ nemein「管理」）→ 拉丁 oeconomia → 英语中的经济学；再加表示「小」的前缀构成微观经济学，一般认为二十世纪四十年代前后随学科分工定型，首见年份来源不确定。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one line: the branch is named and taught, then narrowed to price, to the buyer, to the firm and to market structure, applied to policy, and finally offered as the individual-level foundation beneath aggregate claims.","cn":"八个义项沿一条线展开：先给分支命名并进入课堂，再收窄到价格、买主、企业、市场结构，继而用于政策，最后成为支撑总体结论的个体层面基础。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one stall under a magnifying glass, where a single bargain holds the whole picture.","cn":"核心意象：放大镜下的一处摊位，一桩买卖便构成整幅图景。"},"chain":["INDIVIDUAL","CHOICE","PRICE","FIRM","MARKET","WELFARE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"NAMING AND TEACHING: the branch takes the single unit as its object and becomes the standard first course.","cn":"命名与教学：该分支以单个单位为对象，并成为标准的入门课程。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"PRICE AND BUYER: supply meets demand at one price, and one person chooses under a fixed budget.","cn":"价格与买主：供需在一个价格上相遇，而个人在固定预算下作选择。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"FIRM AND MARKET: one producer weighs cost and output, and markets are sorted by the number of sellers.","cn":"企业与市场：单个生产者权衡成本与产量，市场则按卖者数目分类。"},{"senses":"07","en":"APPLIED POLICY: individual-level evidence is used to judge taxes, subsidies and regulation.","cn":"应用政策：用个体层面的证据评判税收、补贴与监管。"},{"senses":"08","en":"FOUNDATION: individual choices are offered as the base on which national totals rest.","cn":"基础：个体选择被当作国民总量所依托的底层。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The word is a scale prefix plus a discipline noun: a Greek element of smallness in front, and the household-derived name of economics behind.","cn":"这个词是「尺度前缀加学科名词」：前面是表示细小的希腊成分，后面是由治家一词演变来的经济学之名。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin oeconomia and oeconomicus provide the older European forms of the economics half, while the smallness element was latinised as a combining form.","cn":"拉丁 oeconomia 与 oeconomicus 提供「经济学」那一半较早的欧洲形式，而表示细小的成分则被拉丁化为组合形式。"},"items":[{"word":"micro-","structure":"prefix of Greek origin meaning small","meaning":"at a small scale, one unit at a time","meaningCN":"表示「小、单个」的前缀","example":"The prefix fixes the unit of study at one buyer or one firm.","exampleCN":"这个前缀把研究单位锁定为一个买主或一家企业。"},{"word":"mikros","structure":"Greek adjective","meaning":"small, little, slight","meaningCN":"小的；微小的；轻微的","example":"Mikros supplied the smallness element of the compound.","exampleCN":"mikros 提供了这个复合词中表示细小的成分。"},{"word":"oikonomia","structure":"Greek compound noun, oikos plus nemein","meaning":"household management","meaningCN":"治家之术","example":"Oikonomia is the oldest layer of the base word.","exampleCN":"oikonomia 是基础词最古老的一层。"},{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"Latin noun, first declension","meaning":"management of an estate or state","meaningCN":"庄园或国家的管理","example":"Oeconomia carried the idea into learned Latin.","exampleCN":"oeconomia 把这个观念带入学术拉丁语。"},{"word":"economics","structure":"economy + -ics, discipline suffix","meaning":"the study of production, trade and resources","meaningCN":"研究生产、贸易与资源的学科","example":"Economics is the base to which the smallness prefix is added.","exampleCN":"经济学是加接细小前缀的基础词。"},{"word":"-ics","structure":"suffix naming a field of study","meaning":"the academic field of","meaningCN":"表示某一学科领域","example":"The suffix makes a subject name out of a noun.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把名词变成学科名称。"},{"word":"microeconomic","structure":"micro- + economic, adjective","meaning":"relating to individual buyers, firms and markets","meaningCN":"与单个买主、企业与市场相关的","example":"Microeconomic evidence comes from household surveys.","exampleCN":"微观经济证据来自家庭调查。"},{"word":"microeconomist","structure":"micro- + economist, person noun","meaning":"a specialist in the individual-level branch","meaningCN":"个体层面分支的专家","example":"A microeconomist studies one market at a time.","exampleCN":"微观经济学家一次研究一个市场。"},{"word":"macro-","structure":"prefix of Greek origin meaning large","meaning":"at a large scale, taken as a whole","meaningCN":"表示「大、整体」的前缀","example":"The opposite prefix names the whole-economy branch.","exampleCN":"相对的前缀命名整体经济分支。"},{"word":"microeconomics","structure":"micro- + economics, discipline noun","meaning":"the discipline of single units and single markets","meaningCN":"研究单个单位与单个市场的学科","example":"Microeconomics became the standard first course.","exampleCN":"微观经济学成为标准的入门课程。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"oeconomia, oeconomiae (f., first declension)","meaning":"management of a household or state","meaningCN":"家宅或国家的管理"},{"word":"oeconomicus","structure":"oeconomicus, oeconomica, oeconomicum (adj., first and second declension)","meaning":"of household or state management","meaningCN":"治家的；治国的"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"microeconomic","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观经济的"},{"word":"microeconomist","pos":"n.","zh":"微观经济学家"},{"word":"microeconometrics","pos":"n.","zh":"微观计量经济学"},{"word":"microeconometric","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观计量经济学的"},{"word":"micro","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观的；小范围的"}]}},{"word":"macroeconomic","ipa_uk":"/ˌmækrəʊˌiːkəˈnɒmɪk/","ipa_us":"/ˌmækroʊˌiːkəˈnɑːmɪk/","definition_zh":"宏观经济的；研究整体经济运行（国民产出、就业、物价总量）的","definition_en":"relating to the whole economy, especially when it is studied through national totals rather than through single firms or households","core_image":"从高空俯瞰一个国家的经济：成千上万家店铺、工厂与住户缩成一张汇总表，总量曲线在纸面上缓缓起落","scene":"一个国家里有无数工厂、店铺与家庭，研究者把它们合成总量来观察。The annual review offers a macroeconomic reading of output, employment and prices.","sceneCN":"前半情境：一个国家里无数工厂、店铺与家庭被合成总量来观察；句中的 macroeconomic 指「把整个经济作为总量来考察的」（第 1 个义项：以国民产出等全国总量为单位）。图中可辨识物件：汇总表格、起落的曲线、地图轮廓、计算器。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"宏观经济的；整体经济层面的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"macroeconomic policy","zh":"宏观经济政策"},{"phrase":"macroeconomic stability","zh":"宏观经济稳定"},{"phrase":"macroeconomic analysis","zh":"宏观经济分析"},{"phrase":"macroeconomic indicators","zh":"宏观经济指标"},{"phrase":"macroeconomic forecast","zh":"宏观经济预测"},{"phrase":"macroeconomic aggregates","zh":"宏观经济总量"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more macroeconomic"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most macroeconomic"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"macroeconomics","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观经济学"},{"word":"macroeconomist","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观经济学家"},{"word":"macroeconometric","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观经济计量学的"},{"word":"macro-level","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观层面的"},{"word":"macro","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观的；整体层面的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Measured in national totals","titleCN":"以全国总量为单位的","definition":"relating to totals compiled for a whole country rather than for one firm or one household","definitionCN":"与为整个国家编制的总量相关，而非针对单个企业或单个住户","example":"The study compares macroeconomic totals across three decades.","exampleCN":"这项研究比较了跨越三十年的宏观经济总量。","why":"the prefix for 'large' is attached to economic, so the adjective marks the scale at which the economy is observed: the whole rather than the parts.","whyCN":"表示「大」的前缀加在「经济的」之上，这个形容词因而标出观察经济的尺度：看整体，不看局部。"},{"no":"02","title":"Belonging to the level of national policy","titleCN":"属于国家政策层面的","definition":"belonging to the level at which a government or central bank acts on the economy as a whole","definitionCN":"属于政府或中央银行对整个经济采取行动的层面","example":"Interest rates and the budget are macroeconomic instruments.","exampleCN":"利率与预算是宏观经济层面的工具。","why":"a tax rate or an interest rate moves millions of prices at once, so such levers act at the scale the word names.","whyCN":"税率或利率一次牵动千百万个价格，这类杠杆正是在这个词所指的尺度上起作用。"},{"no":"03","title":"Treating the economy as one system","titleCN":"把经济当作一个系统来处理的","definition":"approaching an economy as an interacting system of spending, production and trade instead of as separate units","definitionCN":"把经济看成支出、生产与贸易相互作用的一个系统，而非彼此分离的单位","example":"Her macroeconomic model links consumption, investment and trade.","exampleCN":"她的宏观经济模型把消费、投资与贸易联系起来。","why":"once the units are summed, what matters is how the sums feed back into one another, and the adjective names that system view.","whyCN":"各单位一旦汇总，重要的是各总量如何互相反馈，这个形容词命名的正是这种系统视角。"},{"no":"04","title":"Concerned with growth and recession","titleCN":"关注增长与衰退的","definition":"concerned with the long swings of expansion, slowdown and recovery that a whole economy passes through","definitionCN":"关注整个经济所经历的扩张、放缓与复苏等长期摆动","example":"The chapter explains macroeconomic swings between boom and slump.","exampleCN":"这一章解释繁荣与萧条之间的宏观经济摆动。","why":"booms and slumps are visible only in aggregates, so the word naturally covers the study of such swings.","whyCN":"繁荣与萧条只有在总量上才看得出来，因此这个词自然涵盖对这类摆动的研究。"},{"no":"05","title":"Used for cross-country comparison","titleCN":"用于国与国之间的比较","definition":"used when the totals of different countries are set side by side","definitionCN":"用于把不同国家的总量并排放置比较时","example":"Comparisons of macroeconomic performance depend on exchange rates and trade balances.","exampleCN":"宏观经济表现的比较取决于汇率与贸易收支。","why":"a national total is the only unit that can be placed beside another national total, which is why the word travels across borders.","whyCN":"只有全国总量才能与另一个全国总量并排比较，这个词因此能跨国使用。"},{"no":"06","title":"Tied to national accounts and indicators","titleCN":"与国民账户和统计指标挂钩的","definition":"belonging to the statistical framework of national accounts, price indices and employment figures","definitionCN":"属于国民账户、价格指数与就业数据这一统计框架","example":"Official macroeconomic statistics are revised every quarter.","exampleCN":"官方的宏观经济统计每季度修订一次。","why":"the totals have to be counted somewhere, so the word also names the tables and indices that measure them.","whyCN":"总量必须在某处被数出来，因此这个词也指测量这些总量的报表与指数。"},{"no":"07","title":"Describing risk that spreads through the system","titleCN":"描述在系统内扩散的风险的","definition":"describing a strain or failure that spreads from one part of the economy to the whole system","definitionCN":"描述从经济的一处扩散到整个系统的压力或失灵","example":"A bank failure can become a macroeconomic problem within weeks.","exampleCN":"一家银行的倒闭可能在数周内变成宏观经济问题。","why":"the word's scale sense is applied to danger: what begins in one balance sheet can threaten every total in the accounts.","whyCN":"这个词的尺度义被用到危险上：始于一张资产负债表的事，可能威胁账户里的每一个总量。"},{"no":"08","title":"Built into a whole-economy model","titleCN":"构成整体经济模型的一部分","definition":"describing a model, forecast or simulation constructed at the level of the whole economy","definitionCN":"描述以整个经济为单位构建的模型、预测或模拟","example":"The bank revised its macroeconomic forecast after the quarterly figures were published.","exampleCN":"季度数据公布后，银行修订了它的宏观经济预测。","why":"a model built from national totals is called macroeconomic because its unit of construction is the whole system, not the single firm.","whyCN":"由全国总量构建的模型之所以被称为宏观经济的，是因为它的构建单位是整个系统，而不是单个企业。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"The adjective joins a Greek prefix meaning 'large' to economic, which descends from Greek oikonomikos by way of Latin oeconomicus. Dates are approximate.","cn":"这个形容词把表示「大」的希腊前缀接在 economic 之前，而 economic 经拉丁 oeconomicus 来自希腊 oikonomikos。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK MAKROS","en":"Makros meant 'long' and, by extension, 'large'. The reading 'large in scale' is generally thought to be the one that fed the modern prefix.","cn":"makros 意为「长的」，并引申为「大的」。一般认为「尺度上的大」这一读法是现代前缀的来源。"},{"era":"GREEK OIKONOMIKOS","en":"Oikonomikos described the management of a household, built from oikos 'house' and nemein 'to distribute, manage'.","cn":"oikonomikos 指家宅的管理，由 oikos「家宅」与 nemein「分配、管理」构成。"},{"era":"LATIN OECONOMICUS","en":"Latin borrowed the Greek adjective as oeconomicus, still attached to the estate and the household rather than to a state.","cn":"拉丁语借入这个希腊形容词作 oeconomicus，仍附着于产业与家宅，而非国家。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ECONOMIC","en":"English economic, borrowed in the seventeenth century, widened from household management to the wealth and trade of a nation.","cn":"英语 economic 于十七世纪借入，从家宅管理扩展到国家的财富与贸易。"},{"era":"MODERN MACRO-","en":"In the twentieth century the combining form for 'large' was attached to economic to mark the scale of the whole economy.","cn":"到二十世纪，表示「大」的构词成分被接在 economic 之前，以标出整个经济的尺度。"},{"era":"TWENTIETH-CENTURY COINING","en":"Source uncertain (first date): the adjective is generally dated to the 1930s, when totals-based analysis took shape, but no precise first citation is established.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：一般认为这个形容词出现于二十世纪三十年代前后，与总量分析的兴起同步，但确切的首次书证尚未确立。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one lists words that share the same prefix but have nothing to do with money; group two lists terms that stand close in meaning or form the opposite scale.","cn":"第一组是同用这个表示「大」的前缀、却与经济无关的词；第二组是语义相近或构成相反尺度的说法。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"macrocosm","ipa":"/ˈmækrəʊkɒzəm/","tag":"the large world","definition":"The prefix for 'large' plus Greek kosmos 'world': the universe viewed as a single whole, with no economic content at all.","definitionCN":"由表示「大」的前缀加希腊语「世界」构成：把宇宙看作一个整体，与经济毫无关系。"},{"word":"macroscopic","ipa":"/ˌmækrəˈskɒpɪk/","tag":"visible without a lens","definition":"The same prefix plus Greek skopein 'to look': large enough to be seen with the naked eye, as in physics and biology.","definitionCN":"同一前缀加希腊语「看」：大到肉眼可见，用于物理与生物学。"},{"word":"macromolecular","ipa":"/ˌmækrəʊməˈlekjələ/","tag":"chemistry, not economics","definition":"The prefix plus molecule: belonging to very large molecules such as proteins, a term of chemistry only.","definitionCN":"前缀加「分子」：属于蛋白质一类的大分子，纯属化学术语。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"microeconomic","ipa":"/ˌmaɪkrəʊˌiːkəˈnɒmɪk/","tag":"opposite scale","definition":"The same economic base with the prefix for 'small': it studies single firms, households and single markets, the exact mirror of this word.","definitionCN":"同样的经济词干配表示「小」的前缀：研究单个企业、住户与单个市场，正是本词的反面。"},{"word":"aggregate","ipa":"/ˈæɡrɪɡət/","tag":"added together","definition":"From Latin ad- 'to' plus grex 'flock': a figure formed by adding many units, which is the raw material of macroeconomic work.","definitionCN":"来自拉丁语中表示「向」的前缀加 grex「群」：把许多单位相加而成的数字，正是宏观经济工作的原料。"},{"word":"economy-wide","ipa":"/ɪˈkɒnəmi waɪd/","tag":"plain compound","definition":"A transparent compound meaning 'across the whole economy'; it states the scope plainly, without the technical flavour of the adjective.","definitionCN":"一个意思透明的复合词，指「遍及整个经济」；它朴素地说明范围，没有该形容词的技术色彩。"},{"word":"fiscal","ipa":"/ˈfɪskəl/","tag":"public purse","definition":"From Latin fiscus 'purse': concerning government taxing and spending, one of the main instruments used at this scale.","definitionCN":"来自拉丁 fiscus「钱袋」：关于政府征税与开支，是在这一尺度上使用的主要工具之一。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives rather than invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"The prefix for 'large' plus 'of the economy' gives a word for the economy seen at full scale.","cn":"表示「大」的前缀加上「经济的」，得到的是把经济整体放大来看的词。"},{"en":"The family runs macroeconomic, macroeconomics, macroeconomist, macroeconometric.","cn":"同族词包括 macroeconomic、macroeconomics、macroeconomist、macroeconometric。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the field: macroeconomic policy, macroeconomic stability, macroeconomic indicators.","cn":"固定搭配标出领域：宏观经济政策、宏观经济稳定、宏观经济指标。"},{"en":"It forms a pair with microeconomic: same base, opposite prefix, whole versus part.","cn":"它与 microeconomic 构成一对：同样的词干，相反的前缀，整体对部分。"},{"en":"The phrase macroeconomic aggregates is a reliable signal, because aggregates are exactly what the word studies.","cn":"「宏观经济总量」这一搭配是可靠信号，因为总量正是这个词研究的对象。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture an aerial photograph in which millions of separate transactions blur into one rising curve.","cn":"想象一张航拍照片，千百万笔分散的交易模糊成一条上升的曲线。"},{"en":"Picture a doctor reading a whole-body temperature chart instead of one finger's warmth.","cn":"想象医生看的是全身的体温曲线，而不是一根手指的温热。"},{"en":"Picture a weather map covering a continent where you can no longer find your own street.","cn":"想象一张覆盖整个大陆的天气图，上面再也找不到自己那条街。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Macroeconomic analysis treats inflation and unemployment as connected totals.","cn":"宏观经济分析把通胀与失业看作相互关联的总量。"},{"en":"The central bank raised rates for macroeconomic reasons rather than to protect one industry.","cn":"央行加息是出于宏观经济考虑，而不是为了保护某一个行业。"},{"en":"Nothing in a macroeconomic forecast tells a small shop whether its own prices are too high.","cn":"宏观经济预测里没有任何内容能告诉一家小店，它自己的定价是否过高。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「大」的前缀加「经济的」——把整个国家的经济合起来看 → 宏观经济的","word":"macroeconomic"},"root":"希腊 makros「长的、大的」+ oikonomikos（oikos「家宅」+ nemein「分配、管理」）→ 拉丁 oeconomicus → 英语 economic；二十世纪再加表示「大」的前缀，构成指整体经济层面的形容词。首见年份来源不确定。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses all keep one scale in view: the economy as a whole. From national totals the line moves to the policy levers used at that scale, to system modelling, to booms and slumps, to cross-country tables, to the statistics themselves, to risk that spreads through the system, and finally to forecasts built from those totals.","cn":"八个义项始终守着同一个尺度：作为整体的经济。从全国总量出发，这条线依次走向该尺度上的政策杠杆、系统建模、繁荣与萧条、跨国对照表、统计本身、在系统内扩散的风险，最后落到由这些总量构建的预测。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: an aerial view in which every shop and household becomes one number in a national total.","cn":"核心意象：一张俯瞰图，每间店铺与每户人家都变成一个全国总量里的数字。"},"chain":["WHOLE ECONOMY","NATIONAL TOTALS","DEMAND AND OUTPUT","POLICY LEVERS","BOOM AND SLUMP","SYSTEMIC RISK"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"SCOPE AND LEVER: totals define the scale, and the same scale is where interest rates and budgets act.","cn":"范围与杠杆：总量界定尺度，而利率与预算正是在同一尺度上起作用。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"SYSTEM AND CYCLE: sums that feed back into one another produce the long swings the word also names.","cn":"系统与周期：互相反馈的总量产生长期摆动，这也在词义之内。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"COMPARISON AND COUNTING: national totals can be set beside other nations only because statistics produce them.","cn":"比较与计量：全国总量之所以能与别国并排，是因为统计把它们生产出来。"},{"senses":"07","en":"CONTAGION: scale turns local failure into a threat to every total on the page.","cn":"扩散：尺度使局部的失灵变成对纸面上每一个总量的威胁。"},{"senses":"08","en":"MODEL: the same scale names the forecasts and simulations built from national totals.","cn":"模型：同一尺度也命名由全国总量构建的预测与模拟。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The word can be read morpheme by morpheme: a Greek prefix for size, a Greek noun for the household, a Greek verb for managing, and an English suffix that turns the stem into an adjective.","cn":"这个词可以按语素逐个读出：表示尺度的希腊前缀、指家宅的希腊名词、表示管理的希腊动词，以及把词干变成形容词的英语后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Greek oikonomikos reached English through Latin oeconomicus; the Latin noun oeconomia and the agent noun oeconomus belong to the same estate-management family.","cn":"希腊 oikonomikos 经拉丁 oeconomicus 进入英语；拉丁名词 oeconomia 与施事名词 oeconomus 同属家产管理这一词族。"},"items":[{"word":"macro-","structure":"macro- (Greek prefix, from makros 'long, large')","meaning":"large in scale","meaningCN":"尺度上的「大」","example":"The prefix sets the scale of the whole.","exampleCN":"这个前缀标出整体的尺度。"},{"word":"makros","structure":"makros (Greek adjective)","meaning":"long; large","meaningCN":"长的；大的","example":"Makros is generally thought to be the source of the prefix.","exampleCN":"一般认为这个希腊形容词就是该前缀的来源。"},{"word":"oikos","structure":"oikos (Greek noun, second declension)","meaning":"house, household","meaningCN":"家宅；一家人","example":"Oikos names the household that is managed.","exampleCN":"这个词指被管理的那一家人。"},{"word":"nemein","structure":"nemein (Greek verb)","meaning":"to distribute, to manage","meaningCN":"分配；管理","example":"Nemein supplies the idea of managing a store.","exampleCN":"这个词提供了「管理储备」的意思。"},{"word":"oikonomikos","structure":"oikos + nemein + -ikos (adjective suffix)","meaning":"of household management","meaningCN":"家务管理的","example":"The Greek adjective joined house to management.","exampleCN":"这个希腊形容词把家宅与管理连在一起。"},{"word":"oeconomicus","structure":"oeconomicus, oeconomica, oeconomicum (Latin adjective)","meaning":"of household or estate management","meaningCN":"家宅或产业管理的","example":"Latin kept the adjective close to the household.","exampleCN":"拉丁语保留了它贴近家宅的含义。"},{"word":"economic","structure":"economic (English adjective)","meaning":"of the economy","meaningCN":"经济的","example":"English widened the adjective to the wealth of a state.","exampleCN":"英语把这个形容词扩展到国家财富。"},{"word":"-ic","structure":"-ic (suffix forming adjectives)","meaning":"relating to","meaningCN":"与……有关的","example":"The suffix makes an adjective of a noun stem.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把名词词干变成形容词。"},{"word":"macroeconomic","structure":"macro- + economic","meaning":"of the whole economy","meaningCN":"整体经济的","example":"The adjective names the whole-economy scale.","exampleCN":"这个形容词指整个经济的尺度。"},{"word":"macroeconomics","structure":"macroeconomic + -s (field of study)","meaning":"the study of economy-wide totals","meaningCN":"研究整体经济总量的学科","example":"Macroeconomics grew out of totals-based analysis.","exampleCN":"宏观经济学从总量分析中发展出来。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"oeconomicus","structure":"oeconomicus, oeconomica, oeconomicum (adj., first and second declension)","meaning":"of household or estate management","meaningCN":"家宅或产业管理的"},{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"oeconomia, oeconomiae (f., first declension)","meaning":"household management, economy","meaningCN":"家产管理；经济"},{"word":"oeconomus","structure":"oeconomus, oeconomi (m., second declension)","meaning":"steward, manager of a household","meaningCN":"管家；家产管理者"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"macroeconomics","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观经济学"},{"word":"macroeconomist","pos":"n.","zh":"宏观经济学家"},{"word":"macroeconometric","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观经济计量学的"},{"word":"macro-level","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观层面的"},{"word":"macro","pos":"adj.","zh":"宏观的；整体层面的"}]}},{"word":"microeconomic","ipa_uk":"/ˌmaɪkrəʊˌiːkəˈnɒmɪk/","ipa_us":"/ˌmaɪkroʊˌiːkəˈnɑːmɪk/","definition_zh":"微观经济的；研究单个企业、住户或单个市场层面的","definition_en":"relating to the choices of single firms, households or single markets rather than to the economy as a whole","core_image":"俯身看一间小店的账本：一位店主、一栏进货、一栏售价，视线只落在这一个柜台","scene":"一条街上开着许多小店，研究者却只盯住其中一家的账本。The course begins with microeconomic choices made by a single household and a single firm.","sceneCN":"前半情境：一条街上许多小店，研究者只盯住其中一家的账本；句中的 microeconomic 指「以单个住户或单个企业为观察单位的」（第 1 个义项：研究单个主体而非全国总量）。图中可辨识物件：小店账本、价目牌、进货清单、算盘。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"微观经济的；单个主体层面的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"microeconomic theory","zh":"微观经济理论"},{"phrase":"microeconomic analysis","zh":"微观经济分析"},{"phrase":"microeconomic reform","zh":"微观经济改革"},{"phrase":"microeconomic policy","zh":"微观经济政策"},{"phrase":"microeconomic incentives","zh":"微观经济激励"},{"phrase":"microeconomic level","zh":"微观经济层面"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more microeconomic"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most microeconomic"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"microeconomics","pos":"n.","zh":"微观经济学"},{"word":"microeconomist","pos":"n.","zh":"微观经济学家"},{"word":"microeconometric","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观经济计量学的"},{"word":"micro-level","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观层面的"},{"word":"micro","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观的；单个主体层面的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Measured at the single unit","titleCN":"以单个主体为单位的","definition":"relating to one firm, one household or one producer rather than to totals for a whole country","definitionCN":"与单个企业、单个住户或单个生产者相关，而非整个国家的总量","example":"Each microeconomic decision about hiring stays with the owner of the shop.","exampleCN":"每一个关于雇人的微观经济决定都由店主自己作出。","why":"the prefix for 'small' is attached to economic, so the adjective marks the unit observed: one agent, not the aggregate.","whyCN":"表示「小」的前缀加在「经济的」之上，这个形容词因而标出观察的单位：一个主体，而非总量。"},{"no":"02","title":"Concentrated on one market","titleCN":"集中在单个市场上的","definition":"relating to a single market in which one good or service is bought and sold","definitionCN":"与买卖某一种商品或服务的单个市场相关","example":"The microeconomic question is why the price of one good rose.","exampleCN":"这里的微观经济问题是：某一种商品的价格为何上涨。","why":"a single market is the smallest arena where supply meets demand, and the word marks that arena.","whyCN":"单个市场是供给与需求相遇的最小场所，这个词标出的正是这个场所。"},{"no":"03","title":"Explaining individual choice","titleCN":"解释个体选择的","definition":"concerning the incentives and choices of individual buyers, workers or sellers","definitionCN":"关于个体买方、劳动者或卖方的激励与选择","example":"Microeconomic reasoning explains why a consumer switches brands.","exampleCN":"微观经济推理能解释消费者为何更换品牌。","why":"once the unit is a person or a firm, the question becomes what that unit chooses and why.","whyCN":"一旦单位落到一个人或一家企业，问题就变成这个单位选择什么、为什么选择。"},{"no":"04","title":"Analysing one relation at a time","titleCN":"一次只分析一重关系的","definition":"using partial analysis, in which one relationship is examined while everything else is held unchanged","definitionCN":"采用局部分析，在其余条件不变时考察一重关系","example":"A microeconomic treatment isolates the effect of a single tax.","exampleCN":"微观经济的处理方式把单一税种的影响单独分离出来。","why":"the method follows the unit: to see how one price responds, the analyst must keep the rest of the system still.","whyCN":"方法跟单位走：要看清一个价格如何反应，分析者必须让系统的其余部分静止。"},{"no":"05","title":"Applied to a single industry","titleCN":"应用于单个行业的","definition":"concerning the rules or performance of one industry or one sector rather than of the whole economy","definitionCN":"关于某一个行业或某一个部门的规则或表现，而非整个经济","example":"Rules on one chain of stores are a microeconomic matter.","exampleCN":"针对某一家连锁店的规则属于微观经济事项。","why":"an industry is a collection of units of the same kind, so policy aimed at it stays inside the word's scale.","whyCN":"一个行业是同类单位的集合，针对它的政策仍在这个词的尺度之内。"},{"no":"06","title":"Built on disaggregated data","titleCN":"基于分解到个体的数据的","definition":"based on data collected from separate units, such as individual households or individual plants","definitionCN":"基于从各个独立单位收集的数据，如单个住户或单个工厂","example":"The survey provides microeconomic data on household spending.","exampleCN":"这项调查提供关于住户支出的微观经济数据。","why":"counting one unit at a time is what makes the smallest scale measurable, so the adjective also describes the data.","whyCN":"逐个单位地数是使最小尺度可测量的方式，因此这个形容词也用来描述这类数据。"},{"no":"07","title":"Naming one branch of economics","titleCN":"作为经济学的一个分支名称","definition":"naming the branch of economics that studies single units, as opposed to the branch that studies totals","definitionCN":"命名研究单个单位的经济学分支，与研究对象为总量的分支相对","example":"The textbook turns from microeconomic foundations to national accounts.","exampleCN":"这本教材从微观经济的基础转向国民账户。","why":"universities divided the subject by the size of its unit, and the adjective became the label of one half.","whyCN":"大学按研究单位的大小划分这门学科，这个形容词便成了其中一半的名称。"},{"no":"08","title":"Applied beyond formal markets","titleCN":"用于正式市场之外的微观分析","definition":"describing microeconomic reasoning applied to households, time use and other small-scale choices outside formal markets","definitionCN":"描述把微观经济分析用于住户、时间分配等正式市场之外的小尺度选择","example":"Microeconomic reasoning explains how a household divides unpaid work between its members.","exampleCN":"微观经济推理可以解释一户人家如何在成员之间分配无偿劳动。","why":"the unit of analysis stays the single household or person even when no market transaction is involved, so the adjective travels beyond price-setting.","whyCN":"即使不涉及市场交易，分析单位仍是单户或单人，因此这个形容词能从定价扩展到别的选择。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"The adjective joins a Greek prefix meaning 'small' to economic, which descends from Greek oikonomikos by way of Latin oeconomicus. Dates are approximate.","cn":"这个形容词把表示「小」的希腊前缀接在 economic 之前，而 economic 经拉丁 oeconomicus 来自希腊 oikonomikos。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK MIKROS","en":"Mikros meant 'small, little'. The reading 'small in scale' is generally thought to be the one that fed the modern prefix.","cn":"mikros 意为「小的、微小的」。一般认为「尺度上的小」这一读法是现代前缀的来源。"},{"era":"GREEK OIKONOMIKOS","en":"Oikonomikos described the management of a household, built from oikos 'house' and nemein 'to distribute, manage'.","cn":"oikonomikos 指家宅的管理，由 oikos「家宅」与 nemein「分配、管理」构成。"},{"era":"LATIN OECONOMICUS","en":"Latin borrowed the Greek adjective as oeconomicus, still attached to the estate and the household rather than to a state.","cn":"拉丁语借入这个希腊形容词作 oeconomicus，仍附着于产业与家宅，而非国家。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ECONOMIC","en":"English economic, borrowed in the seventeenth century, widened from household management to the wealth and trade of a nation.","cn":"英语 economic 于十七世纪借入，从家宅管理扩展到国家的财富与贸易。"},{"era":"MODERN MICRO-","en":"In the twentieth century the combining form for 'small' was attached to economic to mark the scale of a single unit.","cn":"到二十世纪，表示「小」的构词成分被接在 economic 之前，以标出单个单位的尺度。"},{"era":"MID-TWENTIETH-CENTURY COINING","en":"Source uncertain (first date): the adjective is generally dated to the mid twentieth century, when analysis of single units was formally named, but no precise first citation is established.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：一般认为这个形容词在二十世纪中期定名，与微观分析的制度化同步，但确切的首次书证尚未确立。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one lists words that share the same prefix but concern lenses, circuits or worlds; group two lists terms that stand close in meaning or form the opposite scale.","cn":"第一组是同用这个表示「小」的前缀、却分别关于透镜、电路与世界的词；第二组是语义相近或构成相反尺度的说法。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"microscopic","ipa":"/ˌmaɪkrəˈskɒpɪk/","tag":"too small to see","definition":"The same prefix plus Greek skopein 'to look': too small to be seen without a lens, a term of optics and biology rather than of money.","definitionCN":"同一前缀加希腊语「看」：小到不借助透镜就看不见，属光学与生物学术语，与经济无关。"},{"word":"microelectronic","ipa":"/ˌmaɪkrəʊɪˌlekˈtrɒnɪk/","tag":"tiny circuits","definition":"The prefix plus electronic: belonging to circuits and devices built on a very small scale.","definitionCN":"前缀加「电子的」：属于以极小尺度制造的电路与器件。"},{"word":"microcosm","ipa":"/ˈmaɪkrəʊkɒzəm/","tag":"the small world","definition":"The prefix plus Greek kosmos 'world': a small world that mirrors a larger one, with no economic sense.","definitionCN":"前缀加希腊语「世界」：映照大世界的小世界，没有经济含义。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"macroeconomic","ipa":"/ˌmækrəʊˌiːkəˈnɒmɪk/","tag":"opposite scale","definition":"The same economic base with the prefix for 'large': it studies national totals, the exact mirror of this word.","definitionCN":"同样的经济词干配表示「大」的前缀：研究全国总量，正是本词的反面。"},{"word":"partial","ipa":"/ˈpɑːʃəl/","tag":"one relation at a time","definition":"From Latin pars 'part': in economics it describes analysis that examines one relation while holding the rest fixed.","definitionCN":"来自拉丁 pars「部分」：在经济学中描述只考察一重关系、把其余条件保持不变的分析方式。"},{"word":"firm-level","ipa":"/fɜːm ˈlevəl/","tag":"plain compound","definition":"A transparent compound meaning 'at the scale of an individual company'; it states the unit without the technical label.","definitionCN":"一个意思透明的复合词，指「以单个公司为尺度」；它朴素地说明单位，不带技术标签。"},{"word":"disaggregated","ipa":"/dɪsˈæɡrɪɡeɪtɪd/","tag":"broken down to units","definition":"From dis- 'apart' plus grex 'flock': separated from a total into its individual units, the typical form of data used here.","definitionCN":"来自拉丁语中表示「分开」的前缀加 grex「群」：从总量拆回各个单位，正是这类研究常用数据的形式。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives rather than invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"The prefix for 'small' plus 'of the economy' gives a word for the economy seen one unit at a time.","cn":"表示「小」的前缀加上「经济的」，得到的是把经济拆到单个单位来看的词。"},{"en":"The family runs microeconomic, microeconomics, microeconomist, microeconometric.","cn":"同族词包括 microeconomic、microeconomics、microeconomist、microeconometric。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the field: microeconomic theory, microeconomic analysis, microeconomic reform.","cn":"固定搭配标出领域：微观经济理论、微观经济分析、微观经济改革。"},{"en":"It forms a pair with macroeconomic: same base, opposite prefix, part versus whole.","cn":"它与 macroeconomic 构成一对：同样的词干，相反的前缀，部分对整体。"},{"en":"The phrase microeconomic data usually signals numbers gathered from individual units.","cn":"「微观经济数据」这一搭配通常信号着从各个独立单位收集来的数字。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a single ledger on a shop counter while the street's other shops stay out of frame.","cn":"想象柜台上摊着一本账，街上其余店铺都留在画面之外。"},{"en":"Picture a biologist adjusting a lens until one cell fills the whole field of view.","cn":"想象生物学家调着透镜，直到一个细胞占满整个视野。"},{"en":"Picture one stone lifted out of a mosaic so its own colour can be studied.","cn":"想象从镶嵌画里取出一块石子，好单独研究它自己的颜色。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Microeconomic theory predicts how a single seller sets a price.","cn":"微观经济理论预测单个卖方如何定价。"},{"en":"The reform was microeconomic in scope, aimed at one industry rather than at national demand.","cn":"这项改革的范围是微观经济的，针对一个行业而非全国需求。"},{"en":"Calling a question microeconomic says nothing about how important the answer is.","cn":"把一个问题称为微观经济的，并不说明它的答案有多重要。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「小」的前缀加「经济的」——把经济拆到一家店、一个柜台来看 → 微观经济的","word":"microeconomic"},"root":"希腊 mikros「小的」+ oikonomikos（oikos「家宅」+ nemein「分配、管理」）→ 拉丁 oeconomicus → 英语 economic；二十世纪再加表示「小」的前缀，构成指单个主体层面的形容词。首见年份来源不确定。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses hold one scale steady: a single unit. The line runs from the individual firm or household, to the single market it trades in, to the choices it makes, to the method that isolates one relation, to one industry as a target, to data gathered unit by unit, to the branch label, and finally to everyday choices made outside formal markets.","cn":"八个义项守住同一个尺度：单个单位。这条线从单个企业或住户出发，走向它交易所在的单个市场、它所作的选择、隔离一重关系的方法、作为政策对象的单个行业、逐个单位收集的数据、分支名称，最后落到正式市场之外的日常选择。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a close-up of one ledger on a counter while the rest of the street stays outside the frame.","cn":"核心意象：柜台上一本账的特写，街上其余一切都被留在画面之外。"},"chain":["ONE UNIT","SINGLE MARKET","CHOICE","PARTIAL METHOD","SECTOR RULE","UNIT-LEVEL DATA"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"UNIT AND ARENA: the agent is one firm or household, and the arena where it acts is one market.","cn":"单位与场所：行动的主体是一家企业或一户人家，行动的场所是一个市场。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"CHOICE AND METHOD: what the unit chooses is studied by isolating a single relation.","cn":"选择与方法：这个单位如何选择，靠隔离一重关系来研究。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"SECTOR AND DATA: one industry can be regulated, and unit-by-unit records make it measurable.","cn":"行业与数据：单个行业可以被规制，逐个单位的记录又使它可测量。"},{"senses":"07","en":"BRANCH LABEL: the scale became the name of one half of the discipline.","cn":"分支名称：这一尺度成了一门学科其中一半的名字。"},{"senses":"08","en":"EVERYDAY CHOICE: unit-level reasoning also covers households and time use outside formal markets.","cn":"日常选择：单位层面的推理也覆盖正式市场之外的住户与时间分配。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The word can be read morpheme by morpheme: a Greek prefix for size, a Greek noun for the household, a Greek verb for managing, and an English suffix that turns the stem into an adjective.","cn":"这个词可以按语素逐个读出：表示尺度的希腊前缀、指家宅的希腊名词、表示管理的希腊动词，以及把词干变成形容词的英语后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Greek oikonomikos reached English through Latin oeconomicus; the Latin noun oeconomia and the agent noun oeconomus belong to the same estate-management family.","cn":"希腊 oikonomikos 经拉丁 oeconomicus 进入英语；拉丁名词 oeconomia 与施事名词 oeconomus 同属家产管理这一词族。"},"items":[{"word":"micro-","structure":"micro- (Greek prefix, from mikros 'small')","meaning":"small in scale","meaningCN":"尺度上的「小」","example":"The prefix sets the scale of one unit.","exampleCN":"这个前缀标出单个单位的尺度。"},{"word":"mikros","structure":"mikros (Greek adjective)","meaning":"small, little","meaningCN":"小的；微小的","example":"Mikros is generally thought to be the source of the prefix.","exampleCN":"一般认为这个希腊形容词就是该前缀的来源。"},{"word":"oikos","structure":"oikos (Greek noun, second declension)","meaning":"house, household","meaningCN":"家宅；一家人","example":"Oikos names the household that is managed.","exampleCN":"这个词指被管理的那一家人。"},{"word":"nemein","structure":"nemein (Greek verb)","meaning":"to distribute, to manage","meaningCN":"分配；管理","example":"Nemein supplies the idea of managing a store.","exampleCN":"这个词提供了「管理储备」的意思。"},{"word":"oikonomikos","structure":"oikos + nemein + -ikos (adjective suffix)","meaning":"of household management","meaningCN":"家务管理的","example":"The Greek adjective joined house to management.","exampleCN":"这个希腊形容词把家宅与管理连在一起。"},{"word":"oeconomicus","structure":"oeconomicus, oeconomica, oeconomicum (Latin adjective)","meaning":"of household or estate management","meaningCN":"家宅或产业管理的","example":"Latin kept the adjective close to the household.","exampleCN":"拉丁语保留了它贴近家宅的含义。"},{"word":"economic","structure":"economic (English adjective)","meaning":"of the economy","meaningCN":"经济的","example":"English widened the adjective to the wealth of a state.","exampleCN":"英语把这个形容词扩展到国家财富。"},{"word":"-ic","structure":"-ic (suffix forming adjectives)","meaning":"relating to","meaningCN":"与……有关的","example":"The suffix makes an adjective of a noun stem.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把名词词干变成形容词。"},{"word":"microeconomic","structure":"micro- + economic","meaning":"of single units in the economy","meaningCN":"单个经济主体的","example":"The adjective names the single-unit scale.","exampleCN":"这个形容词指单个单位的尺度。"},{"word":"microeconomics","structure":"microeconomic + -s (field of study)","meaning":"the study of single firms and markets","meaningCN":"研究单个企业与单个市场的学科","example":"Microeconomics examines one market at a time.","exampleCN":"微观经济学一次考察一个市场。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"oeconomicus","structure":"oeconomicus, oeconomica, oeconomicum (adj., first and second declension)","meaning":"of household or estate management","meaningCN":"家宅或产业管理的"},{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"oeconomia, oeconomiae (f., first declension)","meaning":"household management, economy","meaningCN":"家产管理；经济"},{"word":"oeconomus","structure":"oeconomus, oeconomi (m., second declension)","meaning":"steward, manager of a household","meaningCN":"管家；家产管理者"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"microeconomics","pos":"n.","zh":"微观经济学"},{"word":"microeconomist","pos":"n.","zh":"微观经济学家"},{"word":"microeconometric","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观经济计量学的"},{"word":"micro-level","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观层面的"},{"word":"micro","pos":"adj.","zh":"微观的；单个主体层面的"}]}},{"word":"market","ipa_uk":"/ˈmɑːkɪt/","ipa_us":"/ˈmɑːrkɪt/","definition_zh":"市场；集市；某种商品的交易领域；销路、需求；股市；行销、推销","definition_en":"a place or system in which goods and services are bought and sold, or the willingness of buyers to purchase them","core_image":"清晨的集市街：木棚下摆着成筐的果子，一杆秤搁在摊边，买主与卖主在摊前讨价","scene":"天刚亮，街边木棚下摆满果筐，买卖双方在摊前讨价。Growers bring their produce to a market where buyers bargain over each crate.","sceneCN":"前半情境：天刚亮，街边木棚下摆满果筐，买卖双方在摊前讨价；句中的 market 指「买卖双方定期相聚的集市场地」（第 1 个义项：作为交易场所的集市）。图中可辨识物件：木棚、果筐、杆秤、写价的木牌。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"市场；集市；交易领域；销路；股市；买方群体"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"行销；推销；把产品推向市场"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"on the market","zh":"在售；待售"},{"phrase":"market share","zh":"市场份额"},{"phrase":"market forces","zh":"市场力量"},{"phrase":"market economy","zh":"市场经济"},{"phrase":"stock market","zh":"股票市场"},{"phrase":"target market","zh":"目标市场"},{"phrase":"market research","zh":"市场调研"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"markets"},{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"markets"},{"label":"过去式","form":"marketed"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"marketed"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"marketing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"marketing","pos":"n.","zh":"营销；行销（活动）"},{"word":"marketplace","pos":"n.","zh":"集市；市场场所"},{"word":"marketer","pos":"n.","zh":"营销人员"},{"word":"marketable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可销售的；有销路的"},{"word":"marketization","pos":"n.","zh":"市场化"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A place where buyers and sellers meet","titleCN":"买卖双方相聚的集市场地","definition":"an open place, often with stalls, where people regularly come together to buy and sell goods","definitionCN":"常设有摊位的露天场所，人们定期在此相聚买卖货物","example":"Farmers set up stalls at the weekly market.","exampleCN":"农民每周在集市上摆摊。","why":"the Latin noun mercatus named the place and the trading done there, so the word began as a location for exchange.","whyCN":"拉丁名词 mercatus 既指场所也指在那里进行的交易，因此这个词最初就是交换的地点。"},{"no":"02","title":"Trade in one particular commodity","titleCN":"某一种商品的交易领域","definition":"the whole body of buying and selling in one commodity or one sector, wherever it happens","definitionCN":"某一种商品或某一部门中全部买卖活动的总和，不论发生在何处","example":"The world market for copper tightened last year.","exampleCN":"去年世界铜的交易领域收紧了。","why":"the place sense was transferred from a square to a field of trade, so that copper can have a market with no square at all.","whyCN":"场所义从一方广场转移到一片交易领域，于是铜可以有市场，而完全不需要广场。"},{"no":"03","title":"Demand for a product","titleCN":"销路；需求","definition":"the number of buyers willing to purchase something, or the absence of such buyers","definitionCN":"愿意购买某物的买者数量，或这类买者的缺乏","example":"There is little market for hand-written ledgers now.","exampleCN":"如今手写账簿已没什么销路。","why":"without buyers a place of exchange is empty, so the word came to mean the willingness to buy rather than the ground it stands on.","whyCN":"没有买主，交换的场所就是空的，于是这个词转而指购买的意愿，而不是它所在的那块地。"},{"no":"04","title":"The market for shares and securities","titleCN":"股票与证券的市场","definition":"the organized exchange on which shares, bonds and currencies are traded, or trading there as a whole","definitionCN":"买卖股票、债券与货币的有组织的交易所，或该处的交易整体","example":"Share prices fell across the market before noon.","exampleCN":"午前整个股市的股价都下跌了。","why":"a stock exchange is a marketplace in the original sense, only with paper claims instead of crates, so the old word was kept.","whyCN":"证券交易所就是原义上的集市，只是货物换成了纸面权益，旧词因此被沿用。"},{"no":"05","title":"Offered for sale","titleCN":"在售；待售（置于售卖状态）","definition":"the state of being available to buy, as in a house that has come onto the market","definitionCN":"处于可供购买的状态，如已挂牌出售的房子","example":"The building came onto the market in spring.","exampleCN":"这栋楼在春天挂牌出售。","why":"being placed before buyers is the modern equivalent of being carried to the stalls, and the phrase on the market keeps that image.","whyCN":"被摆到买主面前，相当于旧时把货物挑到摊位上，这一短语保留了那个画面。"},{"no":"06","title":"To sell and promote a product","titleCN":"行销；推销（动词义）","definition":"to promote and sell a product by choosing its buyers, its price and the way it is presented","definitionCN":"通过选择买主、定价与呈现方式来推销并卖出产品","example":"The firm markets its software to schools.","exampleCN":"这家公司把软件行销给学校。","why":"if a market is where goods find buyers, then to market is to do the work of bringing goods and buyers together.","whyCN":"如果市场是货物找到买主的地方，那么行销就是把货物与买主带到一起的工作。"},{"no":"07","title":"The mechanism that sets prices","titleCN":"决定价格的配置机制","definition":"the system in which prices and quantities are settled by the competing decisions of many buyers and sellers","definitionCN":"价格与数量由众多买卖双方的竞争性决定来敲定的系统","example":"The market, not the ministry, decides which suppliers survive.","exampleCN":"决定哪些供应商存活的是市场，而不是部委。","why":"abstracting the place away leaves only its function: bringing competing offers together until a price emerges.","whyCN":"把场所抽掉，只剩它的功能：把互相竞争的报价汇集起来，直到价格出现。"},{"no":"08","title":"The body of intended buyers","titleCN":"目标买方群体","definition":"the group of people or institutions a seller intends to reach, considered as a whole","definitionCN":"卖方打算触及的那一群人或机构，被作为一个整体来看","example":"The brand's market is young urban readers.","exampleCN":"这个品牌的目标买方群体是年轻的城市读者。","why":"a seller who studies the crowd at the stalls ends by treating that crowd as an object to be served, which is the marketing sense.","whyCN":"研究摊位前人群的卖方，最终把那群人当作服务对象，这就是营销义。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Market is Latin in origin, not a native English word: it goes back to Latin mercatus 'market, trading', a noun from the verb mercari 'to trade', which in turn rests on merx (genitive mercis) 'goods'. It reached Old English through Old Northern French and Germanic channels. Dates are approximate.","cn":"market 是拉丁来源，而非英语本族词：它上溯至拉丁名词 mercatus「市场、集市、交易」，该名词出自动词 mercari「做买卖」，而动词又基于 merx（属格 mercis）「货物」。它经古北法语与日耳曼中介进入古英语。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MERX","en":"Merx, genitive mercis, meant 'goods, merchandise'. Its own deeper origin is uncertain, and no pre-Latin source can be demonstrated.","cn":"merx（属格 mercis）意为「货物、商品」。它自身更深的来源不确定，无法证明任何拉丁语之前的源头。"},{"era":"LATIN MERCARI","en":"From the noun came the deponent verb mercari 'to buy and sell, to trade', which names the activity rather than the goods.","cn":"由这个名词产生异态动词 mercari「买卖、做交易」，命名的是活动而非货物。"},{"era":"LATIN MERCATUS","en":"The noun mercatus 'market, marketplace, trading' was formed on the same stem, so place and activity were one word from the start.","cn":"名词 mercatus「市场、集市、交易」由同一词干构成，因此场所与活动从一开始就是一个词。"},{"era":"OLD NORTHERN FRENCH","en":"The form market is generally thought to have come to England through Old Northern French, with Germanic channels also involved in its spread.","cn":"一般认为 market 这一形式经古北法语传入英格兰，其传播也涉及日耳曼中介。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH BORROWING","en":"Old English already had market as a loanword, which is why the word counts as Latin in origin rather than as an inherited native term.","cn":"古英语已经以借词形式拥有 market，因此这个词算作拉丁来源，而非承继的本族词。"},{"era":"MODERN SENSE EXTENSION","en":"From the physical fair the word widened to trade in one commodity, to demand, to the share market and finally to the verb for promoting goods.","cn":"从有形的集市出发，这个词扩展到单一商品的交易、需求、股票市场，最后扩展到推销货物的动词义。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds words from the same Latin root, so their kinship is real and can be traced; group two holds near neighbours that all name places or gatherings for trade.","cn":"第一组的词同出拉丁词根，亲缘关系真实可溯；第二组是同样指交易场所或聚会的近邻词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"merchant","ipa":"/ˈmɜːtʃənt/","tag":"same root, a person","definition":"Through Old French from Latin mercari: a person who trades, so it shares the root for 'goods' with market and adds an agent suffix.","definitionCN":"经古法语来自拉丁 mercari：做买卖的人，与本词同出「货物」这一词根，只多了一个施事后缀。"},{"word":"merchandise","ipa":"/məˈtʃændaɪz/","tag":"same root, the goods","definition":"From merx 'goods' through Old French: the goods themselves, which is the root meaning in concrete form.","definitionCN":"经古法语来自 merx「货物」：货物本身，正是该词根的具体形态。"},{"word":"mercantile","ipa":"/ˈmɜːkəntaɪl/","tag":"same root, an adjective","definition":"From Italian mercante, from Latin mercari: relating to trade, a later borrowing of the same root rather than a new coinage.","definitionCN":"经意大利语来自拉丁 mercari：关于贸易的，是同一词根的后期借入，而非新造词。"},{"word":"commerce","ipa":"/kəˈmɜːs/","tag":"prefix plus the same root","definition":"Com- 'together' plus merx: trade viewed as an organized exchange between parties, another descendant of the same root.","definitionCN":"拉丁语中表示「共同」的前缀加 merx：把贸易看作各方之间有组织的交换，是同一词根的另一支后裔。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"marketplace","ipa":"/ˈmɑːkɪtpleɪs/","tag":"only the place","definition":"Market plus place: the square or platform where trading happens, narrower than market because it has no demand or share-price senses.","definitionCN":"由 market 与表示「地方」的成分复合而成：发生交易的广场或平台，比本词窄，因为不含需求与股价等义。"},{"word":"fair","ipa":"/feə/","tag":"periodic trade gathering","definition":"From Latin feria 'holiday': a periodic, often seasonal gathering for trade, with none of the abstract economic senses of market.","definitionCN":"来自拉丁 feria「节日」：定期、常为季节性的交易聚会，不含本词那些抽象经济义。"},{"word":"bazaar","ipa":"/bəˈzɑː/","tag":"covered rows of shops","definition":"From Persian through Turkish: a covered street of shops, a place word only and never a verb.","definitionCN":"经土耳其语来自波斯语：有顶棚的店铺街，只作场所词，从不用作动词。"},{"word":"mart","ipa":"/mɑːt/","tag":"shortened place word","definition":"A shortened form of market kept for names and poetry; it retains only the place sense.","definitionCN":"market 的缩略形式，多用于名称与诗歌，只保留场所义。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives rather than invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"The chain runs goods, then trade, then place: merx, mercari, mercatus.","cn":"链条是货物、交易、场所：merx、mercari、mercatus。"},{"en":"The family runs market, marketing, marketplace, marketer, marketable, marketization.","cn":"同族词包括 market、marketing、marketplace、marketer、marketable、marketization。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases separate the senses: on the market, market share, market forces, stock market.","cn":"固定搭配分开各个义项：在售、市场份额、市场力量、股票市场。"},{"en":"The same root shows in merchant, merchandise, mercantile and commerce.","cn":"同一词根出现在 merchant、merchandise、mercantile 与 commerce 中。"},{"en":"The verb takes an object: to market a product, and the -ing form is the noun marketing.","cn":"动词要带宾语：把产品行销出去，其动名词形式就是名词「营销」。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a square that is crowded at dawn and swept clean by noon.","cn":"想象一方广场，黎明时挤满人，到正午已被扫空。"},{"en":"Picture two columns on a page: what buyers want, and what they will pay.","cn":"想象纸页上两栏：买主想要什么，愿意付多少。"},{"en":"Picture a board of share prices where one company's fate becomes a single flashing number.","cn":"想象一块股价牌，一家公司的命运变成一个闪动的数字。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The fishing market opens before sunrise and is empty by noon.","cn":"鱼市在日出前开张，到正午便空了。"},{"en":"A product with no market cannot survive, however carefully it is made.","cn":"无论做得多用心，没有销路的产品都活不下去。"},{"en":"The cooperative markets its coffee directly to roasters abroad.","cn":"这家合作社把咖啡直接行销给国外的烘焙商。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「马克」的谐音——集市上每件货物都用马克笔标上价钱 → 市场","word":"market"},"root":"拉丁 merx（属格 mercis）「货物」→ 动词 mercari「做买卖」→ 名词 mercatus「市场、集市、交易」→ 经古北法语与日耳曼中介借入古英语 market；merx 更深来源不确定，故为拉丁来源而非英语本族词。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one building: goods (merx) are traded (mercari) in a place (mercatus). From the dawn square the line moves to trade in a single commodity, to the demand that fills or empties the square, to the share market that inherited the name, to the state of being offered for sale, to the verb that brings goods and buyers together, to the price-setting mechanism abstracted from the square, and finally to the crowd of buyers a seller sets out to serve.","cn":"八个义项沿同一座建筑展开：货物在某个场所里被交易。从黎明时的广场出发，这条线依次走向单一商品的交易、决定广场空与满的需求、继承了这个名称的股票市场、被摆出来售卖的状态、把货物与买主带到一起的动词、从广场抽象出来的定价机制，最后走向卖方打算服务的那群买主。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a dawn market square where crates change hands and the crowd thins by noon.","cn":"核心意象：黎明的集市广场，成筐货物易手，到正午人群渐散。"},"chain":["GOODS","TRADE","PLACE","DEMAND","SHARE PRICES","ALLOCATION"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"PLACE AND COMMODITY: a square for exchange becomes a field of trade in one good.","cn":"场所与商品：用于交换的广场变成某一种商品的交易领域。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"DEMAND AND SHARES: buyers make the square alive, and paper claims inherit its name.","cn":"需求与证券：买主让广场有生气，纸面权益则继承了它的名称。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"OFFER AND PROMOTE: goods are placed before buyers, and someone must bring them there.","cn":"摆出与推销：货物被摆到买主面前，而总得有人把它们带到那里。"},{"senses":"07","en":"ALLOCATION: strip away the square and what remains is a mechanism that settles prices.","cn":"配置：把广场抽走，剩下的就是一个敲定价格的机制。"},{"senses":"08","en":"BUYER GROUP: the crowd at the stalls becomes the audience a seller intends to reach.","cn":"买方群体：摊位前的人群变成卖方打算触及的对象。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The word is a Latin root for 'goods' dressed in noun and verb endings, with English suffixes building the modern family on top.","cn":"这个词是「货物」这一拉丁词根加上名词与动词词尾，再由英语后缀在其上搭起现代词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin merx and its verb mercari supply the stem; mercatus, the noun of place and activity, is the direct ancestor of the English word.","cn":"拉丁 merx 及其动词 mercari 提供词干；指场所与活动的名词 mercatus 则是英语这个词的直接祖先。"},"items":[{"word":"merc-","structure":"merc- (Latin root, from merx 'goods')","meaning":"goods, merchandise","meaningCN":"货物；商品","example":"The root supplies the idea of goods in every member of the family.","exampleCN":"这个词根为词族中每个成员提供「货物」这一观念。"},{"word":"merx","structure":"merx, mercis (Latin noun, third declension)","meaning":"goods, wares","meaningCN":"货物；商品","example":"Merx names what is carried to the stalls.","exampleCN":"merx 指被挑到摊位上的东西。"},{"word":"mercari","structure":"mercari, mercatus sum (Latin deponent verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to trade, to buy and sell","meaningCN":"做交易；买卖","example":"The verb turns goods into an activity.","exampleCN":"这个动词把货物变成一种活动。"},{"word":"mercatus","structure":"mercatus, mercatus (Latin noun, fourth declension)","meaning":"market, trading","meaningCN":"市场；交易","example":"The noun carries both the place and the dealing.","exampleCN":"这个名词同时承载场所与交易。"},{"word":"market","structure":"mercatus (Latin) through Old Northern French","meaning":"a place or system of exchange","meaningCN":"交换的场所或系统","example":"Old English already used the borrowed noun.","exampleCN":"古英语已经使用这个借入的名词。"},{"word":"marketplace","structure":"market + place (compound noun)","meaning":"the physical site of trading","meaningCN":"交易的实体场所","example":"The compound keeps only the place sense.","exampleCN":"这个复合词只保留场所义。"},{"word":"marketing","structure":"market + -ing (activity noun)","meaning":"the work of promoting goods","meaningCN":"推广货物的工作","example":"Marketing grew out of the verb to market.","exampleCN":"营销由动词「行销」发展而来。"},{"word":"-ing","structure":"-ing (suffix forming verbal nouns)","meaning":"the process or activity of doing","meaningCN":"做某事的过程或活动","example":"The suffix turns the verb into a trade activity.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把动词变成一种行业活动。"},{"word":"marketable","structure":"market + -able (can be)","meaning":"able to be sold","meaningCN":"可销售的","example":"Only marketable varieties reached the stalls.","exampleCN":"只有可销售的品种被送上摊位。"},{"word":"-able","structure":"-able (suffix forming adjectives)","meaning":"capable of being","meaningCN":"能够被……的","example":"The suffix marks what can be sold.","exampleCN":"这个后缀标出能够被卖出之物。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"merx","structure":"merx, mercis (f., third declension)","meaning":"goods, merchandise","meaningCN":"货物；商品"},{"word":"mercatus","structure":"mercatus, mercatus (m., fourth declension)","meaning":"market, trading, marketplace","meaningCN":"市场；交易；集市"},{"word":"mercari","structure":"mercari, mercatus sum (deponent verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to trade, to buy and sell","meaningCN":"做交易；买卖"},{"word":"mercator","structure":"mercator, mercatoris (m., third declension)","meaning":"trader, merchant","meaningCN":"商人；交易者"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"marketing","pos":"n.","zh":"营销；行销（活动）"},{"word":"marketplace","pos":"n.","zh":"集市；市场场所"},{"word":"marketer","pos":"n.","zh":"营销人员"},{"word":"marketable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可销售的；有销路的"},{"word":"marketization","pos":"n.","zh":"市场化"}]}},{"word":"market economy","ipa_uk":"/ˌmɑːkɪt ɪˈkɒnəmi/","ipa_us":"/ˌmɑːrkɪt ɪˈkɑːnəmi/","definition_zh":"市场经济；由价格与私人自愿交易配置资源的经济体制；与计划经济相对的经济形态","definition_en":"an economic system in which prices, private ownership and voluntary exchange, rather than central directives, decide what is produced and how resources are allocated","core_image":"天没亮的集市：摊主各自写价牌，买主来回比价，没有谁在高处统一派货，价钱随人流涨落","scene":"一个城镇的早市在天还没亮时开张，摊主各自标价，买主挑拣还价，收摊时谁的货卖得动、谁的要剩下一半，全由当天的价钱决定。In a market economy, no office sets the price of bread; buyers and sellers do.","sceneCN":"早市里没有统一发号施令的人，价格由买卖双方当场议定，货物也随之流向愿出价的一方。句中的 market economy 指「由价格与私人交易配置资源的经济形态」（第 1 个义项：价格信号而非行政指令决定生产与分配）。图中可辨识物件：手写价牌、秤、零钱盒、半空的货筐。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"市场经济（指一种经济体制，通常作不可数；指多个经济体时可用复数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"transition to a market economy","zh":"向市场经济过渡"},{"phrase":"market economy status","zh":"市场经济地位"},{"phrase":"a fully fledged market economy","zh":"成熟的市场经济"},{"phrase":"market-oriented economy","zh":"市场导向型经济"},{"phrase":"the rise of the market economy","zh":"市场经济的兴起"},{"phrase":"market economy reforms","zh":"市场经济改革"},{"phrase":"in a market economy","zh":"在市场经济体中"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"market economy"},{"label":"复数","form":"market economies"},{"label":"作定语（带连字符）","form":"market-economy"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"market","pos":"n./v.","zh":"市场；买卖；推销"},{"word":"marketing","pos":"n.","zh":"营销；销售推广"},{"word":"marketable","pos":"adj.","zh":"有销路的；易于出售的"},{"word":"economic","pos":"adj.","zh":"经济的；经济学的"},{"word":"economist","pos":"n.","zh":"经济学家"},{"word":"economize","pos":"v.","zh":"节约；节省开支"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Prices, not orders, allocate resources","titleCN":"由价格而非指令配置资源的经济体制","definition":"an economic order in which relative prices guide what gets produced and who gets the output","definitionCN":"一种经济秩序，其中相对价格引导生产什么、产出归谁","example":"In a market economy, a shortage of copper shows up as a higher price rather than as a queue.","exampleCN":"在市场经济中，铜的短缺表现为价格上涨，而不是排队。","why":"market names the arena of buying and selling, and economy names the management of a household's resources; joined, they say that the arena itself does the managing.","whyCN":"market 指买卖的场所，economy 指对家计资源的管理；两者相接，等于说「管理」这件事由买卖场所本身来完成。"},{"no":"02","title":"Private ownership as the default","titleCN":"以私人产权为默认前提的经济","definition":"an economy in which the means of production are mostly held privately and can be bought or sold","definitionCN":"生产资料主要由私人持有、可以买卖的经济","example":"A market economy presupposes that factories and farmland have owners who may sell them.","exampleCN":"市场经济的前提是工厂与农田有可以出售它们的所有者。","why":"exchange requires something exchangeable, so the phrase carries private title to productive assets as part of its meaning rather than as an afterthought.","whyCN":"交换需要可交换之物，因此这个短语把生产性资产的私人所有权当作自身含义的一部分，而非附加条件。"},{"no":"03","title":"The destination of post-socialist reform","titleCN":"转轨国家改革的目标形态","definition":"the endpoint that former command economies were said to be moving toward after price controls were lifted","definitionCN":"价格管制解除后，原指令型经济体被称说正在走向的终点","example":"The country declared its intention to build a market economy within ten years.","exampleCN":"该国宣布打算在十年内建成市场经济。","why":"the phrase became a programme in the late twentieth century, when it named not a description but a direction of travel for states leaving central planning.","whyCN":"二十世纪后期，这个短语成了一个纲领：它不再描述现状，而是给离开中央计划的国家指出方向。"},{"no":"04","title":"A legal status in trade disputes","titleCN":"贸易争端中的法律地位认定","definition":"a finding that a country's prices and costs are set by the market, which affects how anti-dumping duties are calculated","definitionCN":"认定一国的价格与成本由市场决定，从而影响反倾销税的计算方式","example":"The exporters argued that their home market was a market economy and that domestic prices should be used as the benchmark.","exampleCN":"出口商主张其国内市场属于市场经济，应以国内价格作为基准。","why":"trade law turned the abstract phrase into a testable label, because the benchmark used in duty calculations depends on whether prices are market-determined.","whyCN":"贸易法把这个抽象短语变成一个可认定的标签，因为计税基准取决于价格是否由市场决定。"},{"no":"05","title":"The market-run half of a mixed system","titleCN":"混合体制中以市场运作的那一部分","definition":"the portion of a mixed system in which firms trade freely, as distinct from the state-run portion","definitionCN":"混合体制中企业与市场自由交易的部分，与国营部分相区别","example":"Even in a mixed system, the market economy covers most retail trade and nearly all farming.","exampleCN":"即使在混合体制中，市场经济也覆盖了大部分零售与几乎所有农业。","why":"the same phrase can be read partitively, naming a slice of an economy rather than the whole of it, which is why it appears beside state sectors.","whyCN":"这个短语也可作部分读，指一个经济体中被市场运作的一块，而非整体，因此它会与国营部门并提。"},{"no":"06","title":"A political label for capitalism","titleCN":"政治话语中对资本主义秩序的代称","definition":"a rhetorical name for a capitalist order, used to praise or to attack it rather than to describe it neutrally","definitionCN":"对资本主义秩序的一种修辞性称呼，用于褒扬或攻击，而非中立描述","example":"The speech praised the market economy as the only road to prosperity.","exampleCN":"演讲称赞市场经济是通往繁荣的唯一道路。","why":"once the phrase entered political argument it acquired a tone, so speakers use it to signal approval of private enterprise or to name an opponent.","whyCN":"这个短语一旦进入政治论辩便带上了色彩：说话者用它表示赞同私营企业，或用来指称对手。"},{"no":"07","title":"A reform package of liberalisation steps","titleCN":"由自由化措施组成的改革方案","definition":"the bundle of measures, such as price liberalisation, privatisation and subsidy cuts, that are meant to create such a system","definitionCN":"价格放开、私有化、削减补贴等一整套旨在建立该体制的措施","example":"Building a market economy required freeing prices, selling state plants and ending cheap credit.","exampleCN":"建立市场经济需要放开价格、出售国营工厂并停止廉价信贷。","why":"because the phrase named a goal, it came to stand for the steps taken toward it, and that bundle is now what officials mean by the term.","whyCN":"因为短语指称一个目标，它也渐渐指称通往目标所采取的步骤，官员说到这个词时指的往往就是那套措施。"},{"no":"08","title":"An ideal type in economic theory","titleCN":"经济理论中的理想类型","definition":"an analytical model in which all allocation is assumed to run through prices, with institutions and politics abstracted away","definitionCN":"一种分析模型，假设全部配置都经价格进行，把制度与政治抽象掉","example":"The textbook treats a market economy as a model in which every actor responds to the same price signal.","exampleCN":"教科书把市场经济当作一个所有行动者都对同一价格信号作出反应的模型。","why":"theory needs a clean benchmark, so the phrase also names a simplified construct rather than any observable country.","whyCN":"理论需要一个干净的基准，因此这个短语也指一个简化的构造，而非任何可观察的国家。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Market economy joins two borrowings: market goes back to Latin mercatus, the noun of trading, while economy goes back to Greek oikonomia, the management of a household, which reached English through Latin oeconomia. The compound itself is a twentieth-century term of political economy.","cn":"market economy 由两个借词拼成：market 出自拉丁 mercatus「交易、市场」，economy 出自希腊 oikonomia「家计管理」，后者经拉丁 oeconomia 进入英语。短语本身是二十世纪政治经济学的术语。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MERCATUS","en":"Mercatus meant a market and the business done there. It came from the verb mercari 'to trade', which in turn rests on the noun merx (genitive mercis) 'goods, merchandise'. The deeper origin of merx is uncertain, and any older form proposed for it is a reconstruction.","cn":"mercatus 指市场以及在那里进行的买卖，出自动词 mercari「做买卖」，而该动词又基于名词 merx（属格 mercis）「货物」。merx 的更早来源不确定，凡为其提出的更古形式均属重构形式。"},{"era":"LATIN MERCARI","en":"Mercari 'to buy and sell' supplied mercatus, which passed through Old North French into English as market, first naming a place of trade and later the demand for a good.","cn":"mercari「买卖」提供了 mercatus，后者经古北法语进入英语作 market，最初指交易场所，后来也指对某种货物的需求。"},{"era":"GREEK OIKONOMIA","en":"Oikonomia combined oikos 'house, household' with nemein 'to distribute, to manage', so it named the running of a household and its stores. The deeper history of nemein is debated, and proposed Indo-European links are reconstructions.","cn":"oikonomia 由 oikos「家宅」与 nemein「分配、管理」合成，指料理家宅与家中储备。nemein 的更早历史有争论，所提出的印欧语关联属重构形式。"},{"era":"LATIN OECONOMIA","en":"Latin took the Greek word as oeconomia. English economy entered in the sixteenth century meaning household management, and by the eighteenth century it meant the ordered system of a state's wealth and production.","cn":"拉丁语以 oeconomia 借入这个希腊词。英语 economy 于十六世纪进入，意为家计管理；到十八世纪，它指一国财富与生产的有序体系。"},{"era":"TWENTIETH-CENTURY COMPOUND","en":"The full phrase was coined in the twentieth century as the counterpart of planned economy and command economy, and it became standard in development policy and in comparisons of economic systems.","cn":"完整短语在二十世纪被造出，作为「计划经济」「指令经济」的对应说法，随后在发展政策与各种经济体制比较中成为标准用语。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain: the pre-Latin origin of merx and the early sense of nemein are unsettled, and no single first citation for the English compound is established, so an earlier date sometimes given is a reconstruction.","cn":"来源不确定：merx 在拉丁语之前的来源与 nemein 的早期含义均无定论，英语复合短语也没有公认的最早书证，因此有时给出的更早年代属于重构。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds phrases that share a word with the target and are routinely mistaken for it; group two holds systems that lie close in meaning but differ over who owns the assets and who does the deciding.","cn":"第一组是与目标短语共用某个词、因而常被混用的说法；第二组是含义相近、但在「谁拥有资产」与「谁作决定」上不同的体制。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"market economics","ipa":"/ˌmɑːkɪt ɪˈkɒnəmɪks/","tag":"a subject, not a system","definition":"The name of an academic field that studies how markets behave; a country cannot build it, and it is not the economy itself.","definitionCN":"一门研究市场如何运作的学科名称；国家无法「建成」它，它也不是经济本身。"},{"word":"marketization","ipa":"/ˌmɑːkɪtɪˈzeɪʃn/","tag":"a process","definition":"The act of making a service or asset run through markets, such as housing or electricity; it names a change, whereas the target names a settled order.","definitionCN":"把某项服务或资产改为经市场运作的过程，如住房或电力；它指变化，而目标词指一种成形秩序。"},{"word":"marketplace","ipa":"/ˈmɑːkɪtpleɪs/","tag":"the venue itself","definition":"The square or website where trade happens; it is only the arena, not the ownership and legal order around it.","definitionCN":"买卖发生的广场或网站；它只是场所，不含围绕它的产权与法律秩序。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"free market","ipa":"/ˌfriː ˈmɑːkɪt/","tag":"least state interference","definition":"A market left almost alone by the state; a market economy may still be heavily regulated, so the two are not interchangeable.","definitionCN":"几乎不受国家干预的市场；市场经济仍可受到严格监管，因此两者不能互换。"},{"word":"capitalist economy","ipa":"/ˌkæpɪtəlɪst ɪˈkɒnəmi/","tag":"ownership focus","definition":"Names the system by who owns the assets rather than by how prices coordinate, shifting the emphasis onto property.","definitionCN":"按「谁拥有资产」而非「价格如何协调」来命名该体制，重点落在产权上。"},{"word":"mixed economy","ipa":"/ˌmɪkst ɪˈkɒnəmi/","tag":"public plus private","definition":"A system in which state and market sectors coexist; it is the ordinary compromise, not the textbook model.","definitionCN":"国家部门与市场部门并存的经济体制；它是常见的折中形态，而非教科书模型。"},{"word":"price system","ipa":"/ˈpraɪs ˌsɪstəm/","tag":"mechanism only","definition":"Names just the network of prices that carries information; it says nothing about ownership, law or policy.","definitionCN":"只指传递信息的整套价格；它对产权、法律与政策不置一词。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real components, real fixed phrases and real historical contrast, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实固定搭配与真实的历史对立，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"Market goes back to Latin mercatus 'a place of trading', which rests on merx 'goods': the word for the goods also gave the word for the place.","cn":"market 上溯拉丁 mercatus「交易场所」，而它基于 merx「货物」：指货物的词同时也给出了指场所的词。"},{"en":"Economy goes back to Greek oikonomia, oikos 'house' plus nemein 'to manage': the word began as the running of a household.","cn":"economy 上溯希腊 oikonomia，由 oikos「家宅」与 nemein「管理」构成：这个词最初指料理家计。"},{"en":"The phrase was built as the opposite of planned economy, so it always drags a comparison along with it.","cn":"这个短语是作为「计划经济」的对立面造出的，因此它总带着一层比较的意味。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the reform sense: transition to a market economy, market economy status, market economy reforms.","cn":"固定搭配标出改革义：向市场经济过渡、市场经济地位、市场经济改革。"},{"en":"Market also names demand itself, as in a market for used cars, which ties the arena to the appetite behind it.","cn":"market 也指需求本身，如二手车市场，这把「场所」与背后的需求连在一起。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a town where every stall writes its own price and nobody in an office upstairs issues a quota.","cn":"想象一个镇上每个摊位自己写价，楼上没有哪间办公室在派定额。"},{"en":"Picture a household budget enlarged to the size of a country: that is the household word hidden inside economy.","cn":"想象一本家用的账本被放大到一国的规模：这就是藏在 economy 里的那个「家」字。"},{"en":"Picture two diagrams side by side, one with arrows from a centre and one with arrows between traders; the phrase names the second.","cn":"想象两张并排的图：一张箭头从中心发出，一张箭头在买卖者之间穿梭；这个短语指的是后一张。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"A market economy allocates goods through prices that move as supply and demand change.","cn":"市场经济通过随供求变化而变动的价格来配置货物。"},{"en":"After the price controls were lifted, the country moved toward a market economy within a decade.","cn":"价格管制取消后，该国在十年内走向市场经济。"},{"en":"Compared with a planned system, a market economy differs less in technology than in who may set a price.","cn":"与计划体制相比，市场经济的差别不在技术，而在谁有权定价。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「market（集市）+ economy（经济）」——摊位自己写价、买卖自己成交，一整国的买卖都照集市的样子运转，就是市场经济。","word":"market economy"},"root":"拉丁 mercatus「市场、交易」← 动词 mercari「做买卖」← 名词 merx（属格 mercis）「货物」；希腊 oikonomia「家计管理」= oikos「家宅」+ nemein「分配、管理」，经拉丁 oeconomia 入英语；短语为二十世纪政治经济学术语，与计划经济相对。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses radiate from one picture: an arena that sets its own prices is scaled up until it runs a whole economy, and that picture is then turned into a reform goal, a legal label, a sector, a slogan, a policy bundle and finally a textbook model.","cn":"八个义项从一个画面辐射开来：一个自己定价的买卖场所被放大到能运转整个经济体，这个画面随后被依次当作改革目标、法律标签、部门、口号、政策组合，最后成为教科书模型。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a morning market where each stall posts a price and the crowd, not an office, decides what sells.","cn":"核心意象：清早的集市，每个摊位自己挂牌，决定货物卖不卖得动的是人流，而不是哪间办公室。"},"chain":["PRICE ARENA","HOUSEHOLD MANAGEMENT","PRICE SIGNAL","PRIVATE TITLE","REFORM GOAL","IDEAL TYPE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"MARKET AS MANAGER: the arena takes over the household's job, and it can only do so if the assets have owners who may sell.","cn":"市场当家：买卖场所接管了「理家」的活，而它要能做到这一点，资产必须有可以出售的所有者。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"FROM GOAL TO LABEL: leaving central planning turns the phrase into a destination, and trade law turns it into a status to be granted or refused.","cn":"从目标到标签：离开中央计划使这个短语成为终点，贸易法则使它成为一项可授予也可拒绝的地位。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"PART AND SLOGAN: the same words can name one sector of a mixed system or serve as a flag in political argument.","cn":"部分与口号：同一串词既可指混合体制中的一个部门，也可在政治论辩中充当旗帜。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE STEPS: because the phrase named a goal, it came to mean the liberalising measures taken to reach it.","cn":"步骤：因为短语指称目标，它也转而指为达到目标而采取的自由化措施。"},{"senses":"08","en":"THE MODEL: theory strips away law and politics to leave a benchmark in which price alone coordinates.","cn":"模型：理论剥去法律与政治，只留下一个仅由价格协调的基准。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase can be read as two morpheme chains: a Latin root for trade that supplies market and its family, and a Greek compound for household management that supplies economy and its family.","cn":"这个短语可以按两条语素链读：一条是拉丁的「交易」词根，提供 market 及其词族；一条是希腊的「家计管理」复合词，提供 economy 及其词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin merx and mercari give market, merchant and commerce; Greek oikos and nemein, taken into Latin as oeconomia, give economy, economic and economist.","cn":"拉丁 merx 与 mercari 衍生 market、merchant 与 commerce；希腊 oikos 与 nemein 经拉丁 oeconomia 衍生 economy、economic 与 economist。"},"items":[{"word":"merc-","structure":"Latin root in merx, mercis (goods)","meaning":"goods, merchandise","meaningCN":"货物；商品","example":"The root also appears in commerce and merchant.","exampleCN":"这个词根也出现在 commerce 与 merchant 中。"},{"word":"mercatus","structure":"mercatus (Latin noun, fourth declension)","meaning":"market, trading","meaningCN":"市场；交易","example":"Mercatus named both the place and the dealing done there.","exampleCN":"mercatus 既指场所，也指在那里进行的买卖。"},{"word":"-atus","structure":"suffix forming nouns from verbs","meaning":"the act or the result of an act","meaningCN":"动作或其结果","example":"Mercari plus the suffix yields the noun mercatus.","exampleCN":"mercari 加上这个后缀得到名词 mercatus。"},{"word":"oikos","structure":"Greek root, 'house, household'","meaning":"a house and everyone in it","meaningCN":"家宅以及家中的所有人","example":"Oikos is the first element of the Greek compound.","exampleCN":"oikos 是这个希腊复合词的第一部分。"},{"word":"nemein","structure":"Greek verb, 'to distribute, to manage'","meaning":"to allot and to run","meaningCN":"分配；料理","example":"Nemein supplies the managing half of the compound.","exampleCN":"nemein 提供这个复合词中「管理」的那一半。"},{"word":"-ia","structure":"suffix forming abstract nouns","meaning":"a state or an activity","meaningCN":"状态或活动","example":"Nemein plus the suffix produces the abstract noun.","exampleCN":"nemein 加上这个后缀构成抽象名词。"},{"word":"oikonomia","structure":"oikos + nemein + -ia","meaning":"household management","meaningCN":"家计管理","example":"Oikonomia meant household management long before it meant national wealth.","exampleCN":"oikonomia 在指国家财富之前很久就已指家计管理。"},{"word":"economy","structure":"Latin oeconomia, taken from Greek","meaning":"the management of resources, then a national system","meaningCN":"资源管理；后指一国经济体系","example":"Economy moved from the household to the nation.","exampleCN":"economy 从家宅走向了国家。"},{"word":"economic","structure":"economy + -ic (relating to)","meaning":"relating to the production and use of wealth","meaningCN":"与财富的生产和使用有关的","example":"The adjective describes what belongs to the system.","exampleCN":"这个形容词描述属于该体系的事物。"},{"word":"economical","structure":"economic + -al (having the character of)","meaning":"sparing, avoiding waste","meaningCN":"节省的；不浪费的","example":"Economical warns against waste, unlike economic.","exampleCN":"economical 提示不要浪费，这一点与 economic 不同。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"merx","structure":"merx, mercis (f., third declension)","meaning":"goods, merchandise","meaningCN":"货物；商品"},{"word":"mercari","structure":"mercari, mercatus sum (deponent verb, first conjugation)","meaning":"to trade, to buy and sell","meaningCN":"做买卖；交易"},{"word":"mercatus","structure":"mercatus, mercatus (m., fourth declension)","meaning":"market, trading","meaningCN":"市场；交易"},{"word":"oeconomia","structure":"oeconomia, oeconomiae (f., first declension, from Greek)","meaning":"household management","meaningCN":"家计管理"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"market","pos":"n./v.","zh":"市场；推销"},{"word":"marketing","pos":"n.","zh":"营销；销售推广"},{"word":"marketable","pos":"adj.","zh":"有销路的"},{"word":"economic","pos":"adj.","zh":"经济的"},{"word":"economist","pos":"n.","zh":"经济学家"},{"word":"economical","pos":"adj.","zh":"节约的；节省的"}]}},{"word":"market structure","ipa_uk":"/ˈmɑːkɪt ˈstrʌktʃə/","ipa_us":"/ˈmɑːrkɪt ˈstrʌktʃər/","definition_zh":"市场结构；市场中卖者的数量与规模分布，连同进入壁垒和产品差异所构成的整体格局；产业组织理论的核心术语","definition_en":"the pattern formed by the number and size distribution of sellers in a market, together with the height of entry barriers and the degree of product differentiation","core_image":"一张街区俯视图：几处摊位占地悬殊，大铺占去大半街面，小摊挤在边角，街口还横着一道进场要先交钱的栏门","scene":"一条商业街刚划好摊位，几家大铺占去大半街面，小摊只能挤在边角，街口还立着一道进场要先交钱的栏门，谁进得来、谁占得宽，一眼就能看出。Economists use the term market structure to describe this layout of sellers.","sceneCN":"同一条街上，卖者的数量、各自占地的宽窄、进场的门槛高低，合起来构成一幅可比的格局。句中的 market structure 指「卖者数量与规模分布连同进入壁垒所形成的格局」（第 1 个义项：卖者构成与规模分布的整体形态）。图中可辨识物件：摊位俯视图、占地界线、门槛、价目牌。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"市场结构（指格局与形态，可数；不同产业各有其结构）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"market structure analysis","zh":"市场结构分析"},{"phrase":"a concentrated market structure","zh":"集中型市场结构"},{"phrase":"a fragmented market structure","zh":"分散型市场结构"},{"phrase":"the market structure of an industry","zh":"某一产业的市场结构"},{"phrase":"changes in market structure","zh":"市场结构的变化"},{"phrase":"market structure and conduct","zh":"市场结构与市场行为"},{"phrase":"reshape the market structure","zh":"重塑市场结构"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"market structure"},{"label":"复数","form":"market structures"},{"label":"作定语（带连字符）","form":"market-structure"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"structure","pos":"n./v.","zh":"结构；构造；组织"},{"word":"structural","pos":"adj.","zh":"结构的；结构性的"},{"word":"structurally","pos":"adv.","zh":"在结构上"},{"word":"restructuring","pos":"n.","zh":"重组；结构调整"},{"word":"structured","pos":"adj.","zh":"有组织的；分层的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"How many sellers, and how big","titleCN":"卖者的数量与规模分布","definition":"the count of firms serving a market and the range of sizes among them","definitionCN":"为同一市场供货的厂商数目，以及它们规模大小的分布","example":"A market structure with two hundred small bakeries differs sharply from one with three large mills.","exampleCN":"两百个小面包坊构成的市场结构，与三家大磨坊构成的结构截然不同。","why":"structure means the way parts are put together, so the phrase first asks what parts a market contains and how much room each occupies.","whyCN":"structure 指各部分被组合起来的方式，因此这个短语首先问的是：一个市场由哪些部分组成，每一部分占多大位置。"},{"no":"02","title":"Concentration of market share","titleCN":"份额向少数厂商集中的程度","definition":"the share of the market held by the largest firms, and whether that share is spread or piled up","definitionCN":"最大几家厂商所占的份额，以及该份额是分散还是堆积在一处","example":"The market structure is highly concentrated, with four firms holding most of the sales.","exampleCN":"该市场结构高度集中，四家厂商握有大部分销量。","why":"once the sizes are known, the next structural question is how they add up: a few large blocks or many small ones make different shapes.","whyCN":"一旦知道规模，下一个结构问题便是它们如何加总：几块大石与一堆小石形成不同的形状。"},{"no":"03","title":"The height of entry barriers","titleCN":"进入壁垒的高低","definition":"the cost, legal obstacle or technical requirement that a newcomer must meet to start selling","definitionCN":"新来者要开始销售必须跨过的成本、法律障碍或技术要求","example":"Licensing rules and a costly pipeline give the incumbents a market structure that few challengers can enter.","exampleCN":"执照规则与昂贵的管线成本，使在位者拥有一个少有挑战者能进入的市场结构。","why":"a structure is held up by walls as much as by contents, and the wall around a market is the barrier that keeps new sellers out.","whyCN":"结构的维持既靠内容也靠围墙，而市场周围的围墙就是挡住新卖者的壁垒。"},{"no":"04","title":"The degree of product differentiation","titleCN":"产品差异化的程度","definition":"how far rival sellers offer goods that buyers treat as distinct rather than interchangeable","definitionCN":"相互竞争的卖者所提供的货物，被买方视为有区别而非可互换的程度","example":"Branding gives shampoo a market structure in which each label is a separate niche.","exampleCN":"品牌化使洗发水形成一种市场结构，每个标签都是一个独立的细分位。","why":"differentiation changes the shape of a market because a market of identical goods behaves like one block, while a market of distinct goods behaves like many.","whyCN":"差异化会改变市场的形状，因为同质货物市场如同一整块，而彼此有别的货物市场则像许多块。"},{"no":"05","title":"A type in the competition typology","titleCN":"按竞争程度划分的类型标签","definition":"a category such as perfect competition, oligopoly or monopoly assigned to a market by its seller pattern","definitionCN":"依据卖者格局给市场指定的类别，如完全竞争、寡头或垄断","example":"Textbooks label the airline market structure as an oligopoly because a few carriers dominate each route.","exampleCN":"教科书把航空市场结构标为寡头，因为每条航线都由少数承运者主导。","why":"because the phrase describes a shape, it became the name of a shelf of shapes, and each shelf is a textbook type rather than a single case.","whyCN":"因为这个短语描述形状，它便成了存放各种形状的架子名，每一格都是一类教科书类型，而非单一实例。"},{"no":"06","title":"An index used in merger review","titleCN":"合并审查中可测量的指标","definition":"a measurable summary of seller shares, such as a concentration ratio, used by regulators to judge a proposed merger","definitionCN":"对卖者份额的可测概括，如集中率，供监管机构评判拟议合并","example":"Regulators computed the post-merger market structure before allowing the deal.","exampleCN":"监管机构先算出合并后的市场结构，才允许这笔交易。","why":"competition law needs a number rather than a diagram, so the phrase shifted from a description of shape to a statistic that can be computed.","whyCN":"竞争法需要数字而非图样，于是这个短语从「形状描述」转为「可计算的统计量」。"},{"no":"07","title":"A shape that changes over time","titleCN":"随时间演变的格局","definition":"the shifting pattern produced by entry, exit, mergers and consolidation within a market","definitionCN":"由进入、退出、合并与整合在市场内造成的变化着的格局","example":"Deregulation altered the market structure as new carriers entered and older ones merged.","exampleCN":"放松管制改变了市场结构：新承运者进入，旧承运者合并。","why":"the phrase can name a process as well as a snapshot, since the arrangement of sellers is never fixed and consolidation keeps redrawing it.","whyCN":"这个短语既可指名一个瞬间，也可指名一个过程，因为卖者的排列从不固定，整合不断把它重画。"},{"no":"08","title":"A layered pattern in platform markets","titleCN":"平台市场中的分层格局","definition":"the arrangement of a platform market into layers, where the owner of the interface and the data sits above the sellers who depend on it","definitionCN":"平台市场分成若干层的排列方式：掌握接口与数据的所有者居于依赖它的卖者之上","example":"A marketplace app creates a market structure in which thousands of sellers depend on one ranking system.","exampleCN":"一个集市应用造出一种市场结构，成千上万的卖者依赖同一套排序系统。","why":"structure can also mean the layering of levels, so the phrase extends naturally to markets where one firm controls the layer through which all trade passes.","whyCN":"structure 也可指层次的叠加，因此这个短语自然延伸到「一家公司掌管所有交易必须穿过的那个层」的市场。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Market structure joins a Latin trade noun to a Latin building noun. Market goes back to mercatus, a place of trading built on merx 'goods'; structure goes back to structura, a fitting together, from struere 'to pile up, to build'.","cn":"market structure 把一个拉丁的「交易」名词与一个拉丁的「建造」名词接在一起。market 上溯 mercatus「交易场所」，基于 merx「货物」；structure 上溯 structura「拼合、构造」，出自 struere「堆叠、建造」。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MERCATUS","en":"Mercatus named a market and the trading done in it, formed from mercari 'to trade', which rests on merx (genitive mercis) 'goods'. The deeper origin of merx is uncertain, and older forms proposed for it are reconstructions.","cn":"mercatus 指市场及其中进行的买卖，出自动词 mercari「做买卖」，而该动词基于 merx（属格 mercis）「货物」。merx 的更早来源不确定，为它提出的更古形式属重构形式。"},{"era":"LATIN STRUERE","en":"Struere meant 'to pile up, to build, to arrange in order'. It is generally thought to descend from a root meaning 'to spread out', but that earlier form is a reconstruction rather than a recorded word.","cn":"struere 意为「堆叠、建造、按序排列」。一般认为它源自表示「铺展开」的词根，但那个更早的形式是重构形式，并非有记录的词。"},{"era":"LATIN STRUCTURA","en":"Structura, from struere, meant the act of building and the arrangement that results, as when stones are laid in a deliberate order rather than heaped at random.","cn":"structura 出自 struere，指建造的动作以及由此形成的排列，就像石头被有意按序砌起，而非随意堆放。"},{"era":"ENGLISH STRUCTURE","en":"English took structure through Old French in the fourteenth century, first as the process of building and later as the internal arrangement of parts in a body, a sentence or a society.","cn":"英语于十四世纪经古法语借入 structure，最初指建造过程，后来指身体、句子或社会中各部分的内部排列。"},{"era":"INDUSTRIAL ORGANIZATION","en":"The full phrase took shape in twentieth-century industrial organization, where the arrangement of sellers was linked to their conduct and to the results a market delivers.","cn":"完整短语在二十世纪的产业组织理论中成形，在那里，卖者的排列被与它们的行为以及市场所交付的结果联系起来。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain: the pre-Latin root of struere is unsettled, and the exact first use of the English phrase is not established, so any earlier citation offered for it is a reconstruction.","cn":"来源不确定：struere 在拉丁语之前的词根无定论，英语短语的确切首见年代亦无定说，因此为它给出的更早书证均属重构。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one shares the word market and is often mistaken for the target; group two names related aspects of the same industrial landscape but at a different level of analysis.","cn":"第一组共用 market 一词，常被误当作目标短语；第二组指同一产业图景中的相关侧面，但分析层次不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"market segmentation","ipa":"/ˌmɑːkɪt ˌseɡmenˈteɪʃn/","tag":"buyers, not sellers","definition":"The splitting of customers into groups with shared traits; it describes demand and marketing, not the number and size of sellers.","definitionCN":"把顾客按共同特征分成若干群；它描述需求与营销，而非卖者的数量与规模。"},{"word":"market mechanism","ipa":"/ˌmɑːkɪt ˈmekənɪzəm/","tag":"how it works","definition":"The way prices and signals coordinate buyers and sellers; it explains the working of a market, not its shape.","definitionCN":"价格与信号协调买卖的方式；它解释市场的运作，而非市场的形状。"},{"word":"market share","ipa":"/ˌmɑːkɪt ˈʃeə/","tag":"one figure inside it","definition":"The portion of sales held by a single firm; it is one measurement used to describe the target, not the target itself.","definitionCN":"单一厂商所占的销量比例；它是描述目标格局的一项测量，而非格局本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"industrial structure","ipa":"/ɪnˈdʌstriəl ˈstrʌktʃə/","tag":"whole economy, by sector","definition":"The mix of agriculture, manufacturing and services across an economy; it works one level above the arrangement of sellers in a single market.","definitionCN":"一个经济体中农业、制造业与服务业的构成；它比单一市场内卖者的排列高一个层次。"},{"word":"industry concentration","ipa":"/ˈɪndəstri ˌkɒnsnˈtreɪʃn/","tag":"one dimension only","definition":"The degree to which output is gathered in a few firms; it measures the second dimension of the target while leaving barriers and differentiation aside.","definitionCN":"产出集中于少数厂商的程度；它只测量目标格局中的第二个维度，搁下壁垒与差异化。"},{"word":"market power","ipa":"/ˌmɑːkɪt ˈpaʊə/","tag":"a consequence","definition":"The ability of a firm to raise price without losing all its customers; it is what a given arrangement allows, not the arrangement.","definitionCN":"厂商提价而不失去全部顾客的能力；它是某种格局所容许的结果，而非格局本身。"},{"word":"entry barrier","ipa":"/ˈentri ˈbæriə/","tag":"one component","definition":"A single obstacle that keeps newcomers out; it is one ingredient of the target rather than the whole pattern.","definitionCN":"阻挡新来者的单项障碍；它是目标格局中的一味成分，而非整个形态。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the real building root behind structure, real relatives and real textbook labels.","cn":"正常联想：structure 背后真实的「建造」词根、真实同族词以及真实的教科书标签。"},"normal":[{"en":"Structure comes from struere 'to pile up, to build': stones laid in a deliberate order, not heaped at random.","cn":"structure 出自 struere「堆叠、建造」：石头被有意按序砌起，而不是随意堆成一堆。"},{"en":"The same root builds construct, instruct, obstruct and infrastructure, all of which carry an idea of putting parts together.","cn":"同一词根还构成 construct、instruct、obstruct 与 infrastructure，这些词都带「把部分拼起来」的意思。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the dimensions: concentrated market structure, fragmented market structure, market structure analysis.","cn":"固定搭配标出各个维度：集中型市场结构、分散型市场结构、市场结构分析。"},{"en":"The textbook shelf holds perfect competition, oligopoly and monopoly, and each is a type of market structure.","cn":"教科书那一格放着完全竞争、寡头与垄断，每一种都是一个市场结构类型。"},{"en":"The old triad links structure to conduct and to performance, so the shape is studied for what it makes firms do.","cn":"旧有的三段式把结构、行为与绩效连在一起，研究形状是为了看它促使厂商做什么。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture an aerial photo of a market district: two warehouses, a row of kiosks and a gate at the only road in.","cn":"想象一张市场街区的俯拍：两座仓库、一排小亭，以及唯一一条进路上的一道门。"},{"en":"Picture a handful of large stones dropped into a jar of gravel: the same total weight, but a very different shape.","cn":"想象几块大石落进一罐碎石：总重一样，形状却全然不同。"},{"en":"Picture a stadium where one owner controls the gate, the seating chart and the list of who may sell snacks inside.","cn":"想象一座体育场，同一个人掌管入口、座位表以及谁能在场内卖零食的名单。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The market structure of the region is fragmented, with no firm holding more than a tenth of sales.","cn":"该地区的市场结构是分散的，没有一家厂商的销量超过一成。"},{"en":"Before approving the merger, the authority asked how the deal would change the market structure.","cn":"在批准合并之前，主管机关询问这笔交易将如何改变市场结构。"},{"en":"Over three decades, deregulation and consolidation reshaped the market structure of the industry.","cn":"三十年间，放松管制与整合重塑了该产业的市场结构。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「market（市场）+ structure（结构）」——把集市画成一张俯视图，看几个摊位、各占多宽、门口有没有门槛，这张图就是市场结构。","word":"market structure"},"root":"拉丁 mercatus「市场、交易」← mercari「做买卖」← merx（属格 mercis）「货物」；拉丁 structura「建造、构造」← struere「堆叠、建造」；英语于十四世纪经古法语借入 structure，短语为二十世纪产业组织理论术语。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one act of drawing: first count the sellers and weigh their sizes, then ask how the shares pile up, what wall keeps newcomers out and how unlike the goods are; the drawing is then given a textbook name, turned into an index, replayed as a film of change and finally extended to the layered architecture of a platform.","cn":"八个义项沿一次「作图」展开：先数卖者、量大小，再问份额如何堆积、什么墙挡住新来者、货物彼此有多不同；这张图随后被赋予教科书名称、被折算成指标、被当作变化的过程重放，最后延伸到平台的分层架构。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a bird's-eye plan of a market district, showing how many stalls there are, how much ground each holds and where the gate stands.","cn":"核心意象：一张市场街区的俯视图，标出有多少摊位、各自占多宽的地面、门开在哪里。"},"chain":["SELLER COUNT","SHARE PILE","ENTRY WALL","PRODUCT DISTINCTION","TEXTBOOK TYPE","LAYERED PLATFORM"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"WHO AND HOW MUCH: the number of sellers and the way their shares stack up are the first two lines of the drawing.","cn":"谁与多少：卖者的数量与份额的堆叠方式，是这张图最先画的两笔。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"WALLS AND DIFFERENCES: barriers fix who can enter, while differentiation decides whether buyers see one block or many.","cn":"围墙与差异：壁垒决定谁能进来，差异化决定买方看到的是一整块还是许多块。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"NAME AND NUMBER: the same drawing is filed under a textbook type and then reduced to a computable index.","cn":"名称与数字：同一张图先被归入某个教科书类型，再被约简为可计算的指标。"},{"senses":"07","en":"TIME: entry, exit and merger keep redrawing the plan, so the structure is also a process.","cn":"时间：进入、退出与合并不断重画这张图，因此结构同时是一个过程。"},{"senses":"08","en":"LAYERS: in a platform market the drawing gains a storey, and the owner of that storey sits above every seller.","cn":"层次：在平台市场中，这张图多出一层，而那一层的所有者居于所有卖者之上。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase is two Latin nouns glued together in English: a trade noun ending in -atus and a building noun ending in -ura, each with its own small family.","cn":"这个短语是两个拉丁名词在英语中的并置：一个带 -atus 后缀的交易名词，一个带 -ura 后缀的建造名词，各自带着自己的小词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin struere and structura stand behind structure and its relatives; mercatus and merx stand behind market and merchant.","cn":"拉丁 struere 与 structura 在后，衍生 structure 及其亲属词；mercatus 与 merx 在后，衍生 market 与 merchant。"},"items":[{"word":"merc-","structure":"Latin root in merx, mercis (goods)","meaning":"goods, merchandise","meaningCN":"货物；商品","example":"The root survives in commerce and merchant as well as market.","exampleCN":"这个词根除 market 外，还留存于 commerce 与 merchant。"},{"word":"-atus","structure":"suffix forming a noun of act or result","meaning":"the doing of something, or its outcome","meaningCN":"动作的进行，或动作的结果","example":"Mercari plus the suffix gives mercatus, the trading.","exampleCN":"mercari 加这个后缀得到 mercatus，即买卖这件事。"},{"word":"stru-","structure":"Latin root in struere, 'to pile up, build'","meaning":"to lay in order, to build","meaningCN":"按序铺设；建造","example":"The root carries the picture of stones stacked in rows.","exampleCN":"这个词根带着「石头成排砌起」的画面。"},{"word":"struere","structure":"struere (Latin verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to build, arrange, equip","meaningCN":"建造；排列；装备","example":"Struere supplies both the building and the arranging sense.","exampleCN":"struere 同时提供「建造」与「排列」两层意思。"},{"word":"-ura","structure":"suffix forming a noun of result","meaning":"the thing produced by an act","meaningCN":"动作所产生之物","example":"Struere plus the suffix yields structura, a built arrangement.","exampleCN":"struere 加这个后缀得到 structura，即被建成的排列。"},{"word":"structura","structure":"struere + -ura","meaning":"a building, a fitting together","meaningCN":"建筑；拼合而成的构造","example":"Structura named both the act of building and its result.","exampleCN":"structura 既指建造的动作，也指其结果。"},{"word":"structure","structure":"structura through Old French","meaning":"the arrangement of parts","meaningCN":"各部分的排列方式","example":"Structure moved from building work to the plan of any whole.","exampleCN":"structure 从建造工程转指任何整体的构成。"},{"word":"structural","structure":"structure + -al (relating to)","meaning":"belonging to the arrangement itself","meaningCN":"属于排列本身的；结构的","example":"Structural flaws cannot be fixed by painting over them.","exampleCN":"结构性的缺陷无法靠刷一层漆来修补。"},{"word":"construct","structure":"con- (together) + struere","meaning":"to build by putting parts together","meaningCN":"把部分拼合起来建造","example":"The same root builds, and so the verb means to put together.","exampleCN":"同一词根意为建造，因此这个动词意为拼合。"},{"word":"restructuring","structure":"re- (again) + structure + -ing","meaning":"the act of arranging again","meaningCN":"重新安排的动作；重组","example":"The restructuring closed two plants and merged the sales teams.","exampleCN":"重组关掉两家工厂，并合并了销售团队。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"struere","structure":"struere, struxi, structum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to pile up, build, arrange","meaningCN":"堆叠；建造；排列"},{"word":"structura","structure":"structura, structurae (f., first declension)","meaning":"a building, a construction","meaningCN":"建筑；构造"},{"word":"mercatus","structure":"mercatus, mercatus (m., fourth declension)","meaning":"market, trading","meaningCN":"市场；交易"},{"word":"merx","structure":"merx, mercis (f., third declension)","meaning":"goods, merchandise","meaningCN":"货物；商品"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"structure","pos":"n./v.","zh":"结构；构造"},{"word":"structural","pos":"adj.","zh":"结构的；结构性的"},{"word":"structurally","pos":"adv.","zh":"在结构上"},{"word":"restructuring","pos":"n.","zh":"重组"},{"word":"structured","pos":"adj.","zh":"有组织的；分层的"}]}},{"word":"market competition","ipa_uk":"/ˌmɑːkɪt ˌkɒmpəˈtɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌmɑːrkɪt ˌkɑːmpəˈtɪʃn/","definition_zh":"市场竞争；市场中多个卖者或买者为争夺同一批顾客、合同与资源而相互角逐的状态；竞争政策所规范的对象","definition_en":"the state in which several sellers or buyers contend for the same customers, contracts or resources, each trying to win business away from the others","core_image":"一条街上几家卖同样货品的铺子并排开着，顾客一走近便被各家招手，铺主不断改价、换招牌、添赠品，只求把人引进自己门里","scene":"同一街区里开着几家卖同样货品的铺子，顾客一走近就被各家招手，铺主不断改价、换招牌、添赠品，只为把客人引进自己门里；傍晚一算账，谁家让价让得多，谁家门口就排得长。Market competition keeps every one of them watching the others' prices.","sceneCN":"几家同类铺子在同一条街上争夺同一批过路人，彼此盯着对方的标价不断调整。句中的 market competition 指「多个主体争夺同一批顾客的状态」（第 1 个义项：同业者为同一批买主相互角逐）。图中可辨识物件：并排的店面、手写价牌、赠品篮、排队的人。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"市场竞争（指争夺状态，通常不可数；指不同细分市场中的多场竞争时可用复数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"intense market competition","zh":"激烈的市场竞争"},{"phrase":"face market competition","zh":"面对市场竞争"},{"phrase":"fair market competition","zh":"公平的市场竞争"},{"phrase":"market competition policy","zh":"市场竞争政策"},{"phrase":"subject to market competition","zh":"受市场竞争约束"},{"phrase":"market competition and consumer choice","zh":"市场竞争与消费者选择"},{"phrase":"shielded from market competition","zh":"受保护而免受市场竞争"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数（不可数用法）","form":"market competition"},{"label":"复数（指多场竞争）","form":"market competitions"},{"label":"作定语（带连字符）","form":"market-competition"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"compete","pos":"v.","zh":"竞争；参赛"},{"word":"competitor","pos":"n.","zh":"竞争者；对手"},{"word":"competitive","pos":"adj.","zh":"有竞争力的；竞争性的"},{"word":"competitiveness","pos":"n.","zh":"竞争力"},{"word":"competitively","pos":"adv.","zh":"以竞争的方式"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Several sellers chasing the same buyers","titleCN":"多个卖者追逐同一批买主","definition":"the ordinary situation in which two or more firms offer similar goods to the same group of customers","definitionCN":"两家或更多厂商向同一群顾客提供相似货物的一般情形","example":"Market competition forces the two chains to match each other's opening hours.","exampleCN":"市场竞争迫使两家连锁店把营业时间对齐。","why":"competition goes back to a Latin verb for seeking the same thing together, and market names the arena, so the phrase says that several parties seek one prize in one place.","whyCN":"competition 上溯一个表示「共同追求同一物」的拉丁动词，market 指场所，因此这个短语是说：多方在同一场所追逐同一个目标。"},{"no":"02","title":"Rivalry conducted through price","titleCN":"以价格手段进行的争夺","definition":"contention carried on by cutting prices, offering discounts or matching a rival's rate","definitionCN":"通过降价、折扣或与对手同价来进行的争夺","example":"Market competition in the budget sector has pushed fares down for a decade.","exampleCN":"廉价市场的竞争已把票价压低了十年。","why":"price is the fastest lever a seller can pull, so the general rivalry is often narrowed to the one instrument that shows up first on a price board.","whyCN":"价格是卖者能拉动的最快的杠杆，因此笼统的角逐常被收窄为最先写在价牌上的那件工具。"},{"no":"03","title":"Rivalry through quality and brands","titleCN":"以品质、品牌与服务进行的争夺","definition":"contention carried on by improving quality, design, service or advertising rather than by cutting the price","definitionCN":"通过提升品质、设计、服务或广告而非降价来进行的争夺","example":"Where fares are fixed by law, market competition shifts to legroom and punctuality.","exampleCN":"当票价由法律规定时，市场竞争便转向腿部空间与准点率。","why":"once price is off the table, sellers must differentiate, so the word's field extends from the price tag to everything else a buyer weighs.","whyCN":"一旦价格不可动，卖者只能在别处做出区别，于是这个词的范围从价签扩展到买方所权衡的一切。"},{"no":"04","title":"The benchmark of many small rivals","titleCN":"作为基准的充分竞争状态","definition":"the idealised condition in which so many sellers exist that none can influence price, used as a measuring rod","definitionCN":"一种理想化状态：卖者多到无人能影响价格，常被用作衡量的标尺","example":"The textbook treats market competition as a benchmark against which real industries are judged.","exampleCN":"教科书把市场竞争当作评判现实产业的基准。","why":"theory needs a limiting case, so the phrase also names the pole of perfect rivalry rather than any observable market.","whyCN":"理论需要一个极值情形，因此这个短语也指「充分角逐」的那一端，而非任何可观察的市场。"},{"no":"05","title":"The object of competition law","titleCN":"竞争法所保护与规范的对象","definition":"the rivalry that authorities protect by blocking mergers, cartels and abuses of dominance","definitionCN":"主管机关通过阻止合并、卡特尔与滥用支配地位来保护的角逐","example":"The case turned on whether a rebate scheme had removed market competition in the dairy aisle.","exampleCN":"该案的争点在于返利方案是否消除了乳品货架上的市场竞争。","why":"law personifies the phrase as something that can be harmed or preserved, which is why it appears as the object of enforcement verbs.","whyCN":"法律把这个短语当作可被损害、也可被保全的对象，因此它常作执法动词的宾语。"},{"no":"06","title":"Rivalry between regions or states","titleCN":"地区或辖区之间为吸引投资而竞争","definition":"contention among jurisdictions that cut taxes or offer subsidies to attract the same firms","definitionCN":"各辖区为吸引同一批企业而减税或提供补贴的争夺","example":"Market competition between cities produced a costly race of tax breaks.","exampleCN":"城市之间的市场竞争演变成一场代价高昂的减税竞赛。","why":"the sellers in this reading are governments offering a location, so the same frame is transferred from shops to jurisdictions.","whyCN":"这种读法中的「卖者」是提供落户地的政府，于是同一框架从店铺转移到了辖区。"},{"no":"07","title":"A selection mechanism that weeds out firms","titleCN":"淘汰落后者的一种选择机制","definition":"the process by which inefficient sellers lose customers and exit while efficient ones expand","definitionCN":"低效卖者失去顾客并退出、高效卖者扩张的过程","example":"Market competition drove three of the seven mills out of business within four years.","exampleCN":"市场竞争使七家磨坊中的三家在四年内停业。","why":"rivalry does not merely set prices, it also decides who survives, so the phrase can name a sorting process rather than a state.","whyCN":"角逐不仅定出价格，也决定谁存活，因此这个短语可指名一个筛选过程，而非一种状态。"},{"no":"08","title":"Contention inside a segment or platform","titleCN":"细分市场或平台内部的争夺","definition":"rivalry confined to one product segment, or played out between platforms that host other sellers","definitionCN":"局限于某一产品细分的争夺，或在承载其他卖者的平台之间展开的争夺","example":"Market competition among delivery apps now turns on who controls the rider network.","exampleCN":"配送应用之间的市场竞争，如今取决于谁掌握骑手网络。","why":"the phrase scales down to a niche and up to a platform layer, because the contending parties can be any sellers sharing one pool of demand.","whyCN":"这个短语既可缩小到一个细分位，也可放大到一个平台层，因为相互角逐的可以是共享同一需求池的任何卖者。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Market competition pairs a Latin trade noun with a Latin noun of striving. Market goes back to mercatus 'a place of trading'; competition goes back to competere, literally 'to seek together', built from com- 'together' and petere 'to seek, to head for'.","cn":"market competition 把一个拉丁的交易名词与一个拉丁的「力争」名词配在一起。market 上溯 mercatus「交易场所」；competition 上溯 competere，字面是「共同追求」，由表示「共同」的前缀与 petere「寻求、奔向」构成。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN PETERE","en":"Petere meant 'to seek, to make for, to attack'. It is generally thought to come from a root for rushing at something, but the older form is a reconstruction, not a recorded word.","cn":"petere 意为「寻求、奔向、攻击」。一般认为它出自表示「扑向某物」的词根，但更早的形式是重构形式，而非有记录的词。"},{"era":"LATIN COMPETERE","en":"Com- 'together' plus petere produced competere, whose first sense was 'to meet, to come together, to coincide'. Only in later Latin did it take on 'to strive after the same thing, to contend'.","cn":"表示「共同」的前缀加 petere 构成 competere，其本义是「相遇、会合、恰好一致」。到较晚的拉丁语中，它才带上「争夺同一物、相争」的意思。"},{"era":"LATIN COMPETITIO","en":"The noun competitio named the act of seeking something together, and in legal and later usage it named a claim laid by several parties to one thing, hence a dispute.","cn":"名词 competitio 指「共同追求某物」的行为，在法律及后世用法中指多方对同一物提出主张，因而带上争执之意。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH AND ENGLISH","en":"Competition reached English through Old French in the sixteenth century, bringing the sense of rivalry between persons or traders rather than the older sense of coincidence.","cn":"competition 于十六世纪经古法语进入英语，带来的是人与人、商人与商人之间的角逐义，而非较早的「恰好一致」义。"},{"era":"ECONOMIC PHRASE","en":"The full phrase became standard with industrial organization and competition policy in the twentieth century, when rivalry among sellers was named, measured and regulated as a distinct object.","cn":"完整短语在二十世纪的产业组织理论与竞争政策中成为标准说法，卖者之间的角逐从此被命名、测量并作为独立对象加以规范。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain: no single citation fixes the moment when the Latin verb shifted from 'meet' to 'contend', and the pre-Latin root of petere is unsettled, so the boundary dates given here are approximations.","cn":"来源不确定：没有单一书证能确定这个拉丁动词由「相遇」转为「相争」的时刻，petere 在拉丁语之前的词根亦无定论，此处给出的分界年代只是约数。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one shares the Latin striving root but names a capacity, a person or a quality instead of the contest itself; group two names neighbouring ideas in the same contest, each with a narrower reach.","cn":"第一组共用拉丁「力争」词根，但指能力、人物或性质，而非角逐本身；第二组指同一场角逐中的邻近概念，各自范围更窄。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"market competitiveness","ipa":"/ˌmɑːkɪt kəmˈpetɪtɪvnəs/","tag":"a capacity, not a contest","definition":"The ability of a firm or country to hold its own against rivals; it is the strength brought to the contest, not the contest itself.","definitionCN":"企业或国家与对手抗衡的能力；它是带入角逐的实力，而非角逐本身。"},{"word":"competitor","ipa":"/kəmˈpetɪtə/","tag":"a person or firm","definition":"One of the parties doing the contending; it names a participant, whereas the target names the relation between participants.","definitionCN":"参与角逐的其中一方；它指参与者，而目标短语指参与者之间的关系。"},{"word":"competitive","ipa":"/kəmˈpetɪtɪv/","tag":"the adjective","definition":"The adjective describing a market or a price that can win business; the target is the noun for the process the adjective describes.","definitionCN":"描述市场或价格足以赢得生意的形容词；目标短语则是该形容词所指过程的名称。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"rivalry","ipa":"/ˈraɪvəlri/","tag":"long-running enmity","definition":"A continuing state of striving between two parties; it stresses duration and personal antagonism, which a market phrase does not.","definitionCN":"两方持续力争的状态；强调持续性与人对人的敌意，市场短语不含这两层。"},{"word":"price war","ipa":"/ˈpraɪs wɔː/","tag":"one tactic, escalated","definition":"A contest fought only by repeated price cuts; it is a single episode inside the target, not the whole relation.","definitionCN":"只靠反复降价进行的争夺；它是目标状态中的一段插曲，而非整段关系。"},{"word":"contestability","ipa":"/kənˌtestəˈbɪləti/","tag":"ease of entry","definition":"The ease with which a newcomer could enter and displace an incumbent; it measures a threat behind the contest rather than the contest.","definitionCN":"新来者进入并取代在位者的容易程度；它衡量角逐背后的威胁，而非角逐本身。"},{"word":"antitrust","ipa":"/ˌæntiˈtrʌst/","tag":"the law that guards it","definition":"The body of law that protects rivalry; it is the policy instrument aimed at the target, not the target.","definitionCN":"保护角逐的法律体系；它是指向目标状态的政策工具，而非目标状态。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the real Latin verb 'to seek together', real relatives and real phrases from competition policy.","cn":"正常联想：真实的拉丁动词「共同追求」、真实同族词，以及竞争政策中的真实说法。"},"normal":[{"en":"Competition rests on competere, com- 'together' plus petere 'to seek': two parties seeking one thing is already the whole picture.","cn":"competition 基于 competere，即表示「共同」的前缀加 petere「寻求」：两方共追一物，画面已然完整。"},{"en":"The old sense was 'to meet or coincide', which is why the same root also gives competent, a word about fitting the case.","cn":"旧义是「相遇、相合」，同一词根因此也给出 competent，一个表示「合于其事」的词。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the intensity: intense market competition, fair market competition, shielded from market competition.","cn":"固定搭配标出强度：激烈的市场竞争、公平的市场竞争、受保护而免受市场竞争。"},{"en":"Policy vocabulary travels with the phrase: competition policy, antitrust enforcement, a merger review.","cn":"政策词汇与这个短语同行：竞争政策、反垄断执法、合并审查。"},{"en":"The phrase is also a benchmark, so textbooks set it beside monopoly and oligopoly on the same scale.","cn":"这个短语同时是一个基准，因此教科书把它与垄断、寡头放在同一标尺上。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture several shopkeepers on one street all watching the same passer-by and stepping forward at the same moment.","cn":"想象一条街上几个店主盯着同一位过路人，并在同一刻一起迎上前去。"},{"en":"Picture a price board rewritten every morning by each shop, then compared with the board across the road.","cn":"想象每家铺子每天早上重写价牌，然后与对街那家的价牌相比。"},{"en":"Picture a race in which the finish line is the customer's hand reaching for one counter out of several.","cn":"想象一场赛跑，终点线是顾客的手在几个柜台之间伸向其中一个。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Intense market competition has cut the average price of a solar panel by more than half in a decade.","cn":"激烈的市场竞争使太阳能板均价在十年间下降了一半以上。"},{"en":"The regulator blocked the merger on the ground that it would remove market competition in two regional routes.","cn":"监管机构阻止该合并，理由是它将消除两条区域航线上的市场竞争。"},{"en":"Where a service is shielded from market competition, providers tend to answer to budgets rather than to users.","cn":"当某项服务免受市场竞争时，提供者往往对预算负责，而非对使用者负责。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「market（市场）+ competition（比赛）」——把集市当成一场比赛：几家铺子同抢一批客人，谁价低、谁货好，谁就得分。","word":"market competition"},"root":"拉丁 mercatus「市场、交易」← mercari「做买卖」← merx（属格 mercis）「货物」；拉丁 competere「共同追求」= 表示「共同」的前缀 + petere「寻求、扑向」，晚期拉丁转为「相争」，名词 competitio 经古法语 competition 入英语；短语为二十世纪产业组织与竞争政策术语。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses unfold from one Latin verb meaning to seek the same thing together: first many sellers chase one crowd, then they chase it by price, then by quality, then the chase is idealized into a benchmark, protected by law, transferred to cities, read as a weeding-out process and finally confined to a segment or a platform.","cn":"八个义项从一个意为「共同追求同一物」的拉丁动词展开：先是多个卖者追同一群人，继而以价格追、以品质追，随后这场追逐被理想化为基准、被法律保护、被移用到城市之间、被读成淘汰过程，最后被限定在某个细分或某个平台之内。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: several shops on one street stepping forward at the same moment toward the same customer.","cn":"核心意象：一条街上几家铺子在同一刻朝同一位顾客迎上前去。"},"chain":["SHARED DEMAND","PRICE LEVER","QUALITY LEVER","IDEAL BENCHMARK","LEGAL OBJECT","SELECTION"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THE BASE AND THE FIRST LEVER: many sellers share one pool of buyers, and the quickest way to pull them over is the price board.","cn":"基本局面与第一根杠杆：多个卖者共享一个买主池，而把人拉过来最快的办法是价牌。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"THE SECOND LEVER AND THE LIMIT: with price fixed, rivalry moves to quality, and pushed to its limit it becomes the theorist's benchmark.","cn":"第二根杠杆与极值：价格被固定时，角逐转向品质；把它推到极值，便成了理论家的基准。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"GUARDED AND RELOCATED: the law treats the contest as a thing to protect, and the same frame is then moved from shops to cities.","cn":"被守护与被移用：法律把这场角逐当作需要保护之物，同一框架随后从店铺移到了城市。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE SORTING: beyond prices, the contest decides which sellers stay and which close their doors.","cn":"筛选：除定出价格之外，角逐还决定哪些卖者留下、哪些关门。"},{"senses":"08","en":"THE NARROW ARENA: the same chase can be scaled down to one niche or up to a platform that hosts the sellers.","cn":"更窄的场地：同一场追逐可缩小到一个细分位，也可放大到承载卖者的平台。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase is a compound of two nouns, and its second half is itself a Latin verb plus a prefix and a noun suffix, so the whole can be read morpheme by morpheme.","cn":"这个短语由两个名词合成，后半部分本身又是一个拉丁动词加上前缀与名词后缀，因此整体可以按语素逐个读出。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin com- and petere build competere, competitio and the English family compete, competitor, competitive; mercatus supplies market and merchant.","cn":"拉丁语中表示「共同」的前缀与 petere 构成 competere、competitio，以及英语词族 compete、competitor、competitive；mercatus 提供 market 与 merchant。"},"items":[{"word":"com-","structure":"Latin prefix, 'together, with'","meaning":"together; jointly","meaningCN":"共同；一起","example":"The prefix marks two parties acting on one object.","exampleCN":"这个前缀标记两方作用于同一对象。"},{"word":"petere","structure":"Latin verb, third conjugation, 'to seek, head for'","meaning":"to seek, to make for, to attack","meaningCN":"寻求；奔向；攻击","example":"The verb supplies the striving at the heart of the word.","exampleCN":"这个动词提供这个词核心处的「力争」。"},{"word":"competere","structure":"com- + petere","meaning":"to seek together, then to contend","meaningCN":"共同寻求；后转为相争","example":"Competere first meant to meet, and later to strive against.","exampleCN":"competere 最初意为相遇，后来意为相争。"},{"word":"-itio","structure":"Latin suffix forming a noun of action","meaning":"the act or process of doing","meaningCN":"动作或过程","example":"Competere plus the suffix yields the noun of striving.","exampleCN":"competere 加这个后缀构成表示「力争」的名词。"},{"word":"competition","structure":"competitio through Old French","meaning":"the act of contending","meaningCN":"角逐的行为","example":"Competition entered English with the sense of rivalry.","exampleCN":"competition 带着「角逐」之义进入英语。"},{"word":"competitive","structure":"compete + -itive (tending to)","meaning":"tending to win against others","meaningCN":"有胜出倾向的；竞争性的","example":"A competitive price is one that can take business from a rival.","exampleCN":"有竞争力的价格是能从对手那里抢走生意的价格。"},{"word":"competitor","structure":"compete + -or (one who acts)","meaning":"one who contends","meaningCN":"参与角逐的人或企业","example":"Each competitor watches the others' moves.","exampleCN":"每个竞争者都盯着其他人的动作。"},{"word":"competitiveness","structure":"competitive + -ness (quality)","meaning":"the quality of being able to contend","meaningCN":"能够角逐的性质；竞争力","example":"The index ranks countries by competitiveness.","exampleCN":"该指数按竞争力给各国排名。"},{"word":"uncompetitive","structure":"un- (not) + competitive","meaning":"unable to hold its own","meaningCN":"无力与对手抗衡的","example":"An uncompetitive price loses the contract.","exampleCN":"无竞争力的价格会丢掉合同。"},{"word":"market","structure":"Latin mercatus, from merx (goods)","meaning":"a place of trade, and demand itself","meaningCN":"交易场所，也指需求本身","example":"Market supplies the arena in which the contending happens.","exampleCN":"market 提供角逐发生的场所。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"petere","structure":"petere, petivi, petitum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to seek, to head for, to attack","meaningCN":"寻求；奔向；攻击"},{"word":"competere","structure":"competere, competivi, competitum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to meet, then to contend","meaningCN":"相遇；后指相争"},{"word":"competitio","structure":"competitio, competitionis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a seeking together, a dispute","meaningCN":"共同追求；争执"},{"word":"mercatus","structure":"mercatus, mercatus (m., fourth declension)","meaning":"market, trading","meaningCN":"市场；交易"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"compete","pos":"v.","zh":"竞争；参赛"},{"word":"competitor","pos":"n.","zh":"竞争者；对手"},{"word":"competitive","pos":"adj.","zh":"有竞争力的"},{"word":"competitiveness","pos":"n.","zh":"竞争力"},{"word":"competitively","pos":"adv.","zh":"以竞争的方式"}]}}]);
